    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30206\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"20\" y=\"36\" width=\"44\" height=\"30\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1: R</text><rect x=\"68\" y=\"36\" width=\"44\" height=\"30\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">2: S</text><rect x=\"116\" y=\"36\" width=\"44\" height=\"30\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"138\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">3: F</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"36\" width=\"44\" height=\"30\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"186\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">4: R S F</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">4 equally likely kinds of race, each \u00bc</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">R rain \u00b7 S safety car \u00b7 F red flag, each in 2 of 4: \u2119 = \u00bd</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">pairs: \u2119(R\u2229S) = \u00bc = \u00bd\u00b7\u00bd \u2713</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">triple: \u2119(R\u2229S\u2229F) = \u00bc \u2260 \u215b \u2717</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">pairwise independent, not mutually</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Four equally likely races with R (rain), S (safety car), F (red flag). Every pair has \u2119 = \u00bc = \u00bd\u00b7\u00bd, but \u2119(R\u2229S\u2229F) = \u00bc \u2260 \u215b, so pairwise independence is not mutual independence.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Tetrahedron Setup:</strong> 4 faces with equal probability $1/4$: Face 1 has colors $\\{R, G\\}$, Face 2 $\\{R, B\\}$, Face 3 $\\{G, B\\}$, Face 4 $\\{R, G, B\\}$.",
      "<strong>Pairwise Independence Holds:</strong> $\\mathbb{P}(R) = \\mathbb{P}(G) = \\mathbb{P}(B) = 2/4 = 1/2$. For any pair, $\\mathbb{P}(R \\cap G) = 1/4 = \\mathbb{P}(R)\\,\\mathbb{P}(G)$.",
      "<strong>Mutual Independence Fails:</strong> $\\mathbb{P}(R \\cap G \\cap B) = 1/4$ (Face 4), whereas $\\mathbb{P}(R)\\,\\mathbb{P}(G)\\,\\mathbb{P}(B) = (1/2)^3 = 1/8 \\ne 1/4$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{P}(R \\cap G) = \\frac{1}{4} = \\mathbb{P}(R)\\mathbb{P}(G), \\quad \\text{yet} \\quad \\mathbb{P}(R \\cap G \\cap B) = \\frac{1}{4} \\ne \\mathbb{P}(R)\\mathbb{P}(G)\\mathbb{P}(B) = \\frac{1}{8}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Four kinds of race.</strong> Imagine only four equally likely races, each with a different mix of rain, safety car and red flag. Any two of the three look unrelated, but all three together happen far more often than independence would give.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming pairwise independence implies mutual independence! For n events, mutual independence requires verifying all 2^n - n - 1 non-trivial subset intersection equations.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Bernstein's example.</b> A tetrahedron has faces coloured $\\{R\\}$, $\\{G\\}$, $\\{B\\}$ and $\\{R,G,B\\}$, each face rolled with probability $\\tfrac14$. Then $\\mathbb P(R)=\\mathbb P(G)=\\mathbb P(B)=\\tfrac12$ and $\\mathbb P(R\\cap G)=\\tfrac14=\\mathbb P(R)\\mathbb P(G)$ (and likewise for the other pairs), so the events are pairwise independent. But $\\mathbb P(R\\cap G\\cap B)=\\tfrac14\\ne\\tfrac18=\\mathbb P(R)\\mathbb P(G)\\mathbb P(B)$, so they are not mutually independent (Grimmett 1.5).",
    "hint": "Can three events be independent in every pair, yet fail to be independent together?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(R)=\\tfrac12$ = each colour is on two of the four equally likely faces.</strong> Say R is rain, S a safety car, F a red flag, each present in two of four kinds of race.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(R\\cap G)=\\tfrac14=\\mathbb P(R)\\mathbb P(G)$ = every pair multiplies.</strong> Each pair of colours shares exactly one face, so every pair is independent.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(R\\cap G\\cap B)=\\tfrac14\\ne\\tfrac18$ = the triple does not multiply.</strong> Only face 4 has all three, so mutual independence needs more equations than the pairs."
    ],
