"104.0\" y2=\"76.9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"76.9\" x2=\"104.0\" y2=\"76.9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"104\" cy=\"76.9\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"108\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"72.93589734283444\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">F(x) = \u2119(X \u2264 x)</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">never decreases</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21921 as x\u2192\u221e, \u21920 as x\u2192\u2212\u221e</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X = minutes to the first safety car; F(x) = \u2119(one by minute x)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The CDF F(x) climbs from 0 to 1 as x (minutes until the first safety car) grows. The marked point shows F(x) = \u2119(X \u2264 x) read off at one x.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Measurable Mapping:</strong> A random variable $X: \\Omega \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is a measurable function satisfying $\\{\\omega : X(\\omega) \\le x\\} \\in \\mathcal{F}$ for all $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$.",
      "<strong>CDF Definition:</strong> $F_X(x) \\triangleq \\mathbb{P}(X \\le x) = \\mathbb{P}(\\{\\omega \\in \\Omega : X(\\omega) \\le x\\})$.",
      "<strong>Four Invariants:</strong> (1) Non-decreasing: $x_1 \\le x_2 \\implies F(x_1) \\le F(x_2)$; (2) Right-continuous: $\\lim_{h \\downarrow 0} F(x+h) = F(x)$; (3) $\\lim_{x \\to -\\infty} F(x) = 0$; (4) $\\lim_{x \\to \\infty} F(x) = 1$."
    ],
    "math": "$$F_X(x) = \\mathbb{P}(X \\le x), \\quad \\lim_{h \\downarrow 0} F_X(x+h) = F_X(x), \\quad F_X(-\\infty) = 0, \\quad F_X(\\infty) = 1$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The first safety car as a number per race.</strong> Each race gets the minute its first safety car comes out. The CDF then answers \u201cin what share of races is there a safety car by minute 30?\u201d for every minute at once, a curve that only goes up.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming CDFs must be continuous everywhere. Jump discontinuities F(x) - F(x\u207b) = \u2119(X = x) occur at every discrete atom; only RIGHT-continuity is universally guaranteed!",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Random variable and CDF.</b> A random variable on $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ is a function $X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ such that $\\{X\\le x\\}\\in\\mathcal F$ for all $x$. Its cumulative distribution function is $F_X(x)=\\mathbb P(X\\le x)$. Then $F_X$ is non-decreasing and right-continuous, with $F_X(-\\infty)=0$ and $F_X(\\infty)=1$, and $F_X(x)-F_X(x^-)=\\mathbb P(X=x)$ (Ross 4.1; Grimmett 2.1).",
    "hint": "How do you turn the minutes until the first safety car into one curve that answers \u201cby minute x?\u201d for every x?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ = a number read off each race.</strong> The minutes until the first safety car: each point of $\\Omega$ is sent to that number.",
      "<strong>$F_X(x)=\\mathbb P(X\\le x)$ = chance of a safety car by minute $x$.</strong> It collects all races whose first safety car comes at or before $x$.",
      "<strong>$F_X(-\\infty)=0,\\ F_X(\\infty)=1$ = it climbs from nothing to everything.</strong> It never decreases, and it is right-continuous: a jump is exactly the chance of one exact value."
    ],
