    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30303\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30303)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30303)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">t min</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f(t)</text><path d=\"M24.0,109.2 L27.4,108.3 L30.7,107.1 L34.1,105.7 L37.5,104.0 L40.8,102.0 L44.2,99.6 L47.6,96.8 L50.9,93.6 L54.3,90.1 L57.7,86.1 L61.0,81.9 L64.4,77.4 L67.8,72.7 L71.1,67.9 L74.5,63.2 L77.9,58.7 L81.2,54.4 L84.6,50.6 L88.0,47.4 L91.3,44.9 L94.7,43.1 L98.1,42.1 L101.4,42.1 L104.8,42.9 L108.2,44.5 L111.5,47.0 L114.9,50.1 L118.3,53.8 L121.6,58.0 L125.0,62.5 L128.4,67.2 L131.7,72.0 L135.1,76.7 L138.5,81.2 L141.8,85.5 L145.2,89.5 L148.6,93.1 L151.9,96.4 L155.3,99.2 L158.7,101.7 L162.0,103.7 L165.4,105.5 L168.8,106.9 L172.1,108.1 L175.5,109.1 L178.9,109.8 L182.2,110.4 L185.6,110.8 L189.0,111.1 L192.3,111.4 L195.7,111.6 L199.1,111.7 L202.4,111.8 L205.8,111.9 L209.2,111.9 L212.5,111.9 L215.9,112.0 L219.3,112.0 L222.6,112.0 L226.0,112.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><polygon points=\"40.0,102.5 43.0,100.5 46.0,98.1 49.0,95.5 52.0,92.5 55.0,89.3 58.0,85.7 61.0,81.9 64.0,77.9 67.0,73.8 70.0,69.5 73.0,65.3 76.0,61.2 79.0,57.2 82.0,53.5 85.0,50.2 88.0,47.4 91.0,45.1 94.0,43.4 97.0,42.3 100.0,42.0 103.0,42.3 106.0,43.4 109.0,45.1 112.0,47.4 115.0,50.2 118.0,53.5 121.0,57.2 124.0,61.2 127.0,65.3 130.0,69.5 130.0,112.0 40.0,112.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"69.5\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"78\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">F(x) = \u222b f(t) dt</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f(x) = F\u2032(x)</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">slope of F</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(X = c) = 0:</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">no area at a point</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">minutes to the first safety car X, shaded area = \u2119(X \u2264 x)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The density f(t) of the minute X of the first safety car. The shaded area up to x is F(x) = \u222bf(t)dt, f is the slope of F, and a single instant carries no area, so \u2119(X = c) = 0.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Absolute Continuity:</strong> $X$ is continuous if there exists non-negative integrable $f_X(x)$ such that $F_X(x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^x f_X(t)\\,dt$ for all $x$.",
      "<strong>Calculus Fundamental:</strong> $f_X(x) = \\frac{d}{dx} F_X(x)$ almost everywhere, with $\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_X(x)\\,dx = 1$.",
      "<strong>Point Mass Zero:</strong> $\\mathbb{P}(X = c) = \\int_c^c f_X(t)\\,dt = 0$ for every single $c \\in \\mathbb{R}$. Probabilities are only non-zero over intervals of positive length."
    ],
    "math": "$$F_X(x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^x f_X(t)\\,dt, \\quad f_X(x) = F_X'(x), \\quad \\mathbb{P}(X = c) = 0 \\quad \\forall c \\in \\mathbb{R}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The safety car at any instant.</strong> A safety car at exactly 27.000\u2026 minutes has chance 0; \u201cbetween minute 25 and 30\u201d has the area of the curve over that stretch. The curve is high where first safety cars usually come.",
    "examTrap": "Believing probability density f_X(x) cannot exceed 1! Densities can be arbitrarily large (e.g. Uniform(0, 0.1) has f(x) = 10). Only PROBABILITIES are bounded by 1.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Continuous random variable and PDF.</b> $X$ is continuous if $F_X(x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^xf_X(t)\\,dt$ for a function $f_X\\ge0$ with $\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_X=1$, the probability density function. Then $f_X(x)=F_X'(x)$ at continuity points of $f_X$, $\\mathbb P(a\\le X\\le b)=\\int_a^bf_X$, and $\\mathbb P(X=c)=0$ for every $c$ (Ross 5.1; Grimmett 4.1).",
    "hint": "If the first safety car can come at any instant, how do chances become areas?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_X(t)$ = density, chance per minute.</strong> A tall spot of the curve means first safety cars near minute $t$ are common. It is not a chance itself and may exceed 1.",
      "<strong>$F_X(x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^xf_X(t)\\,dt$ = area up to $x$.</strong> The shaded area under the curve to the left of $x$ is the chance the first safety car comes by minute $x$.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(X=c)=0$ = a single exact value has no area.</strong> Only stretches of minutes carry chance; and $f_X=F_X'$ recovers the curve from the CDF."
    ],
