    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "Non-Monotonic Transformations & Multi-Branch Sums",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30403\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30403)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30403)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y = g(x)</text><path d=\"M40.0,52.0 L43.2,55.8 L46.4,59.4 L49.6,62.8 L52.8,66.1 L56.0,69.3 L59.2,72.3 L62.4,75.1 L65.6,77.8 L68.8,80.3 L72.0,82.7 L75.2,84.9 L78.4,87.0 L81.6,88.9 L84.8,90.7 L88.0,92.3 L91.2,93.8 L94.4,95.1 L97.6,96.2 L100.8,97.2 L104.0,98.1 L107.2,98.8 L110.4,99.3 L113.6,99.7 L116.8,99.9 L120.0,100.0 L123.2,99.9 L126.4,99.7 L129.6,99.3 L132.8,98.8 L136.0,98.1 L139.2,97.2 L142.4,96.2 L145.6,95.1 L148.8,93.8 L152.0,92.3 L155.2,90.7 L158.4,88.9 L161.6,87.0 L164.8,84.9 L168.0,82.7 L171.2,80.3 L174.4,77.8 L177.6,75.1 L180.8,72.3 L184.0,69.3 L187.2,66.1 L190.4,62.8 L193.6,59.4 L196.8,55.8 L200.0,52.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"62.0\" x2=\"226.0\" y2=\"62.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"222\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">y</text><line x1=\"48.8\" y1=\"62.0\" x2=\"48.8\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"191.2\" y1=\"62.0\" x2=\"191.2\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"48.81947831979126\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2081 = \u2212\u221ay</text><text x=\"191.18052168020876\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2082 = +\u221ay</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">two laps give the same y</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">fY(y) = \u2211 fX(x\u2096)/|g\u2032(x\u2096)|, one term per branch</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A U-shaped g(x), such as the squared deviation from the target lap time. The level y is reached at two points x\u2081 = \u2212\u221ay and x\u2082 = +\u221ay, and f_Y(y) adds one term f_X(x\u2096)/|g\u2032(x\u2096)| for each branch.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Piecewise Monotonicity:</strong> If $g(x) = y$ has multiple discrete roots $\\{x_1, \\dots, x_k\\}$, split the domain into monotonic segments.",
      "<strong>Branch Summation:</strong> Total density sums contributions from every root: $f_Y(y) = \\sum_{k} f_X(x_k) \\left|\\frac{dx_k}{dy}\\right| = \\sum_{k} \\frac{f_X(x_k)}{|g'(x_k)|}$.",
      "<strong>Canonical Square Law:</strong> For $Y = X^2$, roots are $x = \\pm\\sqrt{y}$, yielding $f_Y(y) = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}} [f_X(\\sqrt{y}) + f_X(-\\sqrt{y})] \\mathbf{1}_{\\{y > 0\\}}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_Y(y) = \\sum_{x_k \\in g^{-1}(y)} \\frac{f_X(x_k)}{|g'(x_k)|}; \\quad Y = X^2 \\implies f_Y(y) = \\frac{f_X(\\sqrt{y}) + f_X(-\\sqrt{y})}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\mathbf{1}_{\\{y>0\\}}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Two ways to the same number.</strong> Deviation from the target lap: 0.3 s too fast or 0.3 s too slow both give a squared deviation of 0.09. The chance of that squared value counts both.",
    "examTrap": "Missing branches when g(x) is even or periodic (e.g. Y = |X|, Y = X\u2074, Y = cos X). Every real root x_k contributing to y must be included in the sum!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Many-to-one transformations.</b> Let $g$ be piecewise strictly monotone and differentiable, and let $y$ have preimages $x_1,\\ldots,x_m$ with $g'(x_k)\\ne0$. Then $f_Y(y)=\\sum_{k}\\dfrac{f_X(x_k)}{|g'(x_k)|}$. In particular for $Y=X^2$, $f_Y(y)=\\dfrac{f_X(\\sqrt y)+f_X(-\\sqrt y)}{2\\sqrt y}\\,\\mathbf 1_{\\{y\\gt 0\\}}$ (Ross 5.7; Grimmett 4.7).",
    "hint": "If two different values of X give the same Y, how do you count the chance at that Y?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$x_k\\in g^{-1}(y)$ = every input that lands on $y$.</strong> For $Y=X^2$ both $+\\sqrt y$ and $-\\sqrt y$ do; one must find every real root.",
      "<strong>$f_X(x_k)/|g'(x_k)|$ = one branch's contribution.</strong> Each branch is the one-dimensional change-of-variables term for that piece of $g$.",
      "<strong>$\\sum_k$ = add the branches.</strong> The chance at $y$ is the sum over branches; missing one gives a density that does not integrate to 1."
    ],
    "textbookImg": null,
