    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30502\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30502)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30502)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">t laps</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(X > t)</text><polygon points=\"24.0,32.0 28.4,37.7 32.8,42.9 37.2,47.8 41.6,52.3 46.0,56.6 50.4,60.5 54.8,64.1 59.2,67.5 63.6,70.7 68.0,73.6 72.4,76.3 76.8,78.8 81.2,81.2 85.6,83.3 90.0,85.4 94.4,87.3 98.8,89.0 103.2,90.6 107.6,92.1 112.0,93.5 116.4,94.8 120.8,96.1 125.2,97.2 129.6,98.2 134.0,99.2 138.4,100.1 142.8,101.0 147.2,101.7 151.6,102.5 156.0,103.1 160.4,103.8 164.8,104.3 169.2,104.9 173.6,105.4 178.0,105.9 182.4,106.3 186.8,106.7 191.2,107.1 195.6,107.4 200.0,107.7 200.0,112.0 24.0,112.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><path d=\"M24.0,32.0 L28.0,37.2 L32.1,42.1 L36.1,46.6 L40.2,50.9 L44.2,54.9 L48.2,58.6 L52.3,62.1 L56.3,65.3 L60.4,68.4 L64.4,71.2 L68.4,73.9 L72.5,76.3 L76.5,78.7 L80.6,80.8 L84.6,82.9 L88.6,84.8 L92.7,86.5 L96.7,88.2 L100.8,89.7 L104.8,91.2 L108.8,92.5 L112.9,93.8 L116.9,95.0 L121.0,96.1 L125.0,97.1 L129.0,98.1 L133.1,99.0 L137.1,99.9 L141.2,100.6 L145.2,101.4 L149.2,102.1 L153.3,102.7 L157.3,103.3 L161.4,103.9 L165.4,104.4 L169.4,104.9 L173.5,105.4 L177.5,105.8 L181.6,106.2 L185.6,106.6 L189.6,106.9 L193.7,107.3 L197.7,107.6 L201.8,107.9 L205.8,108.1 L209.8,108.4 L213.9,108.6 L217.9,108.8 L222.0,109.0 L226.0,109.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">area = \ud835\udd3c[X] = \u222b \u2119(X > t) dt</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2211 \u2119(X \u2265 k) for counts</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">average tyre life = area under \u201csame tyres after t laps\u201d</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The survival curve \u2119(X > t) of the tyre life X. The shaded area under it equals \ud835\udd3c[X] = \u222b\u2119(X > t)dt; for counts, the sum \u2211\u2119(X \u2265 k).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Continuous Tail Formula:</strong> For any non-negative random variable $X \\ge 0$, $\\mathbb{E}[X] = \\int_0^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(X > t)\\,dt$.",
      "<strong>Discrete Integer Formula:</strong> For non-negative integer-valued random variables $X \\in \\{0, 1, 2, \\dots\\}$, $\\mathbb{E}[X] = \\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(X \\ge k)$.",
      "<strong>Higher Moments Extension:</strong> $\\mathbb{E}[X^p] = \\int_0^\\infty p t^{p-1} \\mathbb{P}(X > t)\\,dt$ for any $p > 0$ and $X \\ge 0$."
    ],
    "math": "$$X \\ge 0 \\implies \\mathbb{E}[X] = \\int_0^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(X > t)\\,dt = \\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(X \\ge k) \\quad (X \\in \\mathbb{N}_0)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Counting laps on a set of tyres.</strong> Lap by lap, you ask whether Max is still on the same set. Adding up those yes-chances lap by lap gives the average tyre life.",
    "examTrap": "Applying the one-sided tail integral to random variables with negative values. For general RVs on \u211d, \ud835\udd3c[X] = \u222b\u2080^\u221e \u2119(X > t)dt - \u222b_{-\u221e}^0 \u2119(X < t)dt.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Tail-sum formula.</b> If $X\\ge0$ then $\\mathbb E[X]=\\int_0^\\infty\\mathbb P(X\\gt t)\\,dt$. If $X$ takes values in $\\{0,1,2,\\ldots\\}$ then $\\mathbb E[X]=\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty\\mathbb P(X\\ge k)$. For general $X$, $\\mathbb E[X]=\\int_0^\\infty\\mathbb P(X\\gt t)\\,dt-\\int_{-\\infty}^0\\mathbb P(X\\lt t)\\,dt$ (Ross 5.3; Grimmett 4.3).",
    "hint": "How can the average tyre life be read as an area under the curve \u201cstill on the same tyres after t laps\u201d?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(X\\gt t)$ = chance the tyres are still on after lap $t$.</strong> It starts at 1 and falls to 0 as $t$ grows.",
      "<strong>$\\int_0^\\infty\\ldots dt$ = the area under that curve.</strong> Each lap $t$ contributes the chance that the set lasts at least that long.",
      "<strong>$=\\mathbb E[X]$ = the area is the mean.</strong> Slicing the tyre life into laps instead of values gives the same average; for counts, $\\sum_{k\\ge1}\\mathbb P(X\\ge k)$."
    ],
