    "title": "Variance, Covariance & Bilinear Expansion",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30503\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"40\" y=\"22\" width=\"70\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"22\" width=\"50\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#e5e9f0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"75\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Var X</text><text x=\"135\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Cov(X,Y)</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Cov</text><text x=\"135\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Var Y</text><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"22\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"22\" width=\"120\" height=\"98\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"75\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X: pit stop</text><text x=\"135\" y=\"16\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y: traffic</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Var(X+Y)</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">= Var X + Var Y</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">+ 2 Cov(X,Y)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">variance of a total = squares plus cross terms</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Expand (X + Y)\u00b2 as a square of sides X (pit-stop time) and Y (time lost in traffic): Var X, Var Y on the diagonal and Cov(X,Y) twice off it, so Var(X+Y) = Var X + Var Y + 2Cov(X,Y).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Definitions:</strong> $\\operatorname{Var}(X) \\triangleq \\mathbb{E}[(X - \\mu)^2] = \\mathbb{E}[X^2] - (\\mathbb{E}[X])^2 \\ge 0$. Covariance: $\\operatorname{Cov}(X, Y) \\triangleq \\mathbb{E}[(X - \\mu_X)(Y - \\mu_Y)]$.",
      "<strong>Quadratic Scaling:</strong> $\\operatorname{Var}(aX + b) = a^2 \\operatorname{Var}(X)$. Additive constants shift position without altering spread.",
      "<strong>Bilinear Expansion:</strong> $\\operatorname{Var}(\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i) = \\sum_{i=1}^n \\operatorname{Var}(X_i) + 2 \\sum_{i \\lt  j} \\operatorname{Cov}(X_i, X_j)$. If pairwise uncorrelated, cross-terms vanish."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\operatorname{Var}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i\\right) = \\sum_{i=1}^n \\operatorname{Var}(X_i) + 2 \\sum_{1 \\le i \\lt  j \\le n} \\operatorname{Cov}(X_i, X_j)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A bad stop stacks up.</strong> If a slow pit stop also drops Max into traffic, the total time lost varies more than the pieces suggest; independent pieces just add variances.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming Cov(X, Y) = 0 implies independence! Zero covariance only means no LINEAR relationship. Deterministic non-linear pairs (e.g. Y = X\u00b2) can have Cov(X, Y) = 0.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Variance of a sum.</b> For $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ with finite second moments, $\\operatorname{Var}(\\sum_iX_i)=\\sum_i\\operatorname{Var}(X_i)+2\\sum_{i\\lt j}\\operatorname{Cov}(X_i,X_j)$, where $\\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)=\\mathbb E[(X-\\mathbb EX)(Y-\\mathbb EY)]$ (Ross 7.4; Grimmett 3.6).",
    "hint": "If a slow pit stop tends to drop Max into traffic, what does the variance of the total time lost look like?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\sum\\operatorname{Var}(X_i)$ = each part's own spread.</strong> The squares on the diagonal.",
      "<strong>$\\operatorname{Cov}(X_i,X_j)$ = how two parts move together.</strong> Positive if a slow stop comes with more time lost in traffic.",
      "<strong>$2\\sum_{i\\lt j}$ = each pair twice.</strong> Expanding $(\\sum X_i)^2$ gives both $X_iX_j$ and $X_jX_i$."
    ],
