    "title": "Moment Generating Functions (MGF) & Uniqueness",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30504\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30504)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30504)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">t</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">M(t)</text><path d=\"M24.0,107.4 L27.5,107.0 L31.0,106.5 L34.6,106.0 L38.1,105.4 L41.6,104.8 L45.1,104.2 L48.6,103.5 L52.2,102.7 L55.7,101.8 L59.2,100.9 L62.7,99.9 L66.2,98.7 L69.8,97.5 L73.3,96.2 L76.8,94.7 L80.3,93.2 L83.8,91.4 L87.4,89.5 L90.9,87.5 L94.4,85.2 L97.9,82.7 L101.4,80.1 L105.0,77.1 L108.5,73.9 L112.0,70.4 L115.5,66.6 L119.0,62.4 L122.6,57.8 L126.1,52.9 L129.6,47.4 L133.1,41.5 L136.6,35.0 L140.2,27.9 L143.7,20.2 L147.2,11.7 L150.7,2.5 L154.2,-7.6 L157.8,-18.6 L161.3,-30.6 L164.8,-43.7 L168.3,-58.0 L171.8,-73.7 L175.4,-90.8 L178.9,-109.4 L182.4,-129.8 L185.9,-152.0 L189.4,-176.3 L193.0,-202.8 L196.5,-231.8 L200.0,-263.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"88\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"88.0\" x2=\"90.0\" y2=\"88.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"98\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"78\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">slope at 0 = \ud835\udd3c[X]</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">curvature at 0 = \ud835\udd3c[X\u00b2]</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">M(t) = \ud835\udd3c[e^(tX)]</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">independent stints: multiply their M(t); M fixes the law</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The MGF M(t) = \ud835\udd3c[e^(tX)] passes through 1 at t = 0. Its slope there is \ud835\udd3c[X] and its curvature is \ud835\udd3c[X\u00b2]; for independent stints, M of the total is the product.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Definition:</strong> $M_X(t) \\triangleq \\mathbb{E}[e^{tX}]$. If $M_X(t) \\lt  \\infty$ on $(-h, h)$ around $t=0$, then $\\mathbb{E}[X^k] = M_X^{(k)}(0)$ for all $k \\ge 1$.",
      "<strong>Convolution Factorization:</strong> For independent random variables $X \\perp Y$, $M_{X+Y}(t) = \\mathbb{E}[e^{t(X+Y)}] = M_X(t) M_Y(t)$. Sums of RVs become products of MGFs.",
      "<strong>Uniqueness Theorem:</strong> If $M_X(t) = M_Y(t)$ in an open neighborhood around $0$, then $X$ and $Y$ have the exact same probability distribution."
    ],
    "math": "$$M_X(t) = \\mathbb{E}[e^{tX}] = \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty \\frac{t^k}{k!} \\mathbb{E}[X^k], \\quad X \\perp Y \\implies M_{X+Y}(t) = M_X(t) M_Y(t)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>One curve for the whole lap.</strong> Instead of remembering the average, the spread and every higher feature of Max's lap time, the engineers keep one curve that holds them all, and for two independent stints they multiply their curves.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming the MGF always exists! Heavy-tailed distributions (Cauchy, Pareto, Log-Normal) have M_X(t) = \u221e for all t > 0. In such cases, use the Characteristic Function \u03c6_X(t) = \ud835\udd3c[e^{itX}].",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Moment generating function.</b> The MGF of $X$ is $M_X(t)=\\mathbb E[e^{tX}]$ for $t$ in an interval around $0$ where it is finite. Then $M_X(t)=\\sum_{k\\ge0}\\frac{t^k}{k!}\\mathbb E[X^k]$, $M_X^{(k)}(0)=\\mathbb E[X^k]$, and if $M_X$ is finite near $0$ it determines the law of $X$. For independent $X,Y$: $M_{X+Y}(t)=M_X(t)M_Y(t)$ (Ross 7.7; Grimmett 5.1).",
    "hint": "How can one function of t store every moment of a lap time and turn a sum of independent stints into a product?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[e^{tX}]$ = the average exponential tilt of a lap time.</strong> Weight each lap time by $e^{tx}$ and average: slow laps count more as $t$ grows.",
      "<strong>$\\sum\\frac{t^k}{k!}\\mathbb E[X^k]$ = the moments are the Taylor coefficients.</strong> The slope at $t=0$ is the mean $\\mathbb E[X]$ and the curvature gives $\\mathbb E[X^2]$.",
      "<strong>$M_{X+Y}=M_XM_Y$ = sums become products.</strong> For independent stints, the MGF of the total is the product of the MGFs; it needs to exist near 0 for uniqueness."
    ],
