    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30506\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30506)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30506)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X: s off target lap</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Y = X\u00b2</text><path d=\"M54.0,31.0 L56.6,37.4 L59.3,43.4 L61.9,49.3 L64.6,54.8 L67.2,60.2 L69.8,65.2 L72.5,70.0 L75.1,74.5 L77.8,78.8 L80.4,82.8 L83.0,86.6 L85.7,90.1 L88.3,93.3 L91.0,96.3 L93.6,99.0 L96.2,101.5 L98.9,103.7 L101.5,105.6 L104.2,107.3 L106.8,108.8 L109.4,109.9 L112.1,110.8 L114.7,111.5 L117.4,111.9 L120.0,112.0 L122.6,111.9 L125.3,111.5 L127.9,110.8 L130.6,109.9 L133.2,108.8 L135.8,107.3 L138.5,105.6 L141.1,103.7 L143.8,101.5 L146.4,99.0 L149.0,96.3 L151.7,93.3 L154.3,90.1 L157.0,86.6 L159.6,82.8 L162.2,78.8 L164.9,74.5 L167.5,70.0 L170.2,65.2 L172.8,60.2 L175.4,54.8 L178.1,49.3 L180.7,43.4 L183.4,37.4 L186.0,31.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><circle cx=\"54\" cy=\"31\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"76\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"98\" cy=\"103\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"112\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"103\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"164\" cy=\"76\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"186\" cy=\"31\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">best straight line: flat</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Cov(X, X\u00b2) = \ud835\udd3c[X\u00b3] \u2212 \ud835\udd3c[X]\ud835\udd3c[X\u00b2] = 0</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(X=0, Y=1) = 0 \u2260 \u2119(X=0)\u2119(Y=1): dependent</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Points (X, Y = X\u00b2), X = seconds off the target lap, lie on a parabola, yet the best straight line through them is flat, so Cov(X, X\u00b2) = 0 although Y is fixed by X.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Symmetric Setup:</strong> Let $X \\in \\{-1, 0, 1\\}$ with equal probability $1/3$ each. Let $Y = X^2$.",
      "<strong>Covariance Evaluation:</strong> By symmetry, $\\mathbb{E}[X] = 0$ and $\\mathbb{E}[XY] = \\mathbb{E}[X^3] = \\frac{(-1)^3 + 0^3 + 1^3}{3} = 0$. Thus $\\operatorname{Cov}(X, Y) = 0 - 0 = 0$.",
      "<strong>Complete Dependence:</strong> $\\mathbb{P}(X=0, Y=1) = 0 \\ne \\mathbb{P}(X=0)\\mathbb{P}(Y=1) = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{2}{9}$. Knowing $X$ determines $Y$ with 100% certainty!"
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{E}[X] = 0, \\quad \\mathbb{E}[X^3] = 0 \\implies \\operatorname{Cov}(X, X^2) = 0; \\quad \\mathbb{P}(X=0, X^2=1) = 0 \\ne \\tfrac{2}{9}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Too fast or too slow, both are off.</strong> Take the seconds a lap is off the target time, and the size of the miss. Too fast is as likely as too slow, so the two numbers show no straight-line link, though the size is set exactly by the deviation.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming uncorrelated variables are independent! Covariance measures ONLY linear association; quadratic, circular, or higher-order dependencies have Cov = 0.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Uncorrelated but dependent.</b> Let $X$ be symmetric about $0$ with finite third moment (say uniform on $\\{-1,0,1\\}$) and $Y=X^2$. Then $\\mathbb E[X]=\\mathbb E[X^3]=0$, so $\\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)=\\mathbb E[X^3]-\\mathbb E[X]\\mathbb E[X^2]=0$, yet $Y$ is a function of $X$. For $X$ uniform on $\\{-1,0,1\\}$: $\\mathbb P(X=0,Y=1)=0\\ne\\tfrac13\\cdot\\tfrac23=\\mathbb P(X=0)\\mathbb P(Y=1)$, so $X,Y$ are not independent (Ross 7.4; Grimmett 3.6).",
    "hint": "Can Y be completely determined by X and yet have zero covariance with it?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[X]=0,\\ \\mathbb E[X^3]=0$ = the odd moments vanish.</strong> If laps too fast and too slow balance, every odd power averages out to 0.",
      "<strong>$\\operatorname{Cov}(X,X^2)=\\mathbb E[X^3]-\\mathbb E[X]\\mathbb E[X^2]=0$ = no straight-line link.</strong> Covariance only sees how closely the points follow a line; the parabola has a flat best line.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(X=0,X^2=1)=0\\ne\\tfrac13\\cdot\\tfrac23$ = still dependent.</strong> Knowing $X=0$ tells you $Y=0$ for certain, so independence fails."
    ],
