    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30602\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30602)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30602)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><path d=\"M24.0,112.0 L27.4,111.9 L30.7,111.9 L34.1,111.8 L37.5,111.7 L40.8,111.6 L44.2,111.3 L47.6,111.0 L50.9,110.5 L54.3,109.8 L57.7,108.9 L61.0,107.6 L64.4,105.9 L67.8,103.8 L71.1,101.1 L74.5,97.7 L77.9,93.8 L81.2,89.1 L84.6,83.8 L88.0,78.0 L91.3,71.7 L94.7,65.1 L98.1,58.4 L101.4,52.0 L104.8,46.0 L108.2,40.8 L111.5,36.6 L114.9,33.7 L118.3,32.2 L121.6,32.2 L125.0,33.6 L128.4,36.5 L131.7,40.7 L135.1,45.8 L138.5,51.8 L141.8,58.2 L145.2,64.9 L148.6,71.5 L151.9,77.8 L155.3,83.7 L158.7,89.0 L162.0,93.6 L165.4,97.6 L168.8,101.0 L172.1,103.7 L175.5,105.9 L178.9,107.5 L182.2,108.8 L185.6,109.8 L189.0,110.5 L192.3,111.0 L195.7,111.3 L199.1,111.6 L202.4,111.7 L205.8,111.8 L209.2,111.9 L212.5,111.9 L215.9,112.0 L219.3,112.0 L222.6,112.0 L226.0,112.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><polygon points=\"24.0,112.0 27.5,111.9 31.0,111.9 34.5,111.8 38.0,111.7 41.5,111.5 45.0,111.3 48.5,110.9 52.0,110.3 55.5,109.5 59.0,108.4 62.5,106.9 66.0,105.0 66.0,112.0 24.0,112.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><polygon points=\"174.0,105.0 178.3,107.3 182.7,109.0 187.0,110.1 191.3,110.8 195.7,111.3 200.0,111.6 204.3,111.8 208.7,111.9 213.0,111.9 217.3,112.0 221.7,112.0 226.0,112.0 226.0,112.0 174.0,112.0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\"/><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"120.0\" y2=\"30.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc</text><line x1=\"66.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"66.0\" y2=\"90.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"174.0\" y1=\"112.0\" x2=\"174.0\" y2=\"90.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc \u2212 \u03b5</text><text x=\"174\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc + \u03b5</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(|X \u2212 \u03bc| \u2265 \u03b5) \u2264 Var(X)/\u03b5\u00b2</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">tail</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">tail</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">big spread \u03c3\u00b2 lets more of the laps reach the tails</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A lap-time distribution with centre \u03bc. The two tails beyond \u03bc \u00b1 \u03b5 are the laps with |X \u2212 \u03bc| \u2265 \u03b5, and their total chance is at most Var(X)/\u03b5\u00b2.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Formal Statement:</strong> For any random variable with mean $\\mu$ and finite variance $\\sigma^2$, $\\mathbb{P}(|X - \\mu| \\ge \\epsilon) \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{Var}(X)}{\\epsilon^2}$.",
      "<strong>Canonical Form ($k\\sigma$):</strong> Setting $\\epsilon = k\\sigma$, $\\mathbb{P}(|X - \\mu| \\ge k\\sigma) \\le \\frac{1}{k^2}$.",
      "<strong>Distribution-Free Guarantee:</strong> Holds for ANY distribution: at least $75\\%$ of mass lies within $2\\sigma$ ($k=2$), and at least $88.89\\%$ lies within $3\\sigma$ ($k=3$), regardless of skewness."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{P}(|X - \\mu| \\ge \\epsilon) \\le \\frac{\\operatorname{Var}(X)}{\\epsilon^2}, \\qquad \\mathbb{P}(|X - \\mu| \\ge k\\sigma) \\le \\frac{1}{k^2}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>How far from a typical lap.</strong> With an average of 92.0 s and a spread of 0.3 s, a lap more than 0.9 s off (three spreads) happens on at most a ninth of laps, whatever the shape.",
    "examTrap": "Using Chebyshev when a 1-sided bound is required. For 1-sided deviations \u2119(X - \u03bc \u2265 \u03b5), Cantelli's inequality gives the strictly sharper bound \u03c3\u00b2 / (\u03c3\u00b2 + \u03b5\u00b2).",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Chebyshev's inequality.</b> If $X$ has finite mean $\\mu$ and variance $\\sigma^2$, then for every $\\varepsilon\\gt 0$, $\\mathbb P(|X-\\mu|\\ge\\varepsilon)\\le\\dfrac{\\operatorname{Var}(X)}{\\varepsilon^2}$. Equivalently $\\mathbb P(|X-\\mu|\\ge k\\sigma)\\le1/k^2$. It is Markov's inequality applied to $(X-\\mu)^2$ (Ross 8.2; Grimmett 7.3).",
    "hint": "Knowing the average and the spread of Max's lap time, how likely is a lap far from the average?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$|X-\\mu|\\ge\\varepsilon$ = the lap is far from usual.</strong> More than $\\varepsilon$ seconds off the average, faster or slower: the two shaded tails.",
      "<strong>$\\operatorname{Var}(X)$ = the spread.</strong> A bigger variance means more laps reach the tails, so the bound is larger.",
      "<strong>$1/\\varepsilon^2$ = farther is rarer.</strong> Doubling the distance cuts the bound by four: it is Markov on $(X-\\mu)^2$, with no shape assumed.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(X-\\mu\\ge a)\\le\\dfrac{\\sigma^2}{\\sigma^2+a^2}$ = one side only (Cantelli).</strong> For laps slower than average by at least $a$, shift by any $u\\ge0$: $\\mathbb P(X-\\mu\\ge a)\\le\\mathbb P\\big((X-\\mu+u)^2\\ge(a+u)^2\\big)\\le\\frac{\\sigma^2+u^2}{(a+u)^2}$, and $u=\\sigma^2/a$ gives the bound. Halving Chebyshev is not valid."
    ],
