    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30603\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30603)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30603)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">t</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">e^(\u2212ta) M(t)</text><path d=\"M40.0,53.2 L42.7,55.1 L45.3,56.9 L48.0,58.7 L50.7,60.4 L53.3,62.0 L56.0,63.6 L58.7,65.1 L61.3,66.5 L64.0,67.9 L66.7,69.2 L69.3,70.4 L72.0,71.6 L74.7,72.8 L77.3,73.8 L80.0,74.8 L82.7,75.7 L85.3,76.6 L88.0,77.4 L90.7,78.1 L93.3,78.8 L96.0,79.4 L98.7,80.0 L101.3,80.4 L104.0,80.8 L106.7,81.2 L109.3,81.5 L112.0,81.7 L114.7,81.9 L117.3,82.0 L120.0,82.0 L122.7,82.0 L125.3,81.9 L128.0,81.7 L130.7,81.5 L133.3,81.2 L136.0,80.8 L138.7,80.4 L141.3,80.0 L144.0,79.4 L146.7,78.8 L149.3,78.1 L152.0,77.4 L154.7,76.6 L157.3,75.7 L160.0,74.8 L162.7,73.8 L165.3,72.8 L168.0,71.6 L170.7,70.4 L173.3,69.2 L176.0,67.9 L178.7,66.5 L181.3,65.1 L184.0,63.6 L186.7,62.0 L189.3,60.4 L192.0,58.7 L194.7,56.9 L197.3,55.1 L200.0,53.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"82\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"82.0\" x2=\"120.0\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">t*</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">inf over t > 0</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">every t > 0 gives a valid bound:</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">keep the smallest</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(X \u2265 a) \u2264 inf e^(\u2212ta) M(t) = e^(\u2212\u039b*(a))</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The bound e^(\u2212ta)M(t) as a function of t is a bowl. Each t > 0 is a valid ceiling on \u2119(X \u2265 a), and the Chernoff bound is the minimum at t*.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Exponential Markov Step:</strong> For any $t > 0$, $\\mathbb{P}(X \\ge a) = \\mathbb{P}(e^{tX} \\ge e^{ta}) \\le \\frac{\\mathbb{E}[e^{tX}]}{e^{ta}} = e^{-ta} M_X(t)$.",
      "<strong>Convex Dual Optimization:</strong> Squeezing over all $t > 0$ yields the sharpest bound: $\\mathbb{P}(X \\ge a) \\le \\inf_{t > 0} \\exp(-(ta - \\log M_X(t)))$.",
      "<strong>Legendre-Fenchel Conjugate:</strong> Exponent $-I(a) \\triangleq -\\sup_{t > 0}(ta - \\Lambda_X(t))$ is the convex conjugate of the cumulant MGF, giving exponential decay $O(e^{-n I(a)})$ for sample sums."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{P}(X \\ge a) \\le \\inf_{t > 0} e^{-ta} M_X(t) = \\exp\\left(-\\sup_{t > 0}[ta - \\Lambda_X(t)]\\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Tuning the ceiling.</strong> The engineers try different ways of weighing slow stops in the average, each giving a valid ceiling on \u201ca stop this slow\u201d. The smallest ceiling over all weights is the one they keep, and it often shrinks exponentially.",
    "examTrap": "Forgetting the constraint t > 0 for upper tails (and t < 0 for lower tails \u2119(X \u2264 a)). Plugging negative t into an upper-tail bound flips the inequality direction!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Chernoff bound.</b> If $M_X(t)=\\mathbb E[e^{tX}]$ is finite for some $t\\gt 0$, then for every $a$, $\\mathbb P(X\\ge a)\\le\\inf_{t\\gt 0}e^{-ta}M_X(t)=\\exp\\bigl(-\\sup_{t\\gt 0}[ta-\\Lambda_X(t)]\\bigr)$, where $\\Lambda_X=\\ln M_X$. For the lower tail, use $t\\lt 0$ (Ross 8.3; Grimmett 5.11).",
    "hint": "How do you squeeze the best possible bound on a very slow pit stop out of Markov's inequality?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$e^{-ta}M_X(t)$ = Markov applied to $e^{tX}$.</strong> The event $X\\ge a$ is the same as $e^{tX}\\ge e^{ta}$ for $t\\gt 0$, so Markov gives this bound for each $t$.",
      "<strong>$\\inf_{t\\gt 0}$ = keep the best $t$.</strong> Every $t\\gt 0$ gives a valid bound; the smallest one is the tightest, at the bottom of the bowl.",
      "<strong>$\\exp(-\\sup[ta-\\Lambda_X(t)])$ = the exponential rate.</strong> The tail falls exponentially, at a rate set by the log-MGF; $t\\gt 0$ is needed for an upper tail."
    ],
