    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30604\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30604)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30604)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">g(x) convex</text><path d=\"M40.0,75.7 L43.3,77.6 L46.6,79.5 L49.9,81.3 L53.2,83.0 L56.5,84.7 L59.8,86.2 L63.1,87.7 L66.4,89.1 L69.7,90.4 L73.0,91.6 L76.3,92.7 L79.6,93.8 L82.9,94.8 L86.2,95.7 L89.5,96.5 L92.8,97.2 L96.1,97.8 L99.4,98.4 L102.7,98.9 L106.0,99.3 L109.3,99.6 L112.6,99.8 L115.9,99.9 L119.2,100.0 L122.5,100.0 L125.8,99.9 L129.1,99.7 L132.4,99.4 L135.7,99.1 L139.0,98.6 L142.3,98.1 L145.6,97.5 L148.9,96.8 L152.2,96.1 L155.5,95.2 L158.8,94.3 L162.1,93.3 L165.4,92.2 L168.7,91.0 L172.0,89.7 L175.3,88.4 L178.6,87.0 L181.9,85.4 L185.2,83.8 L188.5,82.2 L191.8,80.4 L195.1,78.6 L198.4,76.6 L201.7,74.6 L205.0,72.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"86.32\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"86.32\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"86.32\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"86.32\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"86.32\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"82.32\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[g(X)]</text><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"126\" y=\"109.0\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">g(\ud835\udd3c[X])</text><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"100.0\" x2=\"120.0\" y2=\"118.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[X]</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">convex: the chord lies above the curve</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A convex curve g and two lap times with the chord between them. The point \ud835\udd3c[g(X)] on the chord lies above g(\ud835\udd3c[X]) on the curve.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Convexity Definition:</strong> Function $g$ is convex if $g(\\lambda x + (1-\\lambda)y) \\le \\lambda g(x) + (1-\\lambda)g(y)$ for all $\\lambda \\in [0, 1]$.",
      "<strong>Jensen\u2019s Statement:</strong> If $g$ is convex and expectations exist, $g(\\mathbb{E}[X]) \\le \\mathbb{E}[g(X)]$.",
      "<strong>Supporting Hyperplane Proof:</strong> At $\\mu = \\mathbb{E}[X]$, a tangent subgradient $c$ satisfies $g(x) \\ge g(\\mu) + c(x - \\mu)$. Taking expectations: $\\mathbb{E}[g(X)] \\ge g(\\mu) + c(0) = g(\\mathbb{E}[X])$."
    ],
    "math": "$$g \\text{ convex} \\implies g(\\mathbb{E}[X]) \\le \\mathbb{E}[g(X)]; \\qquad g \\text{ concave} \\implies \\mathbb{E}[g(X)] \\le g(\\mathbb{E}[X])$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Averages do not pass through curves.</strong> The average of the squared seconds off the pace is bigger than the square of the average seconds off, because the very bad laps are weighted extra by the squaring.",
    "examTrap": "Reversing the inequality for concave functions! For concave functions like log(x) or \u221ax, \ud835\udd3c[g(X)] \u2264 g(\ud835\udd3c[X]) (which directly proves the Arithmetic-Geometric Mean AM-GM inequality).",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Jensen's inequality.</b> If $g$ is convex and $X$ and $g(X)$ are integrable, then $g(\\mathbb E[X])\\le\\mathbb E[g(X)]$. If $g$ is concave, $\\mathbb E[g(X)]\\le g(\\mathbb E[X])$. Equality holds for non-degenerate $X$ only if $g$ is affine on the support of $X$. For $g=\\ln$ this gives the AM\u2013GM inequality (Ross 8.5; Grimmett 6.6).",
    "hint": "Is the average of a convex function of the lap time bigger or smaller than the function of the average lap?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$g(\\mathbb E[X])$ = apply $g$ after averaging.</strong> The point on the curve above the average lap time.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[g(X)]$ = average after applying $g$.</strong> This is a point on the chord between the values: for a convex curve the chord lies above the curve.",
      "<strong>$\\le$ = convex curves lie below their chords.</strong> Spread pushes the average of $g(X)$ up; for a concave $g$ like $\\ln$ the direction flips."
    ],
