    "title": "Cauchy-Schwarz & Hoeffding\u2019s Concentration Inequality",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30605\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"80.0\" x2=\"110.0\" y2=\"80.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30605)\"/><line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"80.0\" x2=\"90.0\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30605)\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">X</text><text x=\"88\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">Y</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03b8</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">|\ud835\udd3c[XY]| \u2264 \u221a(\ud835\udd3cX\u00b2 \ud835\udd3cY\u00b2)</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">= cos \u03b8 \u2264 1</text><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30605)\"/><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30605)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">t</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(sum \u2265 t)</text><path d=\"M140.0,26.0 L142.9,35.9 L145.7,44.4 L148.6,51.9 L151.5,58.3 L154.3,63.9 L157.2,68.7 L160.1,72.9 L162.9,76.5 L165.8,79.6 L168.7,82.4 L171.5,84.7 L174.4,86.7 L177.3,88.5 L180.1,90.1 L183.0,91.4 L185.9,92.5 L188.7,93.5 L191.6,94.4 L194.5,95.1 L197.3,95.8 L200.2,96.4 L203.1,96.8 L205.9,97.3 L208.8,97.6 L211.7,97.9 L214.5,98.2 L217.4,98.5 L220.3,98.7 L223.1,98.8 L226.0,99.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">exp(\u22122t\u00b2/\u2211(b\u1d62\u2212a\u1d62)\u00b2)</text><text x=\"117.7\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">angle bound for products; exponential bound for sums of bounded losses</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Left: random variables X and Y as arrows at angle \u03b8, so |\ud835\udd3c[XY]| is at most the product of their lengths. Right: Hoeffding's exponential bound on \u2119(sum \u2212 mean \u2265 t).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Cauchy-Schwarz:</strong> $|\\mathbb{E}[XY]|^2 \\le \\mathbb{E}[X^2]\\,\\mathbb{E}[Y^2]$. Equality holds if and only if $Y = c X$ almost surely for some constant $c$. Guarantees correlation $|\\rho_{X,Y}| \\le 1$.",
      "<strong>Hoeffding's Lemma:</strong> If $X \\in [a, b]$ with $\\mathbb{E}[X] = 0$, its MGF satisfies sub-Gaussian proxy $M_X(t) \\le \\exp\\left(\\frac{t^2(b - a)^2}{8}\\right)$.",
      "<strong>Hoeffding\u2019s Inequality:</strong> For independent $X_i \\in [a_i, b_i]$, $\\mathbb{P}(\\sum_{i=1}^n (X_i - \\mu_i) \\ge t) \\le \\exp\\left(-\\frac{2t^2}{\\sum_{i=1}^n (b_i - a_i)^2}\\right)$."
    ],
    "math": "$$|\\mathbb{E}[XY]|^2 \\le \\mathbb{E}[X^2]\\mathbb{E}[Y^2], \\quad \\mathbb{P}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n (X_i - \\mu_i) \\ge t\\right) \\le \\exp\\left(-\\frac{2t^2}{\\sum_{i=1}^n (b_i - a_i)^2}\\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Many small, bounded losses.</strong> If each lap in traffic costs Max between 0 and 0.2 seconds and the laps are independent, the total loss rarely ends far above its average: the chance falls off exponentially with the excess.",
    "examTrap": "Applying Hoeffding to dependent variables! Mutual independence of X\u2081,...,X_n is strictly mandatory to factorize the joint MGF in Hoeffding's proof.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Cauchy\u2013Schwarz and Hoeffding.</b> For $X,Y$ with finite second moments, $|\\mathbb E[XY]|^2\\le\\mathbb E[X^2]\\,\\mathbb E[Y^2]$. If $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ are independent with $a_i\\le X_i\\le b_i$, then for $t\\gt 0$, $\\mathbb P\\!\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n(X_i-\\mathbb EX_i)\\ge t\\right)\\le\\exp\\!\\left(-\\dfrac{2t^2}{\\sum_i(b_i-a_i)^2}\\right)$ (Ross 8.5; Grimmett 7.3, 12.2).",
    "hint": "How do you bound the average of a product, and the chance that a sum of bounded losses strays far above its mean?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$|\\mathbb E[XY]|^2\\le\\mathbb E[X^2]\\mathbb E[Y^2]$ = the inner product is at most the product of lengths.</strong> Random variables act as vectors, and the cosine of the angle between them is at most 1.",
      "<strong>$b_i-a_i$ = the range of loss $i$.</strong> Each lap's time lost in traffic is confined to an interval of that width.",
      "<strong>$\\exp(-2t^2/\\sum(b_i-a_i)^2)$ = an exponential bound for the sum.</strong> Independent bounded losses can only add up to a large excess with exponentially small chance."
    ],
