    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30703\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30703)\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"12\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30703)\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"9\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y</text><ellipse cx=\"84\" cy=\"52\" rx=\"42\" ry=\"24\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(-20 84 52)\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"20\" width=\"14\" height=\"62\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"77\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">slab at x</text><line x1=\"77.0\" y1=\"86.0\" x2=\"77.0\" y2=\"100.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30703)\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"124\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M30.0,123.7 L32.8,123.6 L35.5,123.4 L38.2,123.1 L41.0,122.7 L43.8,122.2 L46.5,121.6 L49.2,120.8 L52.0,119.8 L54.8,118.7 L57.5,117.4 L60.2,116.0 L63.0,114.4 L65.8,112.8 L68.5,111.2 L71.2,109.7 L74.0,108.4 L76.8,107.3 L79.5,106.5 L82.2,106.1 L85.0,106.0 L87.8,106.4 L90.5,107.1 L93.2,108.1 L96.0,109.3 L98.8,110.8 L101.5,112.4 L104.2,114.0 L107.0,115.5 L109.8,117.0 L112.5,118.4 L115.2,119.5 L118.0,120.5 L120.8,121.4 L123.5,122.1 L126.2,122.6 L129.0,123.0 L131.8,123.3 L134.5,123.5 L137.2,123.7 L140.0,123.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">fX(x) = \u222b f(x, y) dy</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">add up each slab:</text><text x=\"145.0\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">the y direction collapses</text><text x=\"137.72\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">discrete: pX(x) = \u2211 p(x, y)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The joint blob of (pit stop x, traffic y). For each x the slab at x is added up over y, which collapses the y direction into the marginal curve fX(x) = \u222bf(x,y)dy.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Continuous Marginalization:</strong> $f_X(x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_{X,Y}(x, y)\\,dy$ and $f_Y(y) = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_{X,Y}(x, y)\\,dx$.",
      "<strong>Discrete Marginalization:</strong> $p_X(x) = \\sum_{y} p_{X,Y}(x, y)$ and $p_Y(y) = \\sum_{x} p_{X,Y}(x, y)$ (row and column sums).",
      "<strong>Correlation Erasure:</strong> Marginals retain only single-variable laws, discarding all mutual dependence structure. Infinite distinct joints share the same marginals."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_X(x) = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_{X,Y}(x, y)\\,dy, \\qquad p_X(x) = \\sum_{y} p_{X,Y}(x, y)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Forget the traffic.</strong> Of all races with a stop of exactly $x$ seconds, whatever happened in traffic, add up their chance. Doing this for every $x$ gives the curve of stop times alone, as if the traffic had never been timed.",
    "examTrap": "Neglecting dependent boundary limits during integration! If the support is triangular 0 \u2264 y \u2264 x \u2264 1, then f_X(x) = \u222b\u2080^x f(x, y)dy, NOT \u222b\u2080\u00b9!",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Marginal distributions.</b> If $(X,Y)$ has joint density $f_{X,Y}$, then $X$ has density $f_X(x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,dy$, and likewise $f_Y(y)=\\int f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,dx$; in the discrete case $p_X(x)=\\sum_yp_{X,Y}(x,y)$. If the support depends on $x$, the limits of the inner integral are those of the section at $x$ (Ross 6.1; Grimmett 3.6, 4.5).",
    "hint": "If you only care about the pit-stop time, how do you remove the traffic from the joint picture?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_{X,Y}(x,y)$ = the joint hill.</strong> The chance density of the pair (stop $x$, traffic $y$).",
      "<strong>$\\int f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,dy$ = add up the whole slab at $x$.</strong> Fix the stop time $x$ and sum over every possible traffic loss; the traffic direction collapses.",
      "<strong>$f_X(x)$ = the stop time's own density.</strong> For a triangular support the limits of $y$ depend on $x$; integrating over the whole line would be wrong."
    ],
