    "title": "Joint Density of All n Order Statistics & The n! Permutation",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30803\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30803)\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"16\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30803)\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2081</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2082</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"18\" width=\"90\" height=\"90\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"30,108 120,108 120,18\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"30,108 30,18 120,18\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"88\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2081 &lt; x\u2082</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2082 &lt; x\u2081</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">n! orderings fold</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">onto one ordered cone,</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">so multiply by n!:</text><text x=\"137.72\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f = n! \u220f f(x\u1d62), x\u2081 &lt; \u2026 &lt; x\u2099</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">without n! the ordered cone only holds 1/n! of the chance</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "For n = 2: the unit square splits into the cone x\u2081 < x\u2082 and its mirror image. Folding the mirror onto the cone gives the sorted density 2! f(x\u2081)f(x\u2082), that is n! \u220ff(x\u1d62).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Joint Density Formula:</strong> $f_{X_{(1)}, \\dots, X_{(n)}}(x_1, \\dots, x_n) = n! \\prod_{i=1}^n f(x_i) \\cdot \\mathbf{1}_{\\{x_1 \\lt  x_2 \\lt  \\dots \\lt  x_n\\}}$.",
      "<strong>Origin of $n!$:</strong> There are $n!$ distinct permutations of the original unordered vector $(X_1, \\dots, X_n)$ that sort into the identical ordered list $(x_1, \\dots, x_n)$.",
      "<strong>Induced Dependence:</strong> Even though raw samples $X_i$ are independent, order statistics $X_{(1)}, \\dots, X_{(n)}$ are STRONGLY DEPENDENT through the ordering constraints $X_{(1)} \\lt  \\dots \\lt  X_{(n)}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_{X_{(1)},\\dots,X_{(n)}}(x_1, \\dots, x_n) = n! \\prod_{i=1}^n f(x_i) \\cdot \\mathbf{1}_{\\{x_1 \\lt  x_2 \\lt  \\dots \\lt  x_n\\}}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Sorting the timing screen.</strong> Many car-by-car assignments of times lead to the same sorted timing screen; collecting them multiplies the chance by $n!$.",
    "examTrap": "Omitting the factor n! in joint calculations. Without n!, integrating over the ordered domain x\u2081 < ... < x_n yields 1/n! instead of the required probability 1.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Joint density of order statistics.</b> For i.i.d. $X_i$ with density $f$, $(X_{(1)},\\ldots,X_{(n)})$ has density $n!\\prod_{i=1}^nf(x_i)\\mathbf 1_{\\{x_1\\lt \\cdots\\lt x_n\\}}$ (Ross 6.6; Grimmett 4.14).",
    "hint": "If you sort n lap times, why is the joint density of the sorted list n! times the product of the densities?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\prod f(x_i)$ = one particular unsorted list.</strong> Independent cars' times multiply.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbf 1_{\\{x_1\\lt \\cdots\\lt x_n\\}}$ = only sorted lists.</strong> The timing screen shows times in order: the sorted vector lives on one cone, and other orderings fold onto it.",
      "<strong>$n!$ = every ordering gives the same sorted list.</strong> Without it the density integrates to $1/n!$."
    ],
