    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30902\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30902)\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30902)\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">u</text><text x=\"22\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">v</text><rect x=\"36\" y=\"62\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">du dv</text><line x1=\"108.0\" y1=\"68.0\" x2=\"134.0\" y2=\"68.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30902)\"/><text x=\"121\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"6\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x(u,v), y(u,v)</text><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30902)\"/><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30902)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y</text><polygon points=\"164,86 192,82 202,56 176,60\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"186\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">dx dy</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a small box in (u,v) becomes a tilted box in (x,y)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">fU,V(u,v) = fX,Y(x(u,v), y(u,v)) \u00b7 |det \u2202(x,y)/\u2202(u,v)|</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the determinant is the area-stretch factor</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A small box du dv in (u,v) maps to a tilted box dx dy in (x,y). The area ratio is |det \u2202(x,y)/\u2202(u,v)|, the factor that converts the density f(x,y) into f(u,v).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Bijective Smooth Mapping:</strong> Let $(U, V) = g(X, Y)$ be an invertible, continuously differentiable mapping from $S \\subset \\mathbb{R}^2$ to $T \\subset \\mathbb{R}^2$.",
      "<strong>Jacobian Determinant:</strong> $J(u, v) \\triangleq \\det \\begin{bmatrix} \\partial x/\\partial u & \\partial x/\\partial v \\\\ \\partial y/\\partial u & \\partial y/\\partial v \\end{bmatrix}$. Reciprocal identity: $J(u, v) = [J(x, y)]^{-1}$.",
      "<strong>Transformed Density:</strong> $f_{U,V}(u, v) = f_{X,Y}(x(u, v), y(u, v)) |J(u, v)| \\cdot \\mathbf{1}_{\\{(u, v) \\in T\\}}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_{U,V}(u, v) = f_{X,Y}\\left(x(u, v), y(u, v)\\right) \\left| \\det \\frac{\\partial(x, y)}{\\partial(u, v)} \\right|$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Two ways to describe the time lost.</strong> You can describe a race by (pit stop, traffic) or by (total time lost, share lost in the pits). A small box of the second description covers a stretched, tilted box of the first, and the determinant says by how much.",
    "examTrap": "Inverting forward vs inverse Jacobian! If you calculate the forward derivative matrix \u2202(u,v)/\u2202(x,y), you must DIVIDE by its determinant rather than multiply.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Change of variables in two dimensions.</b> Let $(X,Y)$ have density $f_{X,Y}$ and let $(U,V)=(u(X,Y),v(X,Y))$ be a differentiable one-to-one map with inverse $x(u,v),y(u,v)$ and non-vanishing Jacobian. Then $f_{U,V}(u,v)=f_{X,Y}\\bigl(x(u,v),y(u,v)\\bigr)\\left|\\det\\dfrac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|$ (Ross 6.7; Grimmett 4.7).",
    "hint": "If you swap (pit stop, traffic) for new coordinates such as (total time lost, share lost in the pits), how does the density change?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f_{X,Y}(x(u,v),y(u,v))$ = the old density at the matching point.</strong> Find which $(x,y)$ maps to the new coordinates $(u,v)$, and read the old density there.",
      "<strong>$\\partial(x,y)/\\partial(u,v)$ = how the box is stretched.</strong> It records how a small box in $(u,v)$ becomes a tilted box in $(x,y)$.",
      "<strong>$|\\det|$ = the area-stretch factor.</strong> The determinant is the area of the tilted box per unit area of the small box; the absolute value keeps densities positive."
    ],
