    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30903\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30903)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"16\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30903)\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">y</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"112\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">slope z = y/x</text><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"54\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(x, y)</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"94\" y2=\"54\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">r</text><path d=\"M 46,108 A 22,22 0 0 0 44,92\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03b8</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">ratio: Z = Y/X</text><text x=\"148.64\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f(z) = \u222b |x| f(x, xz) dx</text><text x=\"130.7\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">polar: area element r dr d\u03b8</text><text x=\"130.44\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f(r, \u03b8) = r f(r cos\u03b8, r sin\u03b8)</text><text x=\"116.00999999999999\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a line through the origin keeps the ratio fixed; r is the extra stretch</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A point (x, y) = (pit stop, traffic) with ray slope z = y/x, radius r and angle \u03b8. The ratio density adds f along the ray with weight |x|, and the polar density carries the extra factor r.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Ratio Formula:</strong> For $Z = Y / X$, introduce auxiliary $W = X$. Inverse is $x = w, y = wz$ with Jacobian $|J| = |w|$, yielding $f_Z(z) = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty |x| f_{X,Y}(x, xz)\\,dx$.",
      "<strong>Polar Coordinates:</strong> $(X, Y) = (R \\cos\\Theta, R \\sin\\Theta)$. The Jacobian determinant is $\\det \\begin{bmatrix} \\cos\\theta & -r\\sin\\theta \\\\ \\sin\\theta & r\\cos\\theta \\end{bmatrix} = r$.",
      "<strong>Polar Density:</strong> $f_{R,\\Theta}(r, \\theta) = r f_{X,Y}(r \\cos\\theta, r \\sin\\theta)$ for $r \\ge 0, \\theta \\in [0, 2\\pi)$."
    ],
    "math": "$$Z = \\frac{Y}{X} \\implies f_Z(z) = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty |x|\\,f_{X,Y}(x, xz)\\,dx, \\qquad f_{R,\\Theta}(r, \\theta) = r\\,f_{X,Y}(r\\cos\\theta, r\\sin\\theta)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The mix of the time lost versus its size.</strong> The ratio of traffic loss to pit-stop time only depends on the direction of the point in the (pit stop, traffic) plane, not on how far from the origin it is. Direction and distance are the polar coordinates.",
    "examTrap": "Forgetting the absolute value factor |x| in the ratio formula! Neglecting |x| violates physical dimensions (density must have units 1/z) and gives wrong integrals.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Ratios and polar coordinates.</b> If $(X,Y)$ has density $f_{X,Y}$, then $Z=Y/X$ has density $f_Z(z)=\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty|x|\\,f_{X,Y}(x,xz)\\,dx$. In polar coordinates $X=R\\cos\\Theta$, $Y=R\\sin\\Theta$, the density of $(R,\\Theta)$ is $f_{R,\\Theta}(r,\\theta)=r\\,f_{X,Y}(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)$ for $r\\gt 0$ (Ross 6.7; Grimmett 4.7).",
    "hint": "How does a ratio of two random times, say traffic over pit stop, or a switch to polar coordinates, change the density of the pair?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$Z=Y/X$ = the slope of the ray to the point.</strong> Each value $z$ picks a line through the origin; the density of $Z$ adds up the joint density along that whole line.",
      "<strong>$|x|$ = the line is stretched.</strong> Moving along the ray at larger $x$ spreads neighbouring slopes farther apart, so the weight grows like $|x|$.",
      "<strong>$r\\,f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)$ = polar area element.</strong> A small piece of area is $r\\,dr\\,d\\theta$: circles at larger radius have more room."
    ],
