    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30904\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30904)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"16\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30904)\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">Z\u2081</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Z\u2082</text><circle cx=\"77.0\" cy=\"62.0\" r=\"36.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><line x1=\"77\" y1=\"62\" x2=\"106\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"40\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(Z\u2081, Z\u2082)</text><line x1=\"106\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"106\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><line x1=\"77\" y1=\"62\" x2=\"106\" y2=\"62\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"86\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">R</text><path d=\"M 91,62 A 14,14 0 0 0 89,53\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"98\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">2\u03c0U\u2082</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">R = \u221a(\u22122 ln U\u2081)</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">angle = 2\u03c0U\u2082</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Z\u2081 = R cos(2\u03c0U\u2082)</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Z\u2082 = R sin(2\u03c0U\u2082)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">two uniform random numbers give two independent normals</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Two uniform numbers give a radius R = \u221a(\u22122 ln U\u2081) and an angle 2\u03c0U\u2082. The point at that radius and angle has coordinates (Z\u2081, Z\u2082) = (R cos, R sin), two independent standard normals.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Motivation:</strong> Gaussian quantile function $\\Phi^{-1}(u)$ has no closed form. Box-Muller bypasses 1D intractability by operating in 2D polar coordinates.",
      "<strong>Construction:</strong> For $U_1, U_2 \\stackrel{\\text{i.i.d.}}{\\sim} \\text{Uniform}(0, 1)$, set radius $R = \\sqrt{-2\\ln U_1}$ (so $R^2 \\sim \\text{Exp}(1/2) \\equiv \\chi_2^2$) and angle $\\Theta = 2\\pi U_2 \\sim \\text{Uniform}(0, 2\\pi)$.",
      "<strong>Exact Normals:</strong> $Z_1 = R \\cos\\Theta$ and $Z_2 = R \\sin\\Theta$ are EXACTLY independent standard normal random variables: $Z_1, Z_2 \\stackrel{\\text{i.i.d.}}{\\sim} \\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$."
    ],
    "math": "$$Z_1 = \\sqrt{-2\\ln U_1}\\cos(2\\pi U_2), \\quad Z_2 = \\sqrt{-2\\ln U_1}\\sin(2\\pi U_2) \\implies Z_1, Z_2 \\stackrel{\\text{i.i.d.}}{\\sim} \\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Simulating lap-time noise.</strong> Red Bull's race simulator needs the usual wobble around Max's 92.0 s lap. It draws two ordinary random numbers, treats one as a random distance and one as a random direction, and reads off two perfect bell-curve values: the noise for two laps.",
    "examTrap": "Generating standard normals one at a time and discarding Z\u2082! Box-Muller generates TWO independent normal values per pair of uniforms; saving both doubles computational efficiency.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Box\u2013Muller transform.</b> If $U_1,U_2$ are independent $\\text{Uniform}(0,1)$, then $Z_1=\\sqrt{-2\\ln U_1}\\cos(2\\pi U_2)$ and $Z_2=\\sqrt{-2\\ln U_1}\\sin(2\\pi U_2)$ are independent $\\mathcal N(0,1)$. Proof: $R^2=-2\\ln U_1\\sim\\mathrm{Exp}(1/2)$ and $\\Theta=2\\pi U_2\\sim\\text{Uniform}(0,2\\pi)$ are independent, and the Jacobian of the polar map gives the joint density $\\frac1{2\\pi}e^{-(z_1^2+z_2^2)/2}$ (Ross 6.7; Grimmett 4.11).",
    "hint": "How can two uniform random numbers produce two independent normal variables exactly?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$R=\\sqrt{-2\\ln U_1}$ = a random radius.</strong> The squared radius is exponential with rate $1/2$, which is the radial law of the two-dimensional standard normal.",
      "<strong>$\\Theta=2\\pi U_2$ = a uniform angle.</strong> The standard normal pair has no preferred direction, so the angle is uniform on the circle.",
      "<strong>$(R\\cos\\Theta,R\\sin\\Theta)$ = read off the point.</strong> The polar Jacobian $r$ turns this into the density $\\frac1{2\\pi}e^{-(z_1^2+z_2^2)/2}$: two independent standard normals."
    ],
