    "title": "Sum Invariants: Stability of Normal, Poisson & Gamma",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30905\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30905)\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"18\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30905)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">seconds lost</text><path d=\"M24.0,98.8 L25.9,98.1 L27.8,97.1 L29.7,95.7 L31.6,93.7 L33.5,91.3 L35.4,88.3 L37.3,84.8 L39.2,81.0 L41.1,77.1 L43.0,73.4 L44.9,70.1 L46.8,67.7 L48.7,66.3 L50.6,66.1 L52.5,67.0 L54.4,69.1 L56.3,72.1 L58.2,75.7 L60.1,79.6 L62.0,83.5 L63.9,87.1 L65.8,90.2 L67.7,92.9 L69.6,95.0 L71.5,96.6 L73.4,97.8 L75.3,98.6 L77.2,99.2 L79.1,99.5 L81.0,99.7 L82.9,99.8 L84.8,99.9 L86.7,100.0 L88.6,100.0 L90.5,100.0 L92.4,100.0 L94.3,100.0 L96.2,100.0 L98.1,100.0 L100.0,100.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">pit stop</text><path d=\"M40.0,100.0 L42.8,100.0 L45.5,100.0 L48.2,99.9 L51.0,99.8 L53.8,99.7 L56.5,99.4 L59.2,98.9 L62.0,98.0 L64.8,96.7 L67.5,94.8 L70.2,92.3 L73.0,89.0 L75.8,85.2 L78.5,81.0 L81.2,77.0 L84.0,73.5 L86.8,71.1 L89.5,70.0 L92.2,70.5 L95.0,72.5 L97.8,75.6 L100.5,79.5 L103.2,83.7 L106.0,87.7 L108.8,91.1 L111.5,94.0 L114.2,96.1 L117.0,97.6 L119.8,98.6 L122.5,99.2 L125.2,99.6 L128.0,99.8 L130.8,99.9 L133.5,100.0 L136.2,100.0 L139.0,100.0 L141.8,100.0 L144.5,100.0 L147.2,100.0 L150.0,100.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"92\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">traffic</text><path d=\"M60.0,100.0 L63.3,100.0 L66.6,100.0 L70.0,100.0 L73.3,100.0 L76.6,100.0 L79.9,99.9 L83.2,99.9 L86.6,99.9 L89.9,99.8 L93.2,99.7 L96.5,99.6 L99.8,99.4 L103.2,99.2 L106.5,98.9 L109.8,98.5 L113.1,98.0 L116.4,97.4 L119.8,96.6 L123.1,95.7 L126.4,94.6 L129.7,93.4 L133.0,92.0 L136.4,90.5 L139.7,88.9 L143.0,87.2 L146.3,85.5 L149.6,83.8 L153.0,82.3 L156.3,80.9 L159.6,79.7 L162.9,78.8 L166.2,78.2 L169.6,78.0 L172.9,78.1 L176.2,78.6 L179.5,79.4 L182.8,80.5 L186.2,81.9 L189.5,83.4 L192.8,85.0 L196.1,86.7 L199.4,88.4 L202.8,90.1 L206.1,91.6 L209.4,93.0 L212.7,94.3 L216.0,95.4 L219.4,96.4 L222.7,97.2 L226.0,97.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">total: wider</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udca9(\u03bc\u2081,\u03c3\u2081\u00b2) + \ud835\udca9(\u03bc\u2082,\u03c3\u2082\u00b2) = \ud835\udca9(\u03bc\u2081+\u03bc\u2082, \u03c3\u2081\u00b2+\u03c3\u2082\u00b2)</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Pois(\u03bb\u2081) + Pois(\u03bb\u2082) = Pois(\u03bb\u2081+\u03bb\u2082)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">means add, variances add, and the family stays the same</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Bell curves for the pit-stop time and the traffic loss, and the wider bell of their total at the summed centre: \ud835\udca9(\u03bc\u2081,\u03c3\u2081\u00b2) + \ud835\udca9(\u03bc\u2082,\u03c3\u2082\u00b2) = \ud835\udca9(\u03bc\u2081+\u03bc\u2082, \u03c3\u2081\u00b2+\u03c3\u2082\u00b2). Poisson counts, like safety cars over two races, add the same way.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Gaussian Closure:</strong> If $X_i \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_i, \\sigma_i^2)$ are independent, $\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\sum \\mu_i, \\sum \\sigma_i^2)$.",
      "<strong>Poisson Closure:</strong> If $X_i \\sim \\text{Poisson}(\\lambda_i)$ are independent, $\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i \\sim \\text{Poisson}(\\sum \\lambda_i)$.",
      "<strong>Gamma Closure (Shared Rate):</strong> If $X_i \\sim \\text{Gamma}(\\alpha_i, \\beta)$ are independent with IDENTICAL scale $\\beta$, then $\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i \\sim \\text{Gamma}(\\sum \\alpha_i, \\beta)$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\sum_{i=1}^n \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_i, \\sigma_i^2) = \\mathcal{N}\\left(\\sum \\mu_i, \\sum \\sigma_i^2\\right), \\quad \\sum_{i=1}^n \\text{Pois}(\\lambda_i) = \\text{Pois}\\left(\\sum \\lambda_i\\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Adding up the race.</strong> A normal pit-stop time plus a normal traffic loss is a normal total time lost, with the means and the variances added. Safety cars in Saudi Arabia and in Australia add up to a Poisson count for the two races. The family never changes, only its parameters.",
    "examTrap": "Adding Gamma random variables with different scale parameters \u03b2\u2081 \u2260 \u03b2\u2082! The sum of Gammas is Gamma ONLY when the rate/scale parameter is identical across all terms.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Closure under independent sums.</b> If $X_i\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mu_i,\\sigma_i^2)$ are independent, then $\\sum_iX_i\\sim\\mathcal N\\bigl(\\sum\\mu_i,\\sum\\sigma_i^2\\bigr)$. If $X_i\\sim\\mathrm{Pois}(\\lambda_i)$ are independent, then $\\sum_iX_i\\sim\\mathrm{Pois}\\bigl(\\sum\\lambda_i\\bigr)$. If $X_i\\sim\\mathrm{Gamma}(\\alpha_i,\\beta)$ are independent (same rate), then $\\sum_iX_i\\sim\\mathrm{Gamma}\\bigl(\\sum\\alpha_i,\\beta\\bigr)$ (Ross 7.7; Grimmett 4.8, 5.1).",
    "hint": "Which families stay in the same family when you add independent members, and what happens to the parameters?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\sum\\mu_i,\\ \\sum\\sigma_i^2$ = means add and variances add.</strong> The total of independent normal parts is normal, centred at the total mean, with the variances added (not the spreads).",
      "<strong>$\\mathrm{Pois}(\\sum\\lambda_i)$ = counts add, rates add.</strong> Independent Poisson counts, such as the safety cars in two races, add to a Poisson count with the total rate.",
      "<strong>Why:</strong> products of MGFs, $M_{X+Y}=M_XM_Y$, have the same form as each one, so the family is closed under adding independent members.",
      "<strong>$Z_1^2+\\cdots+Z_n^2\\sim\\chi^2_n=\\mathrm{Gamma}(\\tfrac n2,\\tfrac12)$ = squared normals add up.</strong> Each $Z_i^2$ is $\\chi^2_1=\\mathrm{Gamma}(\\frac12,\\frac12)$ (4.05), so $n$ independent ones add to $\\mathrm{Gamma}(\\frac n2,\\frac12)$, with mean $n$ and variance $2n$."
    ],
