    "title": "Worked Benchmark: Sum of Two Uniforms (The Triangle Law)",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-30906\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30906)\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-30906)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">z</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f(z)</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">each delay flat on [0, 1] s</text><polygon points=\"60,104 120,34 180,104\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">peak at 1</text><line x1=\"60.0\" y1=\"102.0\" x2=\"60.0\" y2=\"106.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><line x1=\"120.0\" y1=\"102.0\" x2=\"120.0\" y2=\"106.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><line x1=\"180.0\" y1=\"102.0\" x2=\"180.0\" y2=\"106.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">2</text><text x=\"66\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">f = z</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">f = 2 \u2212 z</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[Z] = 1,  Var(Z) = \u2159</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">two flat delays add to a tent</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Two flat densities on [0,1] s convolve into the tent f(z): rising as z on [0,1], falling as 2 \u2212 z on [1,2], with peak at z = 1, mean 1 and variance 1/6.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Problem Setup:</strong> Let $X, Y \\stackrel{\\text{i.i.d.}}{\\sim} \\text{Uniform}(0, 1)$. Compute the PDF of $Z = X + Y$.",
      "<strong>Convolution Integral:</strong> $f_Z(z) = \\int_0^1 \\mathbf{1}_{\\{0 \\le z - x \\le 1\\}}\\,dx = \\int_{\\max(0, z-1)}^{\\min(1, z)} 1\\,dx$.",
      "<strong>Piecewise Triangle:</strong> For $0 \\le z \\le 1$, $f_Z(z) = z$. For $1 \\lt  z \\le 2$, $f_Z(z) = 2 - z$. Mean is $\\mathbb{E}[Z] = 1$, variance $\\operatorname{Var}(Z) = 1/12 + 1/12 = 1/6$."
    ],
    "math": "$$f_{X+Y}(z) = \\begin{cases} z & 0 \\le z \\le 1 \\\\ 2 - z & 1 \\lt  z \\le 2 \\\\ 0 & \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}, \\qquad \\mathbb{E}[Z] = 1, \\; \\operatorname{Var}(Z) = \\tfrac{1}{6}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Two flat delays.</strong> A sticky wheel nut and a slow front jack each cost Max anywhere from 0 to 1 second, all equally likely. A total near 1 second is most likely, because there are the most ways to make it; totals near 0 or 2 seconds are rare.",
    "examTrap": "Treating the convolution integral as a single algebraic formula over [0, 2]! The overlap geometry changes at z = 1, splitting the solution into two distinct linear regimes.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Sum of two uniforms.</b> If $X,Y$ are independent $\\text{Uniform}(0,1)$, then $f_{X+Y}(z)=z$ on $[0,1]$, $2-z$ on $(1,2]$, and $0$ otherwise (the triangular law); $\\mathbb E[X+Y]=1$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X+Y)=\\frac16$ (Ross 6.3; Grimmett 4.8).",
    "hint": "Two independent flat delays at the pit stop add. What shape does the total take, and why does it peak in the middle?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$f(z)=z$ on $[0,1]$ = the overlap grows.</strong> At small totals the flat densities overlap on a stretch of length $z$.",
      "<strong>$f(z)=2-z$ on $(1,2]$ = the overlap shrinks.</strong> Past the peak at $z=1$ it falls linearly: a tent.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E=1,\\ \\operatorname{Var}=\\frac16$ = means and variances add.</strong> Each delay has mean $\\frac12$ and variance $\\frac1{12}$."
    ],
