    "cardNumber": "01",
    "category": "EXCHANGEABILITY",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "Exchangeability: Permutation Invariance of Joint Law",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31001\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"120\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">races of one season, in any order</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"24\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">race 1</text><rect x=\"84\" y=\"24\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">race 2</text><rect x=\"128\" y=\"24\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"146\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">race 3</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"100\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">race 3</text><rect x=\"84\" y=\"100\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">race 1</text><rect x=\"128\" y=\"100\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"146\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">race 2</text><line x1=\"58.0\" y1=\"46.0\" x2=\"58.0\" y2=\"98.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31001)\"/><line x1=\"102.0\" y1=\"46.0\" x2=\"146.0\" y2=\"98.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31001)\"/><text x=\"189.2\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(X\u2081, X\u2082, X\u2083)</text><text x=\"166.84\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">has the same law as</text><text x=\"189.2\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">(X\u2083, X\u2081, X\u2082)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">same joint law for every reshuffling \u03c0: i.i.d. \u2282 exchangeable</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Max's results (X\u2081, X\u2082, X\u2083) and the same results in another order (X\u2083, X\u2081, X\u2082). Exchangeable races have the same joint law under every reshuffling.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Formal Definition:</strong> $(X_1, \\dots, X_n)$ is exchangeable if $(X_1, \\dots, X_n) \\stackrel{d}{=} (X_{\\pi(1)}, \\dots, X_{\\pi(n)})$ for every permutation $\\pi \\in S_n$.",
      "<strong>Hierarchy:</strong> $\\text{i.i.d.} \\subsetneq \\text{Exchangeable} \\subsetneq \\text{Identically Distributed}$. Exchangeability is strictly weaker than i.i.d. because mutual dependence is permitted.",
      "<strong>Equi-marginality:</strong> All $X_i$ share identical marginal distributions $F$, and all pairs $(X_i, X_j)$ share identical joint bivariate laws."
    ],
    "math": "$$(X_1, \\dots, X_n) \\stackrel{d}{=} (X_{\\pi(1)}, \\dots, X_{\\pi(n)}) \\quad \\forall \\pi \\in S_n; \\qquad \\text{i.i.d.} \\subset \\text{Exchangeable}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Races with no calendar.</strong> Take a stretch of similar high-speed circuits. If you hid the race names, you could not tell which was which, and every ordering of the same results would look equally plausible. The races can still be linked, for example through the same Red Bull car.",
    "examTrap": "Confusing exchangeable with i.i.d.! Exchangeable variables can be strongly correlated (e.g. sampling without replacement from a finite urn).",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Exchangeability.</b> Random variables $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ are exchangeable if $(X_1,\\ldots,X_n)\\overset d=(X_{\\pi(1)},\\ldots,X_{\\pi(n)})$ for every permutation $\\pi$ of $\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$. An infinite sequence is exchangeable if every finite subsequence is. Every i.i.d. sequence is exchangeable, but not conversely (Grimmett 7.2; Durrett 4.1).",
    "hint": "If the order of Max's races carries no information, what does that say about their joint law?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$(X_1,\\ldots,X_n)$ = Max's results in races $1$ to $n$.</strong> Say his gap to P2 in each race: one list, one joint law for the whole stretch.",
      "<strong>$(X_{\\pi(1)},\\ldots,X_{\\pi(n)})$ = the same races reshuffled.</strong> Relabel the races by any permutation $\\pi$, for instance by swapping Monza and Spa.",
      "<strong>$\\overset d=$ = nothing changes in law.</strong> No race is special: the joint chances are the same for every reshuffling. Independent identical races satisfy it, but linked races can too."
    ],
