    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "Finite Exchangeability Correlation Bound: \u03c1 \u2265 -1/(n - 1)",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31003\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31003)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">n races</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c1 = 0</text><path d=\"M24.0,110.0 L27.2,96.0 L30.5,86.7 L33.8,80.0 L37.0,75.0 L40.2,71.1 L43.5,68.0 L46.8,65.5 L50.0,63.3 L53.2,61.5 L56.5,60.0 L59.8,58.7 L63.0,57.5 L66.2,56.5 L69.5,55.6 L72.8,54.7 L76.0,54.0 L79.2,53.3 L82.5,52.7 L85.8,52.2 L89.0,51.7 L92.2,51.2 L95.5,50.8 L98.8,50.4 L102.0,50.0 L105.2,49.7 L108.5,49.3 L111.8,49.0 L115.0,48.8 L118.2,48.5 L121.5,48.2 L124.8,48.0 L128.0,47.8 L131.2,47.6 L134.5,47.4 L137.8,47.2 L141.0,47.0 L144.2,46.8 L147.5,46.7 L150.8,46.5 L154.0,46.4 L157.2,46.2 L160.5,46.1 L163.8,46.0 L167.0,45.8 L170.2,45.7 L173.5,45.6 L176.8,45.5 L180.0,45.4 L183.2,45.3 L186.5,45.2 L189.8,45.1 L193.0,45.0 L196.2,44.9 L199.5,44.8 L202.8,44.7 L206.0,44.7 L209.2,44.6 L212.5,44.5 L215.8,44.4 L219.0,44.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\"></text><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"110.0\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"29\" y=\"108.0\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">n = 2: \u22121</text><circle cx=\"37\" cy=\"75.0\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"73.0\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">n = 3: \u2212\u00bd</text><text x=\"134.6\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">allowed: \u03c1 above the curve</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c1 \u2265 \u22121/(n \u2212 1)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0 \u2264 Var(\u2211X\u1d62) = n\u03c3\u00b2 [1 + (n \u2212 1)\u03c1] \u21d2 1 + (n \u2212 1)\u03c1 \u2265 0</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The smallest allowed correlation \u22121/(n\u22121) as the number of races n grows. For n = 2 it is \u22121, for n = 3 it is \u2212\u00bd, and it climbs towards 0 as races are added.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Sum Variance Expansion:</strong> For sum $S_n = \\sum_{i=1}^n X_i$, $\\operatorname{Var}(S_n) = \\sum \\operatorname{Var}(X_i) + \\sum_{i \\ne j} \\operatorname{Cov}(X_i, X_j) = n\\sigma^2 + n(n-1)\\rho\\sigma^2$.",
      "<strong>Positivity Constraint:</strong> Since $\\operatorname{Var}(S_n) \\ge 0$, we have $n\\sigma^2 [1 + (n-1)\\rho] \\ge 0 \\implies \\rho \\ge -\\frac{1}{n-1}$.",
      "<strong>Extreme Negative Attainment:</strong> Equality $\\rho = -\\frac{1}{n-1}$ is achieved when the sum is deterministic: $\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i = c$ almost surely."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\operatorname{Var}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i\\right) \\ge 0 \\implies 1 + (n-1)\\rho \\ge 0 \\implies \\rho \\ge -\\frac{1}{n-1}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Not every race can make up for every other.</strong> A bad Monza can be balanced by a great Spa. But with five equal races, each race cannot offset all four others strongly: the average negative link is at best \u2212\u00bc.",
    "examTrap": "Believing correlation can never be negative in exchangeable systems. For finite n, negative correlation is completely valid down to the barrier -1/(n-1).",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Correlation bound for finite exchangeable sequences.</b> If $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ are exchangeable with common variance $\\sigma^2\\gt 0$ and pairwise correlation $\\rho$, then $\\rho\\ge-\\dfrac1{n-1}$. Proof: $0\\le\\operatorname{Var}\\bigl(\\sum_iX_i\\bigr)=n\\sigma^2+n(n-1)\\rho\\sigma^2=n\\sigma^2\\bigl[1+(n-1)\\rho\\bigr]$ (Grimmett 7.2).",
    "hint": "How negatively can n exchangeable races be linked, if their total must have a non-negative variance?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\operatorname{Var}(\\sum X_i)\\ge0$ = a variance is never negative.</strong> The total over all races can vary, or not at all, but not less than that.",
      "<strong>$n\\sigma^2[1+(n-1)\\rho]$ = the variance of the total.</strong> There are $n$ variances $\\sigma^2$ and $n(n-1)$ ordered pairs, each adding $\\rho\\sigma^2$.",
      "<strong>$\\rho\\ge-1/(n-1)$ = races cannot be too negatively linked.</strong> With 2 races they may be perfectly opposed; with more races, less so: they cannot all be below average at the same time."
    ],
