    "cardNumber": "04",
    "category": "INFINITE EXCHANGEABILITY",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-purple",
    "title": "Infinite Exchangeability & Non-Negative Correlation",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31004\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31004)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">n races</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c1 = 0</text><path d=\"M24.0,110.0 L27.2,96.0 L30.5,86.7 L33.8,80.0 L37.0,75.0 L40.2,71.1 L43.5,68.0 L46.8,65.5 L50.0,63.3 L53.2,61.5 L56.5,60.0 L59.8,58.7 L63.0,57.5 L66.2,56.5 L69.5,55.6 L72.8,54.7 L76.0,54.0 L79.2,53.3 L82.5,52.7 L85.8,52.2 L89.0,51.7 L92.2,51.2 L95.5,50.8 L98.8,50.4 L102.0,50.0 L105.2,49.7 L108.5,49.3 L111.8,49.0 L115.0,48.8 L118.2,48.5 L121.5,48.2 L124.8,48.0 L128.0,47.8 L131.2,47.6 L134.5,47.4 L137.8,47.2 L141.0,47.0 L144.2,46.8 L147.5,46.7 L150.8,46.5 L154.0,46.4 L157.2,46.2 L160.5,46.1 L163.8,46.0 L167.0,45.8 L170.2,45.7 L173.5,45.6 L176.8,45.5 L180.0,45.4 L183.2,45.3 L186.5,45.2 L189.8,45.1 L193.0,45.0 L196.2,44.9 L199.5,44.8 L202.8,44.7 L206.0,44.7 L209.2,44.6 L212.5,44.5 L215.8,44.4 L219.0,44.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\"></text><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"110.0\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"29\" y=\"108.0\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">n = 2: \u22121</text><circle cx=\"37\" cy=\"75.0\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"42\" y=\"73.0\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">n = 3: \u2212\u00bd</text><text x=\"126.8\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">the bound holds for every n,</text><text x=\"148.64\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">and tends to 0: so \u03c1 \u2265 0</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">endless season: no race can systematically offset the others</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The bound \u22121/(n\u22121) must hold for every n. As n grows it approaches 0, so a common correlation \u03c1 of an infinite exchangeable sequence satisfies \u03c1 \u2265 0.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Infinite Extension:</strong> Sequence $(X_1, X_2, \\dots)$ is infinitely exchangeable if every finite subvector $(X_1, \\dots, X_n)$ is exchangeable for all $n \\ge 2$.",
      "<strong>Vanishing Lower Bound:</strong> The bound $\\rho \\ge -\\frac{1}{n-1}$ must hold for arbitrarily large $n$. Taking $n \\to \\infty$ yields $\\rho \\ge 0$.",
      "<strong>Impossibility of Negative Correlation:</strong> You cannot have an infinite family of variables that are all mutually negatively correlated! Mutual conflict cannot scale to infinity."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\rho \\ge -\\frac{1}{n-1} \\quad \\forall n \\ge 2 \\implies \\rho \\ge \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\left(-\\frac{1}{n-1}\\right) = 0 \\implies \\rho \\ge 0$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A never-ending season.</strong> If the season never ends, you can always ask about more and more races at once, and then no race can systematically make up for the others. The link between races is at least zero.",
    "examTrap": "Applying De Finetti or claiming \u03c1 \u2265 0 for a finite sequence! Sampling without replacement from an urn of N balls stops at N; its correlation -1/(N-1) CANNOT be extended to infinity.",
    "stmtKind": "COROLLARY",
    "statement": "<b>Infinite exchangeability forces non-negative correlation.</b> If $X_1,X_2,\\ldots$ is an infinite exchangeable sequence with finite variance, then every pair has $\\rho\\ge0$. Proof: each finite segment $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ is exchangeable, so $\\rho\\ge-\\frac1{n-1}$ for all $n\\ge2$, and letting $n\\to\\infty$ gives $\\rho\\ge0$ (Grimmett 7.2).",
    "hint": "If the season could go on forever, what is the most negative the link between two races can be?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\rho\\ge-\\tfrac1{n-1}\\ \\forall n$ = the bound holds for every length.</strong> Any $n$ races of an infinite exchangeable sequence are themselves exchangeable.",
      "<strong>$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\bigl(-\\tfrac1{n-1}\\bigr)=0$ = the bound tends to 0.</strong> A fixed $\\rho$ must be at least as large as every term of a sequence whose limit is 0.",
      "<strong>$\\rho\\ge0$ = no negative links.</strong> Races in an infinite exchangeable sequence are never negatively correlated; mixing a hidden common factor creates only positive links."
    ],
