    "id": 31006,
    "subject": "StoMA",
    "topicId": "10_Exchangeable_Random_Variables",
    "topicTitle": "10 \u00b7 Exchangeable Random Variables",
    "cardNumber": "06",
    "category": "WORKED BENCHMARK",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "Worked Benchmark: P\u00f3lya\u2019s Urn Scheme & Exchangeability",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31006\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"32.0\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"46\" cy=\"46\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"62\" cy=\"40\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"60\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"66\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"76\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"74\" cy=\"48\" r=\"3.2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"62.24\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">urn: Max (white), others (black)</text><line x1=\"100.0\" y1=\"56.0\" x2=\"140.0\" y2=\"56.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31006)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">draw one</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a vote for Max:</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">put it back plus</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">c more for Max</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">votes snowball</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(sequence) depends</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">only on counts</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u0398 ~ Beta(w/c, b/c) = long-run share for Max</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">exchangeable but not independent</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "An urn of votes for Max (white) and for the others (black). After each draw the ball is put back with c more of its kind, so the chance of a sequence depends only on counts, and \u0398 ~ Beta(w/c, b/c) is Max's long-run share.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Urn Dynamics:</strong> Start with $w$ white and $b$ black balls. Draw a ball, note its color, and replace it along with $c$ additional balls of the SAME color.",
      "<strong>Exchangeable Proof:</strong> The probability of any specific sequence with $k$ white and $(n - k)$ black balls is identical regardless of order: $\\frac{w(w+c)\\cdots(w+(k-1)c) \\cdot b(b+c)\\cdots(b+(n-k-1)c)}{(w+b)(w+b+c)\\cdots(w+b+(n-1)c)}$.",
      "<strong>Limiting Law:</strong> As $n \\to \\infty$, the proportion of white balls converges almost surely to random variable $\\Theta \\sim \\text{Beta}\\left(\\frac{w}{c}, \\frac{b}{c}\\right)$. For $w=1, b=1, c=1$, $\\Theta \\sim \\text{Uniform}(0, 1)$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{P}(X_1=x_1, \\dots, X_n=x_n) = \\frac{\\prod_{j=0}^{k-1}(w + jc) \\prod_{j=0}^{n-k-1}(b + jc)}{\\prod_{j=0}^{n-1}(w + b + jc)}, \\quad \\Theta \\sim \\text{Beta}\\left(\\tfrac{w}{c}, \\tfrac{b}{c}\\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The vote snowballs.</strong> Fans see the live Driver of the Day count, and each vote for Max makes the next fan a bit more likely to vote for him too. The order of the votes does not matter, only how many went to Max.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming P\u00f3lya's urn trials are independent. The draws are heavily dependent (positive feedback reinforcement), yet perfectly exchangeable!",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>P\u00f3lya's urn.</b> An urn has $w$ white and $b$ black balls; a ball is drawn and returned with $c$ more of its colour. With $k=\\sum x_i$ white draws, $\\mathbb P(X_1=x_1,\\ldots,X_n=x_n)=\\frac{\\prod_{j\\lt k}(w+jc)\\prod_{j\\lt n-k}(b+jc)}{\\prod_{j\\lt n}(w+b+jc)}$, which depends only on $k$: the draws are exchangeable, and $\\Theta\\sim\\mathrm{Beta}(\\frac wc,\\frac bc)$ (Ross 3.6; Grimmett 7.2).",
    "hint": "If every Driver of the Day vote for Max makes the next vote for him more likely, are the votes independent? Exchangeable?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\prod_{j\\lt k}(w+jc)$ = the white draws.</strong> The $j$-th white draw sees white grown by $jc$, in whatever positions they fall.",
      "<strong>$\\prod_{j\\lt n}(w+b+jc)$ = the growing urn.</strong> Each draw adds $c$ balls, the same for every sequence.",
      "<strong>$\\Theta\\sim\\mathrm{Beta}(w/c,b/c)$ = the long-run share.</strong> The chance depends on the count $k$, not the order: exchangeable, not independent."
    ],
