    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "Covariance Matrix Properties & Positive Semidefiniteness",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31101\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31101)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31101)\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">sector 1</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">sector 2</text><ellipse cx=\"76\" cy=\"64\" rx=\"44\" ry=\"18\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" transform=\"rotate(-35 76 64)\"/><line x1=\"76.0\" y1=\"64.0\" x2=\"118.0\" y2=\"36.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31101)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">v</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03a3 = \ud835\udd3c[(X \u2212 \u03bc)(X \u2212 \u03bc)\u1d40]</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">v\u1d40\u03a3v = Var(v\u1d40X) \u2265 0</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">so \u03a3 \u2ab0 0</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03a3(AX+b) = A \u03a3 A\u1d40</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">any direction v through the cloud has spread \u2265 0</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The cloud of (sector 1, sector 2) laps, its tilted outline, and a direction v. The spread of the projection onto v is v\u1d40\u03a3v = Var(v\u1d40X), never negative, so \u03a3 \u2ab0 0.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Definition:</strong> For random vector $X \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$, $\\Sigma_X \\triangleq \\mathbb{E}[(X - \\mu_X)(X - \\mu_X)^\\top] = \\mathbb{E}[XX^\\top] - \\mu_X\\mu_X^\\top$.",
      "<strong>Positive Semidefiniteness ($\\Sigma_X \\succeq 0$):</strong> For any deterministic vector $v \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$, $v^\\top \\Sigma_X v = \\operatorname{Var}(v^\\top X) \\ge 0$. All eigenvalues are real and non-negative ($\\lambda_i \\ge 0$).",
      "<strong>Affine Transformation Law:</strong> If $Y = A X + b$, then $\\mu_Y = A\\mu_X + b$ and $\\Sigma_Y = A \\Sigma_X A^\\top$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\Sigma_X = \\mathbb{E}[(X - \\mu)(X - \\mu)^\\top] \\succeq 0, \\qquad \\Sigma_{AX + b} = A \\Sigma_X A^\\top, \\qquad v^\\top \\Sigma_X v = \\operatorname{Var}(v^\\top X) \\ge 0$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The cloud of laps.</strong> Plot each of Max's laps as (sector 1 time, sector 2 time). The cloud has a shape, and along any direction you cut it, its spread is a variance: zero or more.",
    "examTrap": "Writing \u03a3_{AX} = A\u1d40 \u03a3_X A instead of A \u03a3_X A\u1d40! If A is m \u00d7 n, A \u03a3_X A\u1d40 produces the correct m \u00d7 m covariance matrix.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Covariance matrix.</b> For a random vector $X$ with mean $\\mu$, $\\Sigma_X=\\mathbb E[(X-\\mu)(X-\\mu)^\\top]$ is symmetric and positive semidefinite: $v^\\top\\Sigma_Xv=\\operatorname{Var}(v^\\top X)\\ge0$ for all $v$. Also $\\Sigma_{AX+b}=A\\Sigma_XA^\\top$ (Grimmett 3.6; Ross 7.4).",
    "hint": "Why can a table of covariances between Max's sector times never have a negative direction?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\Sigma_X=\\mathbb E[(X-\\mu)(X-\\mu)^\\top]$ = all variances and covariances in one table.</strong> Entry $(i,j)$ is how sector $i$ and sector $j$ move together.",
      "<strong>$v^\\top\\Sigma_Xv=\\operatorname{Var}(v^\\top X)$ = the spread along direction $v$.</strong> Any weighted mix of the sectors has a variance, which cannot be negative.",
      "<strong>$\\Sigma_{AX+b}=A\\Sigma_XA^\\top$ = how the table transforms.</strong> Shifting by $b$ changes nothing; mixing by $A$ sandwiches $\\Sigma$."
    ],
