    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31103\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31103)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31103)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X: quali gap</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Y: race gap</text><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"110\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"98\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"102\" cy=\"102\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"114\" cy=\"84\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"122\" cy=\"90\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"134\" cy=\"76\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"144\" cy=\"80\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"156\" cy=\"62\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"168\" cy=\"68\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"180\" cy=\"54\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"71\" r=\"2.8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"71.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"112.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"24.0\" y1=\"71.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"71.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bcX</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bcY</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u0176 = \u03bcY + K(X \u2212 \u03bcX)</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">K = \u03a3YX \u03a3X\u207b\u00b9 = slope</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">line through the means, tilted by how X and Y move together</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The scatter of (qualifying gap X, race gap Y). The best straight line passes through the means (\u03bcX, \u03bcY) with slope K = \u03a3YX \u03a3X\u207b\u00b9: \u0176 = \u03bcY + K(X \u2212 \u03bcX).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Closed-Form Estimator:</strong> $\\hat{Y}_{\\text{LLSE}}(X) = \\mu_Y + \\Sigma_{YX} \\Sigma_X^{-1} (X - \\mu_X)$, where $\\Sigma_{YX} = \\mathbb{E}[(Y - \\mu_Y)(X - \\mu_X)^\\top]$.",
      "<strong>Optimal Kalman Gain:</strong> The matrix $K \\triangleq \\Sigma_{YX} \\Sigma_X^{-1}$ is the optimal linear regression weight matrix.",
      "<strong>Data Parsimony:</strong> LLSE requires ONLY means $\\mu_X, \\mu_Y$ and covariances $\\Sigma_X, \\Sigma_{YX}$. It computes without knowing the underlying probability density functions."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\hat{Y}_{\\text{LLSE}}(X) = \\mu_Y + \\Sigma_{YX}\\Sigma_X^{-1}(X - \\mu_X), \\qquad K = \\Sigma_{YX}\\Sigma_X^{-1}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Reading Saturday for Sunday.</strong> Max takes pole by 0.4 s more than usual. If qualifying surprises usually carry over to the race, you pass most of that on to your guess of the race gap; if not, you add little to the usual gap.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming LLSE is the optimal overall estimator. LLSE is optimal ONLY among affine estimators (c\u1d40X + d). The unconditional MMSE estimator is conditional expectation \ud835\udd3c[Y|X], which may be highly non-linear.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Linear least squares estimator.</b> If $\\Sigma_X$ is invertible, the linear estimator of $Y$ from $X$ minimising mean squared error is $\\hat Y=\\mu_Y+\\Sigma_{YX}\\Sigma_X^{-1}(X-\\mu_X)$, with gain $K=\\Sigma_{YX}\\Sigma_X^{-1}$ (Grimmett 7.9; Ross 7.4).",
    "hint": "What is the best straight-line prediction of Max's race gap from his qualifying gap, using only means and covariances?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mu_Y+\\ldots$ = start from the average race gap.</strong> With no information, the best guess is the mean.",
      "<strong>$X-\\mu_X$ = how unusual the signal is.</strong> The qualifying gap's deviation from its own average is the news you add.",
      "<strong>$K=\\Sigma_{YX}\\Sigma_X^{-1}$ = the gain.</strong> How much of the qualifying surprise to pass on: covariance with the race gap, divided by the qualifying gap's own spread."
    ],
