    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31105\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"106\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"106\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"106\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"106\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c1\u03c3Y (explained)</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c3Y\u221a(1 \u2212 \u03c1\u00b2) (error)</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c3Y</text><line x1=\"158\" y1=\"106\" x2=\"158\" y2=\"94\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"158\" y1=\"94\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"94\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c3Y\u00b2 = \u03c1\u00b2\u03c3Y\u00b2 + \u03c3Y\u00b2(1 \u2212 \u03c1\u00b2)</text><text x=\"36\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">MSE = \u03c3Y\u00b2(1 \u2212 \u03c1\u00b2)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u0176 = \u03bcY + \u03c1(\u03c3Y/\u03c3X)(X \u2212 \u03bcX): the slope is \u03c1 in standard units</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A right triangle: hypotenuse \u03c3Y (total spread), one leg \u03c1\u03c3Y (explained by X), the other \u03c3Y\u221a(1 \u2212 \u03c1\u00b2) (error). Pythagoras gives MSE = \u03c3Y\u00b2(1 \u2212 \u03c1\u00b2).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Scalar Formula:</strong> $\\hat{Y} = \\mu_Y + \\rho \\frac{\\sigma_Y}{\\sigma_X} (X - \\mu_X)$, where Pearson correlation $\\rho = \\frac{\\operatorname{Cov}(X, Y)}{\\sigma_X \\sigma_Y} \\in [-1, 1]$.",
      "<strong>Slope & Anchor:</strong> The line passes through the bivariate centroid $(\\mu_X, \\mu_Y)$ with regression slope $\\beta = \\frac{\\operatorname{Cov}(X, Y)}{\\operatorname{Var}(X)} = \\rho \\frac{\\sigma_Y}{\\sigma_X}$.",
      "<strong>Residual MSE:</strong> $\\mathbb{E}[(Y - \\hat{Y})^2] = \\sigma_Y^2 (1 - \\rho^2)$. When $|\\rho| = 1$, MSE is 0 (exact prediction); when $\\rho = 0$, $\\hat{Y} = \\mu_Y$ and MSE is $\\sigma_Y^2$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\hat{Y} = \\mu_Y + \\rho \\frac{\\sigma_Y}{\\sigma_X}(X - \\mu_X), \\qquad \\operatorname{MSE} = \\sigma_Y^2(1 - \\rho^2)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>How much to believe qualifying.</strong> If the qualifying gap and the race gap have correlation 0.9, qualifying explains 81% of how the race gap varies; with correlation 0 it explains nothing and you stay with the average.",
    "examTrap": "Swapping X and Y in the regression slope: the slope for predicting Y from X is \u03c1(\u03c3_Y/\u03c3_X), while the slope for predicting X from Y is \u03c1(\u03c3_X/\u03c3_Y) (which is NOT 1/slope!).",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Scalar LLSE.</b> For scalar $X,Y$ with $\\sigma_X\\gt 0$, $\\hat Y=\\mu_Y+\\rho\\frac{\\sigma_Y}{\\sigma_X}(X-\\mu_X)$ with $\\rho=\\frac{\\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)}{\\sigma_X\\sigma_Y}$, and $\\mathbb E(Y-\\hat Y)^2=\\sigma_Y^2(1-\\rho^2)$ (Ross 7.4; Grimmett 3.6).",
    "hint": "How does one number, the correlation, set both the slope of the prediction and how good it is?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\rho=\\frac{\\operatorname{Cov}(X,Y)}{\\sigma_X\\sigma_Y}$ = covariance in standard units.</strong> A pure number between $-1$ and $1$: how tightly the qualifying gap and the race gap move together.",
      "<strong>$\\rho\\frac{\\sigma_Y}{\\sigma_X}$ = the slope.</strong> A one-spread surprise in qualifying predicts a $\\rho$-spread surprise in the race.",
      "<strong>$\\sigma_Y^2(1-\\rho^2)$ = the error.</strong> A share $\\rho^2$ of the race gap's variance is explained; the rest is left."
    ],
