    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "Worked Benchmark: Signal Estimation in Additive Noise (Wiener Filter)",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31106\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31106)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">s off usual pace</text><line x1=\"124\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"124\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><circle cx=\"174\" cy=\"70\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"174\" y=\"58\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y (one lap's reading)</text><circle cx=\"154\" cy=\"70\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"154\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u0302 = shrink Y</text><line x1=\"124\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"174\" y2=\"44\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y = X + W</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u0302 = \u03c3X\u00b2/(\u03c3X\u00b2 + \u03c3W\u00b2) \u00b7 Y</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">MSE = \u03c3X\u00b2\u03c3W\u00b2 / (\u03c3X\u00b2 + \u03c3W\u00b2)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">trust one lap only as much as signal outweighs noise</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">SNR = \u03c3X\u00b2/\u03c3W\u00b2</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The reading Y = X + W on a line of seconds off usual pace, and the estimate X\u0302 pulled toward 0 by the trust factor \u03c3X\u00b2/(\u03c3X\u00b2 + \u03c3W\u00b2), with the leftover error \u03c3X\u00b2\u03c3W\u00b2/(\u03c3X\u00b2 + \u03c3W\u00b2).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Problem Setup:</strong> Signal $X$ has mean $0$ and variance $\\sigma_X^2$. Observation is $Y = X + W$, where noise $W$ has mean $0$, variance $\\sigma_W^2$, and $X \\perp W$.",
      "<strong>Covariance Derivation:</strong> $\\operatorname{Var}(Y) = \\sigma_X^2 + \\sigma_W^2$. Cross-covariance is $\\operatorname{Cov}(X, Y) = \\mathbb{E}[X(X + W)] = \\mathbb{E}[X^2] = \\sigma_X^2$.",
      "<strong>Wiener Shrinkage Estimator:</strong> $\\hat{X}(Y) = \\frac{\\sigma_X^2}{\\sigma_X^2 + \\sigma_W^2} Y = \\frac{\\text{SNR}}{1 + \\text{SNR}} Y$. Minimum MSE is $\\frac{\\sigma_X^2 \\sigma_W^2}{\\sigma_X^2 + \\sigma_W^2}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\hat{X}(Y) = \\frac{\\sigma_X^2}{\\sigma_X^2 + \\sigma_W^2} Y, \\qquad \\operatorname{MSE} = \\frac{\\sigma_X^2 \\sigma_W^2}{\\sigma_X^2 + \\sigma_W^2} = \\sigma_X^2 \\left(1 - \\frac{\\text{SNR}}{1 + \\text{SNR}}\\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>One fast lap in practice.</strong> Max sets a lap 0.5 s quicker than his usual pace. If single laps are very noisy, the engineers shade that down to a fraction; if laps are clean, they take it almost at face value.",
    "examTrap": "Using raw observation Y as the estimator without shrinkage! Y is unbiased, but has MSE equal to \u03c3_W\u00b2, which is strictly WORSE than the Wiener estimate's MSE.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Wiener filter (scalar).</b> Let $Y=X+W$ with $X,W$ independent, zero mean, variances $\\sigma_X^2,\\sigma_W^2$. Then $\\hat X(Y)=\\frac{\\sigma_X^2}{\\sigma_X^2+\\sigma_W^2}Y$ and $\\operatorname{MSE}=\\frac{\\sigma_X^2\\sigma_W^2}{\\sigma_X^2+\\sigma_W^2}$ (Grimmett 7.9; Ross 7.4).",
    "hint": "One lap time is Max's true pace plus noise. How much of what it shows should you trust?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$Y=X+W$ = the true pace plus lap noise.</strong> What you see is the signal $X$ blurred by independent error $W$ (wind, a lock-up, a backmarker).",
      "<strong>$\\frac{\\sigma_X^2}{\\sigma_X^2+\\sigma_W^2}$ = the trust factor.</strong> Close to 1 if the signal's spread dominates, close to 0 if the noise does; the estimate shrinks $Y$ toward 0.",
      "<strong>$\\frac{\\sigma_X^2\\sigma_W^2}{\\sigma_X^2+\\sigma_W^2}$ = the error left.</strong> It is smaller than both $\\sigma_X^2$ and $\\sigma_W^2$: combining knowledge helps."
    ],
