    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31201\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31201)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31201)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X: tyre age</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"10\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Y: lap time</text><circle cx=\"44\" cy=\"70\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"56\" cy=\"52\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"66\" cy=\"60\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"46\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"56\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"104\" cy=\"62\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"118\" cy=\"52\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"132\" cy=\"68\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"82\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"170\" cy=\"96\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"186\" cy=\"90\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M36.0,74.7 L38.7,72.9 L41.5,71.0 L44.2,68.9 L46.9,66.7 L49.7,64.4 L52.4,62.0 L55.1,59.6 L57.9,57.1 L60.6,54.6 L63.3,52.2 L66.1,49.8 L68.8,47.6 L71.5,45.4 L74.3,43.5 L77.0,41.9 L79.7,40.4 L82.5,39.3 L85.2,38.5 L87.9,38.1 L90.7,38.0 L93.4,38.3 L96.1,38.9 L98.9,39.8 L101.6,41.1 L104.3,42.6 L107.1,44.4 L109.8,46.5 L112.5,48.6 L115.3,51.0 L118.0,53.4 L120.7,55.8 L123.5,58.3 L126.2,60.8 L128.9,63.2 L131.7,65.5 L134.4,67.8 L137.1,69.9 L139.9,71.9 L142.6,73.8 L145.3,75.6 L148.1,77.2 L150.8,78.8 L153.5,80.2 L156.3,81.5 L159.0,82.8 L161.7,83.9 L164.5,85.0 L167.2,86.1 L169.9,87.1 L172.7,88.0 L175.4,89.0 L178.1,89.9 L180.9,90.8 L183.6,91.7 L186.3,92.6 L189.1,93.5 L191.8,94.5 L194.5,95.4 L197.3,96.3 L200.0,97.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[Y | X]</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[Y | X] = argmin \ud835\udd3c[(Y \u2212 g(X))\u00b2]</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[\ud835\udd3c[Y | X]] = \ud835\udd3c[Y]</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the best guess is the average of Y on each vertical slice</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The scatter of (tyre age X, lap time Y). The curve \ud835\udd3c[Y | X] passes through the average of Y on each slice of X and minimises the squared error over all functions of X.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Optimization Problem:</strong> Find $g^*(X) = \\arg\\min_{g} \\mathbb{E}[(Y - g(X))^2]$ over ALL measurable functions (linear or non-linear).",
      "<strong>Fundamental Theorem:</strong> The unique minimizer is the conditional expectation: $g^*(X) = \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X] = \\int y f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\mid X)\\,dy$.",
      "<strong>Random Variable Character:</strong> $\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]$ is NOT a fixed number! It is a random variable measurable with respect to $\\sigma(X)$, taking value $\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X=x]$ when $X=x$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\hat{Y}_{\\text{MMSE}} = \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X] = \\arg\\min_{g \\in \\sigma(X)} \\mathbb{E}\\left[(Y - g(X))^2\\right], \\qquad \\mathbb{E}\\left[\\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]\\right] = \\mathbb{E}[Y]$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The average of similar laps.</strong> Among all of Max's laps on tyres of the same age, take the average lap time. Doing this for every tyre age gives the best possible guess of the next lap.",
    "examTrap": "Treating \ud835\udd3c[Y|X] as a deterministic number! \ud835\udd3c[Y|X] is a random variable, a function of X. Only when evaluated at a fixed sample realization X = x does it become a constant.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Conditional expectation as best guess.</b> If $\\mathbb E[Y^2]\\lt \\infty$, then $\\hat Y=\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X]$ is the unique (a.s.) function of $X$ minimising $\\mathbb E[(Y-g(X))^2]$ over all $g$ with $\\mathbb E[g(X)^2]\\lt \\infty$, and $\\mathbb E[\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X]]=\\mathbb E[Y]$ (Ross 7.5; Grimmett 3.7, 7.9).",
    "hint": "With no restriction on the form of your guess, which function of the tyre age predicts Max's lap time best?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X]$ = the average lap time given what you know.</strong> On each value of $X$, take the average of $Y$ over laps with that $X$.",
      "<strong>$\\arg\\min_g\\mathbb E[(Y-g(X))^2]$ = best of all functions.</strong> No straight-line restriction: the curve through the slice averages wins.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X]]=\\mathbb E[Y]$ = averaging the guesses gives the overall average.</strong> The slice averages, weighted by how common each slice is."
    ],
