    "cardNumber": "02",
    "category": "ORTHOGONALITY",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-amber",
    "title": "The Non-Linear Orthogonality Principle: L\u00b2(\u03c3(X))",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31202\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><polygon points=\"30,100 150,100 200,70 80,70\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">all functions h(X): L\u00b2(\u03c3(X))</text><line x1=\"110.0\" y1=\"85.0\" x2=\"110.0\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31202)\"/><text x=\"116\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Y \u2212 \ud835\udd3c[Y | X]</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y</text><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"85\" r=\"2.4\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"118\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[Y | X]</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[(Y \u2212 \ud835\udd3c[Y | X]) h(X)] = 0 for every h</text><text x=\"106.78\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the error is orthogonal to every function of X, not just straight lines</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">so it is the nearest point of the whole sheet</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The sheet of all functions h(X) of what you know. The best guess \ud835\udd3c[Y | X] is the foot of the perpendicular from Y, and the error Y \u2212 \ud835\udd3c[Y | X] is orthogonal to every h(X).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Orthogonality Condition:</strong> For any measurable function $h(X)$ with $\\mathbb{E}[h(X)^2] \\lt  \\infty$, $\\mathbb{E}[(Y - \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]) h(X)] = 0$.",
      "<strong>Zero Residual Prediction:</strong> No transformation of $X$\u2014whether $X, X^2, e^X$, or a deep neural network\u2014can extract any further predictive correlation from the residual error.",
      "<strong>Unbiasedness:</strong> Setting $h(X) = 1$ immediately proves $\\mathbb{E}[Y - \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]] = 0$, guaranteeing that the MMSE estimator is unconditionally unbiased."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{E}\\left[\\left(Y - \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid X]\\right) h(X)\\right] = 0 \\quad \\forall h \\in L^2(\\sigma(X))$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Nothing left to learn.</strong> After the best guess from tyre age, no trick with the tyre age, however clever, predicts the leftover error: all the information in the tyre age has been used.",
    "examTrap": "Confusing LLSE with MMSE orthogonality! LLSE error is orthogonal only to affine functions aX + b; MMSE error is orthogonal to ALL measurable non-linear functions h(X).",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Orthogonality in $L^2$.</b> For $\\mathbb E[Y^2]\\lt \\infty$, $\\hat Y=\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X]$ is the orthogonal projection of $Y$ onto $L^2(\\sigma(X))$: $\\mathbb E\\bigl[(Y-\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X])h(X)\\bigr]=0$ for all $h$ with $\\mathbb E[h(X)^2]\\lt \\infty$ (Grimmett 7.9).",
    "hint": "Which property of the error tells you the conditional average is the nearest possible guess?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$h(X)$ = any function of what you know.</strong> Not just straight lines: squares, thresholds, anything computed from $X$.",
      "<strong>$Y-\\mathbb E[Y\\mid X]$ = what the best guess misses.</strong> The part of the lap time that $X$ does not pin down.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[(\\ldots)h(X)]=0$ = the miss is uncorrelated with every function of $X$.</strong> Nothing computed from $X$ can predict the miss."
    ],
