    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31304\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31304)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"16\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31304)\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2082</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2081</text><ellipse cx=\"76\" cy=\"62\" rx=\"46\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" transform=\"rotate(-35 76 62)\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"126\" y2=\"26\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"84\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"84\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">x\u2082</text><text x=\"150.2\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2081 | X\u2082 = x\u2082 ~ \ud835\udca9(m, S)</text><text x=\"141.36\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">m = \u03bc\u2081 + \u03a3\u2081\u2082\u03a3\u2082\u2082\u207b\u00b9(x\u2082 \u2212 \u03bc\u2082)</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">S = \u03a3\u2081\u2081 \u2212 \u03a3\u2081\u2082\u03a3\u2082\u2082\u207b\u00b9\u03a3\u2082\u2081</text><text x=\"137.72\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">m is the LLSE; S its error:</text><text x=\"145.0\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">MMSE = LLSE for Gaussians</text><text x=\"109.25\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">slice the cloud at x\u2082: a bell, centred on the line, narrower than the cloud</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The cloud sliced at x\u2082 gives a narrower bell for X\u2081, centred on the line m = \u03bc\u2081 + \u03a3\u2081\u2082\u03a3\u2082\u2082\u207b\u00b9(x\u2082 \u2212 \u03bc\u2082) with spread S = \u03a3\u2081\u2081 \u2212 \u03a3\u2081\u2082\u03a3\u2082\u2082\u207b\u00b9\u03a3\u2082\u2081.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Conditional Law:</strong> If $\\begin{bmatrix} X_1 \\\\ X_2 \\end{bmatrix} \\sim \\mathcal{N}\\left(\\begin{bmatrix}\\mu_1\\\\\\mu_2\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}\\Sigma_{11}&\\Sigma_{12}\\\\\\Sigma_{21}&\\Sigma_{22}\\end{bmatrix}\\right)$, then $X_1 \\mid X_2 = x_2 \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_{1|2}, \\Sigma_{1|2})$.",
      "<strong>Linear Conditional Mean:</strong> $\\mu_{1|2} = \\mu_1 + \\Sigma_{12} \\Sigma_{22}^{-1}(x_2 - \\mu_2)$. The conditional mean is strictly affine, proving **MMSE $\\equiv$ LLSE**!",
      "<strong>Constant Conditional Covariance:</strong> $\\Sigma_{1|2} = \\Sigma_{11} - \\Sigma_{12} \\Sigma_{22}^{-1} \\Sigma_{21}$ is completely independent of the observed value $x_2$."
    ],
    "math": "$$X_1 \\mid X_2 = x_2 \\sim \\mathcal{N}\\left(\\mu_1 + \\Sigma_{12}\\Sigma_{22}^{-1}(x_2 - \\mu_2), \\; \\Sigma_{11} - \\Sigma_{12}\\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\\Sigma_{21}\\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Slicing the cloud.</strong> Among Max's laps with the same sector 2 time, the sector 1 times form a bell centred on the regression line, narrower than over all laps, and equally wide whatever the sector 2 time was.",
    "examTrap": "Expecting conditional variance \u03a3_{1|2} to change with observation x\u2082! For Gaussians, measurements shift the mean, but uncertainty reduction is invariant to observed data.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Gaussian conditioning.</b> If $(X_1,X_2)\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mu,\\Sigma)$ with $\\Sigma_{22}\\succ0$, then $X_1\\mid X_2=x_2\\sim\\mathcal N\\bigl(\\mu_1+\\Sigma_{12}\\Sigma_{22}^{-1}(x_2-\\mu_2),\\ \\Sigma_{11}-\\Sigma_{12}\\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\\Sigma_{21}\\bigr)$. So $\\mathbb E[X_1\\mid X_2]$ equals the LLSE: MMSE $=$ LLSE (Ross 7.8; Grimmett 4.9).",
    "hint": "Given one jointly Gaussian sector time, what is the law of the other, and how does it compare to the best straight-line guess?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mu_1+\\Sigma_{12}\\Sigma_{22}^{-1}(x_2-\\mu_2)$ = the conditional mean.</strong> It is exactly the straight-line LLSE: the guess moves linearly with what you see.",
      "<strong>$\\Sigma_{11}-\\Sigma_{12}\\Sigma_{22}^{-1}\\Sigma_{21}$ = the conditional spread.</strong> The Schur complement; it does not depend on the value $x_2$ you saw.",
      "<strong>Still normal.</strong> Slicing a Gaussian cloud gives a Gaussian slice, so the best guess of any kind is the linear one."
    ],
