    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31402\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31402)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31402)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">number of pit stops</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">time per stop</text><rect x=\"24\" y=\"52\" width=\"110\" height=\"60\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"79\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">area = \ud835\udd3c[S]</text><text x=\"79\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[N]</text><text x=\"19.6\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[X]</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[S] = \ud835\udd3c[N] \u00b7 \ud835\udd3c[X]</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">needs \ud835\udd3c[N] &lt; \u221e,</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c|X| &lt; \u221e</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">N must be a stopping</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">rule: no peeking ahead</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A rectangle of width \ud835\udd3c[N] (average number of pit stops) and height \ud835\udd3c[X] (average time per stop). Its area is \ud835\udd3c[S] = \ud835\udd3c[N]\u00b7\ud835\udd3c[X].",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Theorem Statement:</strong> If $X_i$ are i.i.d. with $\\mathbb{E}[|X|] \\lt  \\infty$ and $N$ is a stopping time with $\\mathbb{E}[N] \\lt  \\infty$, then $\\mathbb{E}[S_N] = \\mathbb{E}[N]\\,\\mathbb{E}[X]$.",
      "<strong>Indicator Proof:</strong> $\\mathbb{E}[S_N] = \\mathbb{E}[\\sum_{i=1}^\\infty X_i \\mathbf{1}_{\\{N \\ge i\\}}] = \\sum_{i=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{E}[X_i] \\mathbb{P}(N \\ge i) = \\mathbb{E}[X] \\sum_{i=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(N \\ge i) = \\mathbb{E}[X]\\mathbb{E}[N]$.",
      "<strong>Tower Proof (if $N \\perp X$):</strong> By the law of total expectation, $\\mathbb{E}[S_N] = \\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[S_N \\mid N]] = \\mathbb{E}[N \\mathbb{E}[X]] = \\mathbb{E}[N]\\,\\mathbb{E}[X]$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{E}\\left[\\sum_{i=1}^N X_i\\right] = \\mathbb{E}[N]\\,\\mathbb{E}[X], \\quad \\text{provided } \\mathbb{E}[N] \\lt  \\infty, \\; \\mathbb{E}[|X|] \\lt  \\infty$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Average stops times average stop.</strong> If Max makes 1.8 stops a race on average and the car stands still for 2.5 seconds per stop on average, his average total time standing still is 4.5 seconds, even though the number of stops is random.",
    "examTrap": "Ignoring integrability conditions: if \ud835\udd3c[N] = \u221e or \ud835\udd3c[|X|] = \u221e, Wald's equation breaks down and can yield undefined \u221e \u00d7 0 forms.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Wald's first identity.</b> Let $X_1,X_2,\\ldots$ be i.i.d. with $\\mathbb E|X|\\lt \\infty$ and $N$ a stopping time with $\\mathbb E[N]\\lt \\infty$. Then $\\mathbb E\\bigl[\\sum_{i=1}^NX_i\\bigr]=\\mathbb E[N]\\,\\mathbb E[X]$ (Ross 7.5; Grimmett 12.5).",
    "hint": "With a random number of pit stops, what is the average total time Max spends standing in the pits?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[N]$ = the average number of stops.</strong> How many times Max pits in a typical race.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[X]$ = the average time of one stop.</strong> The same for every stop, since the stop times are identically distributed.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[N]\\,\\mathbb E[X]$ = the product.</strong> Write $S_N=\\sum X_i\\mathbf 1_{\\{N\\ge i\\}}$ and take expectations term by term; the switch is independent of $X_i$, so each term is $\\mathbb E[X]\\mathbb P(N\\ge i)$ and $\\sum\\mathbb P(N\\ge i)=\\mathbb E[N]$."
    ],
