    "id": 31404,
    "subject": "StoMA",
    "topicId": "14_Random_Sums_and_Walds_Equation",
    "topicTitle": "14 \u00b7 Random Sums & Wald\u2019s Identity",
    "cardNumber": "04",
    "category": "COMPOUND DISTRIBUTIONS",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-purple",
    "title": "Compound Distributions: Functional Composition of PGFs & MGFs",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31404\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"20\" y=\"56\" width=\"40\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">t</text><rect x=\"88\" y=\"56\" width=\"62\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"119.0\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">M(t) of one stop</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"56\" width=\"66\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"197.0\" y=\"71\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">G(\u00b7) of the count</text><line x1=\"60.0\" y1=\"67.0\" x2=\"88.0\" y2=\"67.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31404)\"/><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"67.0\" x2=\"164.0\" y2=\"67.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31404)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">MGF of total = G of N applied to the stop MGF</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[e^(tS)] = G\u2099(M\u2093(t))   and   \ud835\udd3c[s^S] = G\u2099(G\u2093(s))</text><text x=\"117.7\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">condition on N: the stops multiply, then average the power over N</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A chain of boxes: the argument t goes into one stop's MGF M\u2093(t), whose value is fed into the count's generating function G\u2099, giving the MGF of the total time in the pits.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Compound MGF:</strong> $M_{S_N}(t) \\triangleq \\mathbb{E}[e^{t S_N}] = \\mathbb{E}[\\mathbb{E}[e^{t \\sum X_i} \\mid N]] = \\mathbb{E}[(M_X(t))^N] = G_N(M_X(t))$.",
      "<strong>Compound PGF:</strong> For discrete non-negative integer RVs $X_i \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$, $G_{S_N}(s) \\triangleq \\mathbb{E}[s^{S_N}] = G_N(G_X(s))$ (exact nested functional composition).",
      "<strong>Cumulant Generating Function:</strong> $\\log M_{S_N}(t) = \\log G_N(M_X(t))$. Successive derivatives at $t=0$ generate all higher-order cumulants and skewness."
    ],
    "math": "$$M_{S_N}(t) = G_N\\left(M_X(t)\\right), \\qquad G_{S_N}(s) = G_N\\left(G_X(s)\\right) \\quad (X_i \\in \\mathbb{N}_0)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Plug one into the other.</strong> To describe the total time in the pits, take the description of one stop and feed it into the description of the number of stops. The same trick gives Max's season points: feed the points-per-race law into the law of how many races he scores in.",
    "examTrap": "Swapping the composition order: writing M_X(G_N(t)) instead of G_N(M_X(t))! The outer function is always the counter N; the inner function is the term X.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Compound generating functions.</b> If $N$ is independent of the i.i.d. $X_i$, then $M_{S_N}(t)=G_N\\bigl(M_X(t)\\bigr)$, and for $X_i\\in\\{0,1,2,\\ldots\\}$, $G_{S_N}(s)=G_N\\bigl(G_X(s)\\bigr)$ (Ross 7.7; Grimmett 5.1).",
    "hint": "How do you find the generating function of a random sum, like the total pit time or Max's points from a random number of scoring races, from those of the count and of one term?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$M_X(t)$ = the MGF of one stop's time.</strong> Given $N=n$, independent stops multiply: $\\mathbb E[e^{tS}\\mid N=n]=M_X(t)^n$.",
      "<strong>$G_N(u)=\\mathbb E[u^N]$ = the count's generating function.</strong> Averaging $u^N$ over $N$, with $u=M_X(t)$.",
      "<strong>$G_N(M_X(t))$ = compose.</strong> The same works for counts, such as points from a random number of scoring races: $G_{S_N}(s)=G_N(G_X(s))$. Differentiating at $s=1$ gives Wald's identities."
    ],
