    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "Galton-Watson Branching Processes & Extinction Probability",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31405\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"74\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"78\" y2=\"54\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"54\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"78\" y2=\"94\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"94\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"78\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"116\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"78\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"116\" y2=\"66\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"78\" y1=\"94\" x2=\"116\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"78\" y1=\"94\" x2=\"116\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"40\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"66\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"90\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"112\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Z\u2080</text><text x=\"78\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Z\u2081</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Z\u2082</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">each singer pulls in \u03be others</text><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31405)\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31405)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">s</text><path d=\"M150.0,97.6 L152.5,97.3 L155.1,96.9 L157.6,96.4 L160.1,95.7 L162.7,95.0 L165.2,94.1 L167.7,93.2 L170.3,92.1 L172.8,90.9 L175.3,89.6 L177.9,88.2 L180.4,86.7 L182.9,85.0 L185.5,83.3 L188.0,81.4 L190.5,79.4 L193.1,77.3 L195.6,75.1 L198.1,72.8 L200.7,70.4 L203.2,67.9 L205.7,65.2 L208.3,62.5 L210.8,59.6 L213.3,56.6 L215.9,53.5 L218.4,50.3 L220.9,47.0 L223.5,43.5 L226.0,40.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"134.07999999999998\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u2080: smallest s with s = G(s)</text><text x=\"130.44\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3c[Z\u2099] = \u03bc\u207f: dies out if \u03bc \u2264 1</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A tree Z\u2080, Z\u2081, Z\u2082 of fans joining the chant round by round, and the PGF G(s) against the line y = s. The extinction probability \u03c0\u2080 is the smallest s where they meet.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Model Formulation:</strong> $Z_0 = 1$. Generation $n+1$ has size $Z_{n+1} = \\sum_{i=1}^{Z_n} \\xi_{n,i}$ where $\\xi_{n,i} \\stackrel{\\text{i.i.d.}}{\\sim} \\xi$. By Wald's equation, $\\mathbb{E}[Z_n] = \\mu^n$ with $\\mu = \\mathbb{E}[\\xi]$.",
      "<strong>Phase Transition:</strong> (1) If $\\mu \\lt  1$ (subcritical) or $\\mu = 1$ (critical, $\\xi \\not\\equiv 1$), extinction is CERTAIN: $\\pi_0 = 1$; (2) If $\\mu > 1$ (supercritical), survival is possible: $\\pi_0 \\lt  1$.",
      "<strong>Fixed-Point Theorem:</strong> The extinction probability $\\pi_0 = \\mathbb{P}(\\lim Z_n = 0)$ is the SMALLEST non-negative root of the fixed-point equation $s = G_\\xi(s)$ in $[0, 1]$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{E}[Z_n] = \\mu^n \\quad (\\mu = \\mathbb{E}[\\xi]); \\qquad \\pi_0 = \\min \\{s \\in [0, 1] : s = G_\\xi(s)\\}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A chant in the grandstand.</strong> One fan in the orange stand starts singing for Max; each singer pulls in a random number of neighbours, who pull in others. If on average each singer brings in at most one new one, the chant surely dies out; otherwise it may take over the whole stand.",
    "examTrap": "Selecting the trivial root s = 1 when solving s = G(s). The root s = 1 is always a mathematical solution (G(1)=1); the true extinction probability is the SMALLEST root in [0, 1].",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Galton\u2013Watson process.</b> Let $Z_0=1$ and $Z_{n+1}=\\sum_{i=1}^{Z_n}\\xi_{n,i}$ with i.i.d. offspring counts $\\xi$, mean $\\mu$ and PGF $G$. Then $\\mathbb E[Z_n]=\\mu^n$, and the extinction probability $\\pi_0=\\mathbb P(Z_n=0\\text{ for some }n)$ is the smallest root of $s=G(s)$ in $[0,1]$; $\\pi_0=1$ iff $\\mu\\le1$ (excluding $\\xi\\equiv1$) (Ross 4.7; Grimmett 5.4).",
    "hint": "If each fan singing a chant pulls in a random number of new singers, when does the chant surely die out?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$Z_{n+1}=\\sum_{i\\le Z_n}\\xi_{n,i}$ = a random sum.</strong> Each of the $Z_n$ singers in round $n$ pulls in their own number of new singers in the next round.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[Z_n]=\\mu^n$ = Wald, round by round.</strong> The expected size is multiplied by $\\mu$ each time: it grows if $\\mu\\gt 1$ and shrinks if $\\mu\\lt 1$.",
      "<strong>$\\pi_0=G(\\pi_0)$ = the extinction chance.</strong> The chant dies out if every line started in the first round dies out: the smallest solution of $s=G(s)$; it is 1 when $\\mu\\le1$."
    ],
