    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "The Sliding Typewriter: Convergence in Probability \u2260 Almost Sure",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31503\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">lap n question: is the warning light on (X\u2099 = 1)?</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"34\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"34\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"26\" width=\"180\" height=\"8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"33\" font-size=\"6\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2081</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"46\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"46\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"38\" width=\"90.0\" height=\"8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"6\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2082</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"58\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"120.0\" y=\"50\" width=\"90.0\" height=\"8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"57\" font-size=\"6\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2083</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"30\" y=\"62\" width=\"45.0\" height=\"8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"6\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2084</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"75.0\" y=\"74\" width=\"45.0\" height=\"8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"81\" font-size=\"6\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2085</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"94\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"94\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"120.0\" y=\"86\" width=\"45.0\" height=\"8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"6\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2086</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"106\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"106\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"165.0\" y=\"98\" width=\"45.0\" height=\"8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#d9dee7\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"6\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">X\u2087</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(X\u2099 = 1) = width \u2192 0 \u21d2 X\u2099 \u2192 0 in probability</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">but every \u03c9 is covered again and again: no a.s. limit</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">lim sup X\u2099(\u03c9) = 1 for every \u03c9</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Rows are laps X\u2081, X\u2082, \u2026: a block of width 1/k sweeping across [0,1], the set of all races. The block shrinks, so \u2119(X\u2099 = 1) \u2192 0, but it keeps sweeping, so no single race \u03c9 has a limit.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Typewriter Construction:</strong> On $\\Omega = [0, 1]$ with uniform Lebesgue measure. Let $X_n = \\mathbf{1}_{I_n}$ where intervals $I_n$ of width $1/k$ sweep from left to right across $[0, 1]$ repeatedly.",
      "<strong>Convergence in Probability:</strong> $\\mathbb{P}(|X_n| \\ge \\epsilon) = \\text{Length}(I_n) = 1/k \\to 0$, so $X_n \\xrightarrow{P} 0$.",
      "<strong>Almost Sure Divergence:</strong> Because the intervals sweep past every point $\\omega \\in [0, 1]$ infinitely many times, the sequence of values $X_n(\\omega)$ oscillates between $0$ and $1$ forever for EVERY $\\omega$. Thus $\\mathbb{P}(\\lim X_n = 0) = 0$!"
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb{P}(X_n = 1) = \\frac{1}{k} \\to 0 \\implies X_n \\xrightarrow{P} 0, \\quad \\text{yet } \\limsup_{n \\to \\infty} X_n(\\omega) = 1 \\quad \\forall \\omega \\implies X_n \\not\\xrightarrow{a.s.} 0$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A warning light that wanders.</strong> Picture an endless race. On each lap, a small and shrinking slice of all possible races gets a warning light on Max's steering wheel. On any one lap he is almost surely fine, yet in every possible race the light comes on again and again.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming that \u2119(|X_n| \u2265 \u03b5) \u2192 0 guarantees sample paths settle down. Probability measures only instantaneous mass size; almost sure convergence requires mass to stop wandering across points.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Sliding typewriter.</b> On $\\Omega=[0,1]$ with Lebesgue measure, enumerate intervals of length $1/k$ sweeping $[0,1]$ for $k=1,2,\\ldots$, and let $X_n=\\mathbf 1_{I_n}$ for the $n$-th interval. Then $\\mathbb P(X_n=1)=1/k\\to0$, so $X_n\\xrightarrow{P}0$, but each $\\omega$ lies in infinitely many $I_n$, so $\\limsup X_n(\\omega)=1$ for all $\\omega$: $X_n\\not\\to0$ a.s. (Grimmett 7.2; Durrett 2.3).",
    "hint": "Can a warning light be almost surely off on any given lap, and yet never stay off in any single race?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(X_n=1)=1/k\\to0$ = a shrinking block.</strong> On lap $n$ the light is on only for a block of races of width $1/k$, whose chance goes to zero.",
      "<strong>$\\limsup X_n(\\omega)=1$ = every race is hit again.</strong> Each sweep of the blocks passes over every race $\\omega$, so in every race the light comes on infinitely often.",
      "<strong>$\\not\\to0$ a.s. = no race settles.</strong> In each race the light flips between 0 and 1 forever, so a.s. convergence fails though convergence in probability holds."
    ],
