    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31506\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31506)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31506)\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">numerator</text><path d=\"M30.0,89.3 L31.9,89.0 L33.9,88.4 L35.9,87.6 L37.8,86.5 L39.8,85.0 L41.7,83.0 L43.6,80.5 L45.6,77.5 L47.5,73.9 L49.5,69.8 L51.5,65.3 L53.4,60.5 L55.4,55.7 L57.3,51.1 L59.2,47.0 L61.2,43.7 L63.1,41.3 L65.1,40.1 L67.0,40.2 L69.0,41.5 L71.0,43.9 L72.9,47.3 L74.8,51.5 L76.8,56.1 L78.8,60.9 L80.7,65.7 L82.7,70.2 L84.6,74.2 L86.5,77.8 L88.5,80.8 L90.5,83.2 L92.4,85.1 L94.3,86.6 L96.3,87.7 L98.2,88.4 L100.2,89.0 L102.2,89.4 L104.1,89.6 L106.0,89.8 L108.0,89.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"38\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u221an(X\u0304 \u2212 \u03bc)/\u03c3 \u2192 \ud835\udca9(0,1)</text><line x1=\"124\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31506)\"/><line x1=\"124\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31506)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">S\u2099/\u03c3</text><path d=\"M130.0,90.0 L132.3,90.0 L134.6,90.0 L136.9,90.0 L139.2,90.0 L141.5,90.0 L143.8,90.0 L146.1,90.0 L148.4,90.0 L150.7,90.0 L153.0,90.0 L155.3,89.7 L157.6,88.7 L159.9,85.3 L162.2,76.9 L164.5,61.8 L166.8,43.6 L169.1,31.2 L171.4,32.9 L173.7,47.4 L176.0,65.6 L178.3,79.3 L180.6,86.4 L182.9,89.1 L185.2,89.8 L187.5,90.0 L189.8,90.0 L192.1,90.0 L194.4,90.0 L196.7,90.0 L199.0,90.0 L201.3,90.0 L203.6,90.0 L205.9,90.0 L208.2,90.0 L210.5,90.0 L212.8,90.0 L215.1,90.0 L217.4,90.0 L219.7,90.0 L222.0,90.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2192 1 in prob.</text><text x=\"66\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u00f7</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">T\u2099 \u2192 \ud835\udca9(0,1)/1 = \ud835\udca9(0,1)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Slutsky: unknown \u03c3 replaced by S\u2099 costs nothing in the limit</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A numerator that tends to the standard bell and a denominator S\u2099/\u03c3 that tends to 1. Slutsky divides one by the other: T\u2099 \u2192 \ud835\udca9(0,1)/1 = \ud835\udca9(0,1).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Problem Setup:</strong> For i.i.d. $X_i \\sim (\\mu, \\sigma^2)$, test statistic is $T_n = \\frac{\\sqrt{n}(\\bar{X}_n - \\mu)}{S_n}$ where $S_n^2 = \\frac{1}{n-1}\\sum (X_i - \\bar{X}_n)^2$.",
      "<strong>Component Decomposition:</strong> Numerator $Z_n = \\frac{\\sqrt{n}(\\bar{X}_n - \\mu)}{\\sigma} \\xrightarrow{d} \\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$ by Central Limit Theorem. Denominator $\\frac{S_n}{\\sigma} \\xrightarrow{P} 1$ by WLLN and Continuous Mapping Theorem.",
      "<strong>Slutsky Ratio Law:</strong> By Slutsky's theorem with constant $c = 1$, $T_n = \\frac{Z_n}{S_n / \\sigma} \\xrightarrow{d} \\frac{\\mathcal{N}(0, 1)}{1} = \\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$. Student's $t$ statistic is asymptotically Gaussian!"
    ],
    "math": "$$T_n = \\frac{\\sqrt{n}(\\bar{X}_n - \\mu)}{S_n} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{n}(\\bar{X}_n - \\mu)}{\\sigma}}{\\frac{S_n}{\\sigma}} \\xrightarrow{d} \\frac{\\mathcal{N}(0, 1)}{1} = \\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Not knowing the spread costs nothing.</strong> After enough laps the engineers can replace the true spread of the gap between Max and Checo by the sample spread, and the bell-curve answer for the average gap stays the same.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming T_n is strictly Gaussian for finite n! T_n has heavier polynomial tails (Student's t) for finite n; it becomes Gaussian ONLY in the asymptotic limit n \u2192 \u221e.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Asymptotic normality of the $t$-statistic.</b> For i.i.d. $X_i$ with mean $\\mu$, variance $\\sigma^2\\in(0,\\infty)$ and sample variance $S_n^2$: $\\sqrt n(\\bar X_n-\\mu)/\\sigma\\xrightarrow{d}\\mathcal N(0,1)$ (CLT) and $S_n/\\sigma\\xrightarrow{P}1$ (LLN), so by Slutsky $T_n=\\frac{\\sqrt n(\\bar X_n-\\mu)}{S_n}\\xrightarrow{d}\\mathcal N(0,1)$ (Grimmett 5.10).",
    "hint": "If you do not know the spread of the lap-time gap between Max and Checo and use the sample spread, does the bell shape survive?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\sqrt n(\\bar X_n-\\mu)/\\sigma\\xrightarrow{d}\\mathcal N(0,1)$ = the numerator.</strong> The standardised average lap-time gap over $n$ laps tends to a standard bell (CLT).",
      "<strong>$S_n/\\sigma\\xrightarrow{P}1$ = the denominator.</strong> The sample spread settles to the true spread (law of large numbers).",
      "<strong>$\\mathcal N(0,1)/1$ = Slutsky.</strong> Dividing a bell-shaped limit by a quantity tending to 1 leaves the bell unchanged: the $t$-statistic is asymptotically standard normal."
    ],
