    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31704\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"112\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31704)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31704)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">lap n</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">|X\u2099|</text><path d=\"M24.0,112.0 L34.1,107.5 L44.2,102.9 L54.3,98.4 L64.4,93.8 L74.5,89.3 L84.6,84.7 L94.7,80.2 L104.8,75.6 L114.9,71.1 L125.0,66.5 L135.1,62.0 L145.2,57.5 L155.3,52.9 L165.4,48.4 L175.5,43.8 L185.6,39.3 L195.7,34.7 L205.8,30.2 L215.9,25.6 L226.0,21.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">cap at n</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"92\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"92\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"98\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"54\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"54\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"88\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"88\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"22\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"190\" cy=\"82\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"94\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"94\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y\u2099 = X\u2099 1{|X\u2099| \u2264 n}: clip the laps that exceed the cap</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2211 \u2119(X\u2099 \u2260 Y\u2099) \u2264 \ud835\udd3c|X| &lt; \u221e: only finitely many laps are clipped</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Each lap's |X\u2099| and the growing cap n. Laps above the cap are clipped (open dots): Y\u2099 = X\u20991{|X\u2099| \u2264 n}. Only finitely many laps are clipped since \u2211\u2119(X\u2099 \u2260 Y\u2099) \u2264 \ud835\udd3c|X|.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Sharpest Condition:</strong> For i.i.d. $X_i$, $\\bar{X}_n \\xrightarrow{a.s.} \\mu$ IF AND ONLY IF $\\mathbb{E}[|X|] \\lt  \\infty$. Finite variance is NOT required!",
      "<strong>Truncation Idea:</strong> Define $Y_n = X_n \\mathbf{1}_{\\{|X_n| \\le n\\}}$. The tails satisfy $\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(X_n \\ne Y_n) = \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(|X| > n) \\le \\mathbb{E}[|X|] \\lt  \\infty$.",
      "<strong>Equivalence via BC1:</strong> By BC1, $X_n = Y_n$ for all but finitely many $n$ almost surely! Thus $\\bar{X}_n$ and $\\bar{Y}_n$ have identical asymptotic limits."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\bar{X}_n \\xrightarrow{\\text{a.s.}} \\mu \\iff \\mathbb{E}[|X|] \\lt  \\infty, \\qquad Y_n = X_n\\,\\mathbf{1}_{\\{|X_n| \\le n\\}} \\implies \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\mathbb{P}(X_n \\ne Y_n) \\le \\mathbb{E}[|X|] \\lt  \\infty$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Ignore the freak laps.</strong> Cap the time lost on each lap (a spin, a red flag) at a level that grows slowly with the lap number. Only finitely many laps ever exceed their cap, so capping does not change where the running average ends up.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming variance is required for SLLN. Kolmogorov proved that \ud835\udd3c[|X|] < \u221e alone suffices; distributions with infinite variance (e.g. Pareto with 1 < \u03b1 \u2264 2) still satisfy SLLN!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Kolmogorov's SLLN and truncation.</b> $\\bar X_n\\to\\mu$ a.s. iff $\\mathbb E|X|\\lt \\infty$. Sketch: put $Y_n=X_n\\mathbf 1_{\\{|X_n|\\le n\\}}$. Then $\\sum_n\\mathbb P(X_n\\ne Y_n)=\\sum_n\\mathbb P(|X|\\gt n)\\le\\mathbb E|X|\\lt \\infty$, so $X_n=Y_n$ eventually (Borel\u2013Cantelli), and the truncated variables have bounded variance sums (Grimmett 7.5; Durrett 2.4).",
    "hint": "How do you tame an unbounded lap by clipping it, and why do only finitely many laps get clipped?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$Y_n=X_n\\mathbf 1_{\\{|X_n|\\le n\\}}$ = clip the big laps.</strong> Replace a lap by 0 if it exceeds a cap that grows with $n$.",
      "<strong>$\\sum\\mathbb P(X_n\\ne Y_n)\\le\\mathbb E|X|$ = few laps are clipped.</strong> The chances $\\mathbb P(|X|\\gt n)$ sum to at most $\\mathbb E|X|$, which is finite.",
      "<strong>Borel\u2013Cantelli = finitely many clipped laps.</strong> After some lap $X_n=Y_n$, so the clipped and original averages have the same limit."
    ],
