    "title": "L\u00e9vy\u2019s Continuity Theorem: Pointwise Fourier Convergence",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31802\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31802)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31802)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">t</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c6\u2099(t)</text><path d=\"M30.0,92.3 L33.2,91.0 L36.3,89.7 L39.5,88.2 L42.7,86.5 L45.8,84.7 L49.0,82.8 L52.2,80.6 L55.3,78.4 L58.5,76.0 L61.7,73.4 L64.8,70.7 L68.0,68.0 L71.2,65.1 L74.3,62.1 L77.5,59.2 L80.7,56.2 L83.8,53.2 L87.0,50.2 L90.2,47.4 L93.3,44.6 L96.5,42.0 L99.7,39.6 L102.8,37.4 L106.0,35.4 L109.2,33.7 L112.3,32.3 L115.5,31.2 L118.7,30.5 L121.8,30.1 L125.0,30.0 L128.2,30.3 L131.3,30.9 L134.5,31.9 L137.7,33.2 L140.8,34.8 L144.0,36.6 L147.2,38.8 L150.3,41.1 L153.5,43.6 L156.7,46.3 L159.8,49.2 L163.0,52.1 L166.2,55.1 L169.3,58.0 L172.5,61.0 L175.7,64.0 L178.8,66.9 L182.0,69.7 L185.2,72.4 L188.3,75.0 L191.5,77.5 L194.7,79.8 L197.8,82.0 L201.0,84.0 L204.2,85.9 L207.3,87.6 L210.5,89.1 L213.7,90.6 L216.8,91.8 L220.0,93.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 3\"/><path d=\"M30.0,98.6 L33.2,98.2 L36.3,97.7 L39.5,97.0 L42.7,96.3 L45.8,95.3 L49.0,94.2 L52.2,92.9 L55.3,91.3 L58.5,89.5 L61.7,87.5 L64.8,85.1 L68.0,82.5 L71.2,79.7 L74.3,76.5 L77.5,73.1 L80.7,69.5 L83.8,65.7 L87.0,61.8 L90.2,57.8 L93.3,53.8 L96.5,49.9 L99.7,46.1 L102.8,42.6 L106.0,39.4 L109.2,36.5 L112.3,34.1 L115.5,32.2 L118.7,30.9 L121.8,30.1 L125.0,30.0 L128.2,30.5 L131.3,31.6 L134.5,33.3 L137.7,35.6 L140.8,38.3 L144.0,41.4 L147.2,44.8 L150.3,48.5 L153.5,52.4 L156.7,56.4 L159.8,60.4 L163.0,64.3 L166.2,68.2 L169.3,71.8 L172.5,75.3 L175.7,78.5 L178.8,81.5 L182.0,84.2 L185.2,86.7 L188.3,88.8 L191.5,90.7 L194.7,92.3 L197.8,93.7 L201.0,94.9 L204.2,95.9 L207.3,96.8 L210.5,97.5 L213.7,98.0 L216.8,98.5 L220.0,98.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M30.0,99.8 L33.2,99.6 L36.3,99.5 L39.5,99.3 L42.7,99.0 L45.8,98.6 L49.0,98.1 L52.2,97.4 L55.3,96.5 L58.5,95.5 L61.7,94.1 L64.8,92.5 L68.0,90.5 L71.2,88.2 L74.3,85.5 L77.5,82.4 L80.7,78.9 L83.8,75.0 L87.0,70.8 L90.2,66.3 L93.3,61.6 L96.5,56.8 L99.7,52.0 L102.8,47.4 L106.0,43.1 L109.2,39.2 L112.3,35.8 L115.5,33.2 L118.7,31.3 L121.8,30.2 L125.0,30.0 L128.2,30.8 L131.3,32.4 L134.5,34.8 L137.7,37.9 L140.8,41.6 L144.0,45.8 L147.2,50.3 L150.3,55.0 L153.5,59.8 L156.7,64.6 L159.8,69.1 L163.0,73.5 L166.2,77.5 L169.3,81.1 L172.5,84.4 L175.7,87.2 L178.8,89.7 L182.0,91.8 L185.2,93.6 L188.3,95.0 L191.5,96.2 L194.7,97.1 L197.8,97.8 L201.0,98.4 L204.2,98.8 L207.3,99.2 L210.5,99.4 L213.7,99.6 L216.8,99.7 L220.0,99.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"124\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><text x=\"224\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c6\u2099 \u2192 \u03c6 at every t</text><text x=\"224\" y=\"47\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u21d4 X\u2099 \u2192 X in law</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">n small</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">L\u00e9vy: pointwise convergence of the Fourier transforms</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">is the same as convergence of the laws</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Characteristic functions \u03c6\u2099(t) for increasing n converging pointwise to \u03c6(t). Pointwise convergence of \u03c6\u2099 at every t is equivalent to X\u2099 \u2192 X in distribution.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Equivalence Statement:</strong> $X_n \\xrightarrow{d} X \\iff \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\varphi_{X_n}(t) = \\varphi_X(t)$ for all $t \\in \\mathbb{R}$.",
      "<strong>Continuity at Origin:</strong> If $\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\varphi_{X_n}(t) = g(t)$ pointwise, and $g(t)$ is continuous at $t = 0$, then $g(t)$ is the characteristic function of a valid random variable $X$, and $X_n \\xrightarrow{d} X$.",
      "<strong>Mass Escape Warning:</strong> If $g(t)$ is discontinuous at $t=0$, probability mass escapes to $\\pm\\infty$ (tightness fails) and no limiting random variable exists."
    ],
    "math": "$$X_n \\xrightarrow{d} X \\iff \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\varphi_{X_n}(t) = \\varphi_X(t) \\quad \\forall t \\in \\mathbb{R}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Judging the shape by its fingerprint.</strong> Instead of watching the histogram of Max's total race time change with the number of laps $n$, you watch its transform at each frequency; when every frequency has settled, the shape has settled.",
    "examTrap": "Ignoring continuity at t = 0! For Uniform(-n, n), \u03c6(t) = sin(nt)/(nt) \u2192 0 for t \u2260 0 and 1 at t = 0. The limit is discontinuous at 0, signaling mass escape to infinity.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>L\u00e9vy's continuity theorem.</b> $X_n\\xrightarrow{d}X$ if and only if $\\varphi_{X_n}(t)\\to\\varphi_X(t)$ for every $t\\in\\mathbb R$. More generally, if $\\varphi_{X_n}(t)\\to\\varphi(t)$ pointwise and $\\varphi$ is continuous at $0$, then $\\varphi$ is the characteristic function of some $X$ and $X_n\\xrightarrow{d}X$ (Grimmett 5.9; Durrett 3.3).",
    "hint": "How can you check that a sequence of laws settles by looking at their transforms only?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\varphi_{X_n}(t)$ = the transform of the $n$-th law.</strong> One function of $t$ for each $n$.",
      "<strong>$\\lim\\varphi_{X_n}(t)=\\varphi_X(t)$ for every $t$ = pointwise convergence.</strong> At each fixed frequency $t$, the values settle on those of the limit.",
      "<strong>$\\iff X_n\\xrightarrow{d}X$ = it is the same statement.</strong> Convergence of the transforms is equivalent to convergence of the laws, and continuity at 0 guarantees a limit law exists."
    ],
