    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "The Lindeberg-L\u00e9vy Central Limit Theorem",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31803\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31803)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-31803)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">z\u2099: standardised race time</text><rect x=\"52\" y=\"102.38177075777838\" width=\"12\" height=\"5.618229242221624\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"66\" y=\"98.51875376055958\" width=\"12\" height=\"9.48124623944043\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"80\" y=\"89.9681114777453\" width=\"12\" height=\"18.0318885222547\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"94\" y=\"76.85120964995775\" width=\"12\" height=\"31.14879035004224\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"108\" y=\"64.30074224935265\" width=\"12\" height=\"43.699257750647355\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"122\" y=\"60.1255348647953\" width=\"12\" height=\"47.8744651352047\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"136\" y=\"67.35296623096107\" width=\"12\" height=\"40.64703376903892\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"80.86532692526569\" width=\"12\" height=\"27.13467307473431\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"164\" y=\"92.96212554501446\" width=\"12\" height=\"15.037874454985536\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><rect x=\"178\" y=\"100.01979832126655\" width=\"12\" height=\"7.980201678733457\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><path d=\"M40.0,107.3 L42.7,107.0 L45.3,106.7 L48.0,106.3 L50.7,105.8 L53.3,105.2 L56.0,104.4 L58.7,103.5 L61.3,102.3 L64.0,101.0 L66.7,99.5 L69.3,97.7 L72.0,95.6 L74.7,93.4 L77.3,90.8 L80.0,88.0 L82.7,85.0 L85.3,81.9 L88.0,78.6 L90.7,75.2 L93.3,71.7 L96.0,68.4 L98.7,65.1 L101.3,62.1 L104.0,59.3 L106.7,56.9 L109.3,54.9 L112.0,53.4 L114.7,52.4 L117.3,52.0 L120.0,52.2 L122.7,52.9 L125.3,54.1 L128.0,55.9 L130.7,58.1 L133.3,60.7 L136.0,63.6 L138.7,66.7 L141.3,70.0 L144.0,73.4 L146.7,76.9 L149.3,80.2 L152.0,83.5 L154.7,86.6 L157.3,89.5 L160.0,92.1 L162.7,94.5 L165.3,96.7 L168.0,98.6 L170.7,100.3 L173.3,101.7 L176.0,102.9 L178.7,104.0 L181.3,104.8 L184.0,105.5 L186.7,106.1 L189.3,106.5 L192.0,106.9 L194.7,107.2 L197.3,107.4 L200.0,107.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Z\u2099 = (\u2211X\u1d62 \u2212 n\u03bc)/(\u03c3\u221an) \u2192 \ud835\udca9(0,1)</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c6(Z\u2099)(t) = (1 \u2212 t\u00b2/2n + o(t\u00b2/n))\u207f \u2192 e^(\u2212t\u00b2/2)</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">any lap-law,</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">same bell</text><text x=\"115.88\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the total of many laps is bell-shaped, whatever one lap looks like</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Histogram of the standardised race time Z\u2099 and the standard bell \ud835\udca9(0,1). The transform (1 \u2212 t\u00b2/2n + o(t\u00b2/n))\u207f tends to e^(\u2212t\u00b2/2), which proves it.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Theorem Statement:</strong> Let $X_1, X_2, \\dots$ be i.i.d. with mean $\\mu$ and finite variance $\\sigma^2 > 0$. Then $Z_n = \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i - n\\mu}{\\sigma \\sqrt{n}} \\xrightarrow{d} \\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$.",
      "<strong>Characteristic Function Proof:</strong> Taylor expansion: $\\varphi_{\\frac{X-\\mu}{\\sigma}}(u) = 1 - \\frac{u^2}{2} + o(u^2)$. Standardized sum has CF $\\varphi_{Z_n}(t) = \\left[1 - \\frac{t^2}{2n} + o(t^2/n)\\right]^n \\to e^{-t^2/2}$ (the exact CF of $\\mathcal{N}(0, 1)$).",
      "<strong>Universal Invariance:</strong> Holds regardless of the underlying distribution's shape (bimodal, uniform, exponential, discrete) as long as variance $\\sigma^2 \\lt  \\infty$."
    ],
    "math": "$$Z_n = \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^n X_i - n\\mu}{\\sigma \\sqrt{n}} \\xrightarrow{d} \\mathcal{N}(0, 1), \\qquad \\varphi_{Z_n}(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t^2}{2n} + o\\left(\\frac{t^2}{n}\\right)\\right)^n \\to e^{-t^2/2}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A whole race is a bell.</strong> Whatever shape one lap time has (a few slow laps in traffic make it lopsided), Max's total time over 57 laps, measured in standard units, has a bell-shaped histogram. Only the average and the spread of one lap matter.",
    "examTrap": "Applying CLT to unscaled sums S_n or raw means X\u0304_n! S_n variance explodes to \u221e; X\u0304_n variance collapses to 0. CLT applies ONLY to the \u221an-standardized deviation.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Central limit theorem (Lindeberg\u2013L\u00e9vy).</b> Let $X_1,X_2,\\ldots$ be i.i.d. with mean $\\mu$ and variance $\\sigma^2\\in(0,\\infty)$. Then $Z_n=\\dfrac{\\sum_{i=1}^nX_i-n\\mu}{\\sigma\\sqrt n}\\xrightarrow{d}\\mathcal N(0,1)$. Proof: $\\varphi_{Z_n}(t)=\\bigl(1-\\frac{t^2}{2n}+o(\\frac{t^2}n)\\bigr)^n\\to e^{-t^2/2}$, then L\u00e9vy (Ross 8.3; Grimmett 5.10).",
    "hint": "Why does the total of many independent laps look like a bell, whatever one lap looks like?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\sum X_i-n\\mu$ = the total, centred.</strong> Subtract the expected race time, so the leftover has mean 0.",
      "<strong>$\\div\\,\\sigma\\sqrt n$ = rescale by the spread.</strong> The total has standard deviation $\\sigma\\sqrt n$; dividing by it gives a variable with variance 1.",
      "<strong>$\\bigl(1-\\frac{t^2}{2n}+o\\bigr)^n\\to e^{-t^2/2}$ = the transform of a bell.</strong> Only the mean and variance survive the $n$-th power; the limit is the standard normal's transform."
    ],
