    "title": "State Periodicity & Class Sharing Properties",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-31905\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"66.0\" r=\"34.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"32.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"94.0\" cy=\"66.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"26.0\" cy=\"66.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">2</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">3</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">cycle of length 4: d = 4</text><text x=\"226\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">d(i) = gcd{n : P\u1d62\u1d62\u207d\u207f\u207e > 0}</text><text x=\"226\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">returns possible at</text><text x=\"226\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">n = 4, 8, 12, \u2026</text><text x=\"226\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">i \u2194 j \u21d2 d(i) = d(j)</text><text x=\"226\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">and both recurrent or</text><text x=\"226\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">both transient</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A four-state cycle, like four set-ups used in strict turn: from state 0 you can be back only after 4, 8, 12, \u2026 races, so the period is 4. Every state of the class has the same period.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Period Definition:</strong> Period of state $i$ is $d(i) \\triangleq \\gcd\\{n \\ge 1 : P_{ii}^{(n)} > 0\\}$. If $d(i) = 1$, the state is **aperiodic**.",
      "<strong>Class Invariance Theorem:</strong> Recurrence, transience, and periodicity are **CLASS PROPERTIES**: if $i \\leftrightarrow j$, then $d(i) = d(j)$, and $i$ is recurrent $\\iff j$ is recurrent.",
      "<strong>Self-Loop Shortcut:</strong> If state $i$ has a self-loop ($P_{ii} > 0$), then $1 \\in \\{n : P_{ii}^{(n)} > 0\\}$, so $d(i) = \\gcd(1, \\dots) = 1$ (instantly aperiodic!)."
    ],
    "math": "$$d(i) \\triangleq \\gcd\\{n \\ge 1 : P_{ii}^{(n)} > 0\\}; \\qquad i \\leftrightarrow j \\implies d(i) = d(j) \\text{ and } (i \\text{ rec} \\iff j \\text{ rec})$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A strict four-race rotation.</strong> Say Red Bull rotates Max's car through four set-ups in a fixed order, one per race. Set-up 0 can only come back every 4th race, and so can every other set-up in the loop. Any shortcut of another length would break the rhythm.",
    "examTrap": "Defining period as the minimum return time! Period is the GREATEST COMMON DIVISOR of all return times, not the length of the shortest loop.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Period and class properties.</b> The period of $i$ is $d(i)=\\gcd\\{n\\ge1:P^{(n)}_{ii}\\gt 0\\}$; $i$ is aperiodic if $d(i)=1$. If $i\\leftrightarrow j$ then $d(i)=d(j)$, and $i$ is recurrent iff $j$ is recurrent: period, recurrence and transience are class properties (Ross 4.3; Grimmett 6.2).",
    "hint": "If a state can only come back every fourth race, what does that say about the rest of its class?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\{n\\ge1:P^{(n)}_{ii}\\gt 0\\}$ = possible return times.</strong> The numbers of races after which you can be back at $i$.",
      "<strong>$d(i)=\\gcd$ = the period.</strong> The greatest common divisor of those times: returns can only happen at multiples of $d(i)$.",
      "<strong>$i\\leftrightarrow j\\Rightarrow d(i)=d(j)$ = shared by the class.</strong> Period, recurrence and transience are the same for all states in a communicating class."
    ],
