    "cardNumber": "01",
    "category": "INVARIANT MEASURES",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "Stationary Distribution \u03c0 & Invariant Probability Measure",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32001\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32001)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32001)\"/><rect x=\"50\" y=\"60.0\" width=\"18\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"80.0\" width=\"18\" height=\"20.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"59\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">W</text><text x=\"83\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">N</text><text x=\"59\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0(W)</text><text x=\"83\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0(N)</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">one more race:</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u1d40P = \u03c0\u1d40</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">nothing changes</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the long-run shares of wins and non-wins</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u2c7c = \u2211\u1d62 \u03c0\u1d62 P\u1d62\u2c7c,   \u2211\u1d62 \u03c0\u1d62 = 1</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">W: 0.8\u00b7\u2154 + 0.4\u00b7\u2153 = \u2154</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The stationary split (\u03c0 win = \u2154, \u03c0 no win = \u2153) as bars. One more race leaves the split unchanged, since \u03c0\u1d40P = \u03c0\u1d40.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Invariant Probability Measure:</strong> A row probability vector $\\pi = (\\pi_i)_{i \\in S}$ is stationary if $\\pi^\\top P = \\pi^\\top$ with $\\pi_i \\ge 0$ and $\\sum_{i \\in S} \\pi_i = 1$. If initial state $X_0 \\sim \\pi$, then $X_n \\sim \\pi$ for all steps $n \\ge 1$ identically.",
      "<strong>Component-wise Inflow Balance:</strong> Expanding $\\pi^\\top P = \\pi^\\top$ yields $\\pi_j = \\sum_{i \\in S} \\pi_i P_{ij}$ for all states $j \\in S$. The stationary probability mass at state $j$ equals the aggregate probability flux entering $j$ from all predecessor states $i$ weighted by steady-state occupancies.",
      "<strong>Left Eigenvector Formulation:</strong> Mathematically, $\\pi^\\top$ is a normalized left eigenvector of transition matrix $P$ corresponding to the dominant Perron-Frobenius eigenvalue $\\lambda_1 = 1$, ensuring non-negativity and existence for finite stochastic matrices."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\pi^\\top P = \\pi^\\top, \\quad \\sum_{i \\in S} \\pi_i = 1, \\quad \\pi_j = \\sum_{i \\in S} \\pi_i P_{ij} \\quad \\forall j \\in S$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Max's steady win rate.</strong> Say after a win he wins again with chance $0.8$, and after a non-win he wins with chance $0.4$. Then a split of $\\frac23$ wins and $\\frac13$ non-wins reproduces itself: $0.8\\cdot\\frac23+0.4\\cdot\\frac13=\\frac23$.",
    "examTrap": "Confusing left vs right eigenvectors! \u03c0^T P = \u03c0^T is a *left* eigenvector equation. The trivial *right* eigenvector with eigenvalue 1 is the vector of all ones P 1 = 1, which represents row-stochasticity, not the stationary distribution!",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Stationary distribution.</b> A probability vector $\\pi$ on $S$ is stationary for $P$ if $\\pi^{\\top}P=\\pi^{\\top}$, i.e. $\\pi_j=\\sum_{i\\in S}\\pi_iP_{ij}$ for all $j$, with $\\pi_i\\ge0$ and $\\sum_i\\pi_i=1$. If $X_0\\sim\\pi$ then $X_n\\sim\\pi$ for every $n$ (Ross 4.4; Grimmett 6.4).",
    "hint": "Which split of wins and non-wins stays exactly the same from one race to the next?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\pi_j=\\sum_i\\pi_iP_{ij}$ = inflow equals share.</strong> The weight of $j$ next race is what flows in from every $i$, weighted by this race's share $\\pi_i$.",
      "<strong>$\\sum_i\\pi_i=1$ = a genuine split.</strong> The shares are probabilities, so they add to one.",
      "<strong>$\\pi^{\\top}P=\\pi^{\\top}$ = left eigenvector for 1.</strong> Start from $\\pi$ and one step of the chain gives back $\\pi$: the law is frozen."
    ],
    "textbookImg": null,
