    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32103\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"40\" y=\"24\" width=\"110\" height=\"70\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"59\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"59\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><line x1=\"95\" y1=\"24\" x2=\"95\" y2=\"94\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"67\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Q</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">R</text><text x=\"67\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"9\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">I</text><text x=\"67\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">transient</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">absorbing</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Q: transient \u2192</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">transient</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">R: transient \u2192</text><text x=\"188\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">absorbing</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">N = \u2211\u2096 Q\u1d4f = (I \u2212 Q)\u207b\u00b9</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">N\u1d62\u2c7c = expected visits to j starting from i</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Canonical form of an absorbing chain: block Q for moves between gap states, exits R, and the identity I for the ends. The fundamental matrix N = (I \u2212 Q)\u207b\u00b9 gives the expected visits N\u1d62\u2c7c.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Canonical Partitioning:</strong> Reordering states into $t$ transient states followed by $r$ absorbing states formats transition matrix $P$ as $P = \\begin{pmatrix} Q & R \\\\ 0 & I_r \\end{pmatrix}$, where $Q$ governs internal transient jumps and $R$ governs transitions into absorbing sinks.",
      "<strong>Fundamental Matrix Definition:</strong> Because transient states are eventually abandoned ($Q^n \\to 0$ as $n \\to \\infty$), the matrix Neumann series converges: $N = \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty Q^k = (I - Q)^{-1}$, termed the Fundamental Matrix of the absorbing chain.",
      "<strong>Occupancy Counting Meaning:</strong> Entry $N_{ij}$ equals the exact expected number of visits to transient state $j$ prior to absorption, given the process initialized in transient state $i$: $N_{ij} = \\mathbb{E}\\left[\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty \\mathbf{1}_{\\{X_n = j\\}} \\,\\middle|\\, X_0 = i\\right]$."
    ],
    "math": "$$P = \\begin{pmatrix} Q & R \\\\ 0 & I \\end{pmatrix} \\implies N = \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty Q^k = (I - Q)^{-1}, \\quad N_{ij} = \\mathbb{E}[\\text{Visits to } j \\mid X_0 = i]$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A lap counter for each gap.</strong> Entry $N_{ij}$ tells you how many laps, on average, Max spends at gap $j$ before the chase ends, if it starts at gap $i$.",
    "examTrap": "Forgetting that N_ii \u2265 1 always! When starting in state i, step n=0 counts as a visit to state i (1_{X_0=i} = 1), so the diagonal entries of N are always at least 1, even if Q_ii = 0.",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Canonical form and fundamental matrix.</b> Order the states with the transient ones first: $P=\\begin{pmatrix}Q&R\\\\0&I\\end{pmatrix}$. Then $P^n=\\begin{pmatrix}Q^n&\\ast\\\\0&I\\end{pmatrix}$, $Q^n\\to0$, and $N=\\sum_{k\\ge0}Q^k=(I-Q)^{-1}$, where $N_{ij}=\\mathbb E_i[\\text{number of visits to }j\\text{ before absorption}]$ (Grimmett 6.3; Kemeny\u2013Snell).",
    "hint": "How can the whole chase be packed into one matrix that counts visits to each gap?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$Q$ and $R$ = stay or leave.</strong> $Q$ holds the moves between gap states and $R$ the moves from a gap state into an absorbing end.",
      "<strong>$N=\\sum_kQ^k$ = add up visits step by step.</strong> $(Q^k)_{ij}$ is the chance to be at $j$ after $k$ steps, so the sum is the expected number of visits.",
      "<strong>$N=(I-Q)^{-1}$ = the geometric series.</strong> It converges because $Q^n\\to0$: the chase ends for sure."
    ],
