    "cardNumber": "05",
    "category": "GAMBLER'S RUIN",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "Gambler\u2019s Ruin: Difference Equations & Drift Regimes",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32105\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32105)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32105)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">start i</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">a\u1d62</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"56\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">p = \u00bd : a\u1d62 = i/N</text><path d=\"M24.0,108.0 L29.1,100.2 L34.1,93.1 L39.1,86.7 L44.2,80.9 L49.2,75.7 L54.3,71.0 L59.4,66.7 L64.4,62.9 L69.5,59.4 L74.5,56.2 L79.5,53.4 L84.6,50.8 L89.7,48.5 L94.7,46.4 L99.8,44.5 L104.8,42.7 L109.8,41.2 L114.9,39.8 L120.0,38.5 L125.0,37.4 L130.1,36.3 L135.1,35.4 L140.2,34.5 L145.2,33.8 L150.2,33.1 L155.3,32.5 L160.3,31.9 L165.4,31.4 L170.4,30.9 L175.5,30.5 L180.6,30.1 L185.6,29.8 L190.7,29.5 L195.7,29.2 L200.8,28.9 L205.8,28.7 L210.8,28.5 L215.9,28.3 L220.9,28.2 L226.0,28.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">p > \u00bd : bends up</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">gambler's ruin on {0, \u2026, N}</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc\u1d62 = i(N \u2212 i) expected rounds when p = \u00bd</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Chance of hitting N before 0 against the start i. Equal cars give the straight line i/N; a faster car (p > \u00bd) bends the curve up. The expected length is i(N \u2212 i) laps for p = \u00bd.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Difference Equation Formulation:</strong> Let $a_i$ be the probability of ruin starting with $\\$i$. First-step conditioning gives $a_i = p a_{i+1} + q a_{i-1}$ with boundary conditions $a_0 = 1$ and $a_N = 0$. The characteristic ratio is $\\rho = q/p$.",
      "<strong>Closed-Form Ruin Probability:</strong> Solving the homogeneous difference equation yields $a_i = \\frac{\\rho^i - \\rho^N}{1 - \\rho^N}$ when $p \\ne q$. In a fair game ($p = q = 1/2$, $\\rho = 1$), L'H\u00f4pital's limit yields the linear ruin probability $a_i = 1 - \\frac{i}{N}$.",
      "<strong>Expected Game Duration:</strong> The mean time until the game ends is $\\mu_i = \\frac{i}{q - p} - \\frac{N}{q - p} \\left(\\frac{1 - \\rho^i}{1 - \\rho^N}\\right)$ for $p \\ne q$, simplifying to parabolic duration $\\mu_i = i(N - i)$ for a fair coin ($p = 1/2$)."
    ],
    "math": "$$a_i = \\begin{cases} \\frac{(q/p)^i - (q/p)^N}{1 - (q/p)^N} & p \\ne q \\\\ 1 - \\frac{i}{N} & p = q = \\frac{1}{2} \\end{cases}; \\quad \\mu_i = i(N - i) \\quad (\\text{if } p = 1/2)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The faster car.</strong> In the chase with $N$ steps, if Max gains or loses a step on each lap with equal chance, his chance of getting past is just how far along he already is. If his car is faster ($p\\gt \\frac12$), the line bends upwards: even from far back he usually gets there.",
    "examTrap": "Using the biased formula when p = 1/2! Substituting p = q = 1/2 into (\u03c1^i - \u03c1^N)/(1 - \u03c1^N) gives indeterminate 0/0. For p = 1/2, the solution is linear a_i = 1 - i/N, not exponential!",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Gambler's ruin.</b> Win each round with prob. $p$, lose with $q=1-p$, start at $i$, stop at $0$ or $N$. Then $a_i=\\mathbb P_i(\\text{reach }N)=\\dfrac{(q/p)^i-1}{(q/p)^N-1}$ for $p\\ne q$ (equivalently $\\frac{1-(q/p)^i}{1-(q/p)^N}$ for reaching $0$ with the roles swapped), and $a_i=i/N$ for $p=q=\\frac12$, where $\\mu_i=i(N-i)$ (Ross 4.5; Grimmett 3.9).",
    "hint": "With a fair or a biased step each lap, how likely is Max to reach the far end before the near one?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$p=q=\\frac12$: $a_i=i/N$ = linear.</strong> The chance of reaching $N$ before $0$ is the fraction of the way he already is.",
      "<strong>$p\\ne q$: $\\frac{(q/p)^i-1}{(q/p)^N-1}$ = bends with the drift.</strong> A drift towards $N$ makes the chance rise faster than linear.",
      "<strong>$\\mu_i=i(N-i)$ = expected rounds when $p=\\frac12$.</strong> Longest in the middle, and zero at both ends."
    ],
