    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "Birth-Death Chains & Detailed Balance Equations",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32201\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"50.0\" r=\"10.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">0</text><circle cx=\"72.0\" cy=\"50.0\" r=\"10.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"72\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">1</text><circle cx=\"114.0\" cy=\"50.0\" r=\"10.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">2</text><circle cx=\"156.0\" cy=\"50.0\" r=\"10.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"156\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">3</text><circle cx=\"198.0\" cy=\"50.0\" r=\"10.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"198\" y=\"53\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2026</text><line x1=\"41.0\" y1=\"47.0\" x2=\"61.0\" y2=\"47.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32201)\"/><line x1=\"61.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"41.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32201)\"/><line x1=\"83.0\" y1=\"47.0\" x2=\"103.0\" y2=\"47.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32201)\"/><line x1=\"103.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"83.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32201)\"/><line x1=\"125.0\" y1=\"47.0\" x2=\"145.0\" y2=\"47.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32201)\"/><line x1=\"145.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"125.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32201)\"/><line x1=\"167.0\" y1=\"47.0\" x2=\"187.0\" y2=\"47.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32201)\"/><line x1=\"187.0\" y1=\"53.0\" x2=\"167.0\" y2=\"53.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32201)\"/><text x=\"72\" y=\"35\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">p\u1d62</text><text x=\"72\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">q\u1d62\u208a\u2081</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">places behind the leader: i</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">drop a place: p\u1d62    gain a place: q\u1d62</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">cut between i and i+1: \u03c0\u1d62 p\u1d62 = \u03c0\u1d62\u208a\u2081 q\u1d62\u208a\u2081</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u1d62\u208a\u2081 = (p\u1d62 / q\u1d62\u208a\u2081) \u03c0\u1d62</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Places behind the leader as a ladder 0, 1, 2, \u2026. In steady state the flow back across each rung equals the flow forward: \u03c0\u1d62p\u1d62 = \u03c0\u1d62\u208a\u2081q\u1d62\u208a\u2081.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Tridiagonal Transition Structure:</strong> A discrete-time birth-death chain on $\\{0, 1, 2, \\dots\\}$ only permits transitions to adjacent neighbors: $P_{i, i+1} = p_i$, $P_{i, i-1} = q_i$, and $P_{i, i} = r_i = 1 - p_i - q_i$. Boundary state 0 satisfies $q_0 = 0$.",
      "<strong>Cut Equivalence to Detailed Balance:</strong> Taking the cut between $\\{0, 1, \\dots, i\\}$ and $\\{i+1, \\dots\\}$, the only crossing transitions are the birth $i \\to i+1$ and the death $i+1 \\to i$. Flux conservation directly yields pairwise detailed balance: $\\pi_i p_i = \\pi_{i+1} q_{i+1}$.",
      "<strong>Recursive Ratio:</strong> Rearranging gives $\\pi_{i+1} = \\left(\\frac{p_i}{q_{i+1}}\\right) \\pi_i$, transforming the matrix inversion problem $(I - P^\\top)\\pi = 0$ into a simple 1D recursive product."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\pi_i p_i = \\pi_{i+1} q_{i+1} \\implies \\pi_{i+1} = \\left(\\frac{p_i}{q_{i+1}}\\right) \\pi_i \\quad \\forall i \\ge 0$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A ladder of championship places.</strong> Count how many places Max is behind the leader: 0 means he leads. If gaining a place is likelier than dropping one, being far back is rare; the ratio of neighbouring shares is exactly the drop/gain ratio.",
    "examTrap": "Applying birth-death formulas to chains with skip transitions! If transitions like i \u2192 i+2 or resets to 0 occur, the chain is no longer tridiagonal and simple detailed balance \u03c0_i p_i = \u03c0_{i+1} q_{i+1} breaks!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Birth\u2013death chains.</b> A chain on $\\{0,1,2,\\ldots\\}$ moves only $i\\to i\\pm1$, with $P_{i,i+1}=p_i$ and $P_{i,i-1}=q_i$. A stationary $\\pi$ satisfies the detailed balance (cut) equations $\\pi_ip_i=\\pi_{i+1}q_{i+1}$, so $\\pi_{i+1}=\\frac{p_i}{q_{i+1}}\\pi_i$ for all $i\\ge0$ (Ross 4.8; Grimmett 6.5).",
    "hint": "If Max's championship place only moves one at a time, how do the steady shares of neighbouring places compare?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$P_{i,i+1}=p_i,\\ P_{i,i-1}=q_i$ = one step up or down.</strong> After a race he drops one place or gains one; nothing jumps further.",
      "<strong>$\\pi_ip_i=\\pi_{i+1}q_{i+1}$ = balance across a cut.</strong> The flow from $i$ back to $i+1$ equals the flow from $i+1$ forward to $i$.",
      "<strong>$\\pi_{i+1}=\\frac{p_i}{q_{i+1}}\\pi_i$ = a recursion.</strong> Each share is the one before times (chance to drop over chance to gain)."
    ],
