    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32202\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32202)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32202)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">n places back</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u2099</text><rect x=\"34\" y=\"34.0\" width=\"14\" height=\"66.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"54\" y=\"52.480000000000004\" width=\"14\" height=\"47.519999999999996\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"65.7856\" width=\"14\" height=\"34.2144\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"94\" y=\"75.365632\" width=\"14\" height=\"24.634368\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"114\" y=\"82.26325504\" width=\"14\" height=\"17.736744959999996\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"134\" y=\"87.2295436288\" width=\"14\" height=\"12.770456371199998\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"154\" y=\"90.805271412736\" width=\"14\" height=\"9.194728587263997\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"174\" y=\"93.37979541716992\" width=\"14\" height=\"6.620204582830078\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"194\" y=\"95.23345270036235\" width=\"14\" height=\"4.766547299637656\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u2099 = \u03c0\u2080 \u220f p\u2096 / q\u2096\u208a\u2081</text><text x=\"126.8\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">normalise: \u03c0\u2080 = (1 + \u2211\u2099 \u220f \u2026)\u207b\u00b9</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a steady law exists iff the sum is finite (ratios</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">p\u2096/q\u2096\u208a\u2081 &lt; 1 eventually: places gained beat places lost)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Steady shares \u03c0\u2099 of being n places behind the leader, falling geometrically when gaining beats dropping (ratio < 1). They add to one only if \u2211 \u220f p\u2096/q\u2096\u208a\u2081 is finite.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Product Form Invariant Measure:</strong> Iterating the detailed balance ratio yields $\\pi_n = \\pi_0 \\prod_{k=0}^{n-1} \\frac{p_k}{q_{k+1}}$ for all $n \\ge 1$, where $\\pi_0$ acts as an overall scale factor.",
      "<strong>Normalization Condition:</strong> The chain is positive recurrent (ergodic) if and only if the series converges: $S = \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\prod_{k=0}^{n-1} \\frac{p_k}{q_{k+1}} \\lt  \\infty$. When $S \\lt  \\infty$, $\\pi_0 = \\frac{1}{1 + S} > 0$.",
      "<strong>M/M/1 Queue Benchmark:</strong> With constant rates $p_k = p$ and $q_k = q$, the ratio is constant $\\rho = p/q$. The sum converges iff traffic intensity $\\rho \\lt  1$, yielding the classic geometric distribution $\\pi_n = (1 - \\rho)\\rho^n$ with mean occupancy $\\mathbb{E}[N] = \\frac{\\rho}{1 - \\rho}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\pi_n = \\pi_0 \\prod_{k=0}^{n-1} \\frac{p_k}{q_{k+1}}, \\qquad \\pi_0 = \\left(1 + \\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\prod_{k=0}^{n-1} \\frac{p_k}{q_{k+1}}\\right)^{-1} > 0 \\iff S \\lt  \\infty$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Does he stay near the top?</strong> If Max gains places more easily than he loses them, the share of time spent $n$ places back falls off geometrically, and he is mostly leading. If he loses places more easily, he just keeps sliding back and there is no steady law.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming traffic intensity \u03c1 = 1 has a stationary distribution! When \u03c1 = p/q = 1, all \u03c0_n = \u03c0_0 are equal, so the sum diverges. The chain is null recurrent, not positive recurrent!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Birth\u2013death invariant law.</b> Solving the recursion, $\\pi_n=\\pi_0\\prod_{k=0}^{n-1}\\frac{p_k}{q_{k+1}}$ and $\\pi_0=\\Bigl(1+\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\prod_{k=0}^{n-1}\\frac{p_k}{q_{k+1}}\\Bigr)^{-1}$. An irreducible birth\u2013death chain is positive recurrent iff this sum is finite (Ross 4.8; Grimmett 6.5).",
    "hint": "When does Max's championship place have a steady law, and what does it look like?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\pi_n=\\pi_0\\prod_{k\\lt n}\\frac{p_k}{q_{k+1}}$ = multiply the ratios.</strong> Each rung further back multiplies the weight by drop-over-gain.",
      "<strong>$\\pi_0=\\bigl(1+\\sum_n\\prod\\bigr)^{-1}$ = normalise.</strong> The weights must add to one, which fixes the constant.",
      "<strong>The sum must be finite.</strong> If the ratios stay at or above 1, the sum diverges: no steady law, and the chain is not positive recurrent."
    ],
