    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "Time Reversibility & Kolmogorov\u2019s Cycle Criterion",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32203\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><circle cx=\"60.0\" cy=\"40.0\" r=\"10.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a</text><circle cx=\"180.0\" cy=\"40.0\" r=\"10.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"43\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">b</text><circle cx=\"120.0\" cy=\"100.0\" r=\"10.0\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">c</text><line x1=\"72.0\" y1=\"40.0\" x2=\"168.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32203)\"/><line x1=\"174.0\" y1=\"50.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"91.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32203)\"/><line x1=\"110.0\" y1=\"92.0\" x2=\"66.0\" y2=\"50.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32203)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">forward loop</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">P(a,b) P(b,c) P(c,a)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">= P(a,c) P(c,b) P(b,a)  (reverse loop)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u1d62P\u1d62\u2c7c = \u03c0\u2c7cP\u2c7c\u1d62 \u21d4 every loop has equal chance both ways</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A cycle a \u2192 b \u2192 c \u2192 a and its reverse. The chain is reversible iff the products of the one-step chances around every such loop agree in both directions.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Time-Reversed Chain Law:</strong> For a stationary Markov chain $\\{X_n\\}$, the time-reversed chain $Y_n = X_{-n}$ has transition probabilities $P_{ij}^* = \\frac{\\pi_j P_{ji}}{\\pi_i}$. The chain is reversible if $P_{ij}^* = P_{ij}$ for all $i, j$, which is identical to detailed balance $\\pi_i P_{ij} = \\pi_j P_{ji}$.",
      "<strong>Kolmogorov\u2019s Cycle Criterion:</strong> A stationary Markov chain is reversible if and only if for every closed loop of states $i_0, i_1, \\dots, i_k, i_0$, the product of transition probabilities in the forward direction equals the reverse direction: $\\prod_{m=0}^k P_{i_m, i_{m+1}} = \\prod_{m=0}^k P_{i_{m+1}, i_m}$.",
      "<strong>Vortex Impossibility:</strong> Kolmogorov's criterion checks reversibility directly from the transition matrix $P$ without having to solve for the stationary distribution $\\pi$ first; non-reversible chains contain net directional probability circulation (vortices)."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\pi_i P_{ij} = \\pi_j P_{ji} \\iff P_{i_0 i_1} P_{i_1 i_2} \\cdots P_{i_k i_0} = P_{i_0 i_k} \\cdots P_{i_2 i_1} P_{i_1 i_0} \\quad \\forall \\text{ cycles}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Does the season make sense in reverse?</strong> Take three results, win, podium and off the podium. If going round the loop win \u2192 podium \u2192 off \u2192 win has the same chance as going round the other way, then a highlight reel of Max's long-run results played backwards looks just as believable.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming every stationary chain is reversible! Cyclic chains (e.g. 1 \u2192 2 \u2192 3 \u2192 1 with probability 1) have stationary distribution \u03c0 = (1/3, 1/3, 1/3) but reverse direction product is 0 \u2260 1, completely violating reversibility!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Reversibility and Kolmogorov's criterion.</b> An irreducible stationary chain is reversible, $\\pi_iP_{ij}=\\pi_jP_{ji}$, if and only if for every cycle $P_{i_0i_1}P_{i_1i_2}\\cdots P_{i_ki_0}=P_{i_0i_k}\\cdots P_{i_2i_1}P_{i_1i_0}$: each loop has the same probability in both directions (Grimmett 6.5; Kelly, Reversibility).",
    "hint": "How can you tell, from the one-step chances alone, that the chain looks the same run backwards?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\pi_iP_{ij}=\\pi_jP_{ji}$ = reversible.</strong> In steady state, the film run backwards has the same law as the film run forwards.",
      "<strong>$P_{i_0i_1}\\cdots P_{i_ki_0}$ = chance of a loop forwards.</strong> Multiply the one-step chances around a closed cycle of states.",
      "<strong>$=P_{i_0i_k}\\cdots P_{i_1i_0}$ = same loop backwards.</strong> Reversibility holds exactly when this equality holds for every cycle, with no need to know $\\pi$."
    ],
