    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32304\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"64\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32304)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32304)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">lag \u03c4</text><path d=\"M24.0,26.0 L25.7,26.4 L27.4,27.5 L29.1,29.3 L30.7,31.8 L32.4,35.0 L34.1,38.7 L35.8,42.9 L37.5,47.5 L39.1,52.5 L40.8,57.6 L42.5,62.9 L44.2,68.3 L45.9,73.5 L47.6,78.6 L49.2,83.3 L50.9,87.7 L52.6,91.6 L54.3,95.0 L56.0,97.8 L57.7,99.9 L59.4,101.3 L61.0,101.9 L62.7,101.9 L64.4,101.0 L66.1,99.5 L67.8,97.2 L69.5,94.3 L71.1,90.8 L72.8,86.8 L74.5,82.4 L76.2,77.5 L77.9,72.4 L79.5,67.2 L81.2,61.8 L82.9,56.5 L84.6,51.4 L86.3,46.5 L88.0,42.0 L89.7,37.9 L91.3,34.3 L93.0,31.2 L94.7,28.9 L96.4,27.2 L98.1,26.2 L99.8,26.0 L101.4,26.5 L103.1,27.8 L104.8,29.8 L106.5,32.4 L108.2,35.7 L109.8,39.5 L111.5,43.8 L113.2,48.5 L114.9,53.5 L116.6,58.7 L118.3,64.1 L120.0,69.4 L121.6,74.6 L123.3,79.6 L125.0,84.3 L126.7,88.6 L128.4,92.4 L130.1,95.6 L131.7,98.3 L133.4,100.2 L135.1,101.5 L136.8,102.0 L138.5,101.8 L140.2,100.8 L141.8,99.1 L143.5,96.7 L145.2,93.7 L146.9,90.0 L148.6,85.9 L150.2,81.4 L151.9,76.5 L153.6,71.3 L155.3,66.0 L157.0,60.7 L158.7,55.5 L160.3,50.4 L162.0,45.5 L163.7,41.1 L165.4,37.1 L167.1,33.6 L168.8,30.7 L170.4,28.5 L172.1,26.9 L173.8,26.1 L175.5,26.1 L177.2,26.7 L178.9,28.2 L180.6,30.3 L182.2,33.1 L183.9,36.5 L185.6,40.4 L187.3,44.8 L189.0,49.6 L190.7,54.6 L192.3,59.9 L194.0,65.2 L195.7,70.5 L197.4,75.6 L199.1,80.6 L200.8,85.2 L202.4,89.4 L204.1,93.1 L205.8,96.2 L207.5,98.7 L209.2,100.5 L210.8,101.6 L212.5,102.0 L214.2,101.6 L215.9,100.5 L217.6,98.6 L219.3,96.1 L220.9,93.0 L222.6,89.2 L224.3,85.0 L226.0,80.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">R(\u03c4)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">R(\u03c4) = \u00bd \ud835\udd3c[A\u00b2] cos(\u03c9\u2080\u03c4)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">needs \u0398 ~ Uniform(\u2212\u03c0, \u03c0): otherwise the mean moves with t</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">S(\u03c9) = (\u03c0\ud835\udd3c[A\u00b2]/2)[\u03b4(\u03c9 \u2212 \u03c9\u2080) + \u03b4(\u03c9 + \u03c9\u2080)]: two spikes</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The correlation of a random cosine, like the engine vibration at fixed revs: R(\u03c4) = \u00bd\ud835\udd3c[A\u00b2] cos(\u03c9\u2080\u03c4), oscillating for ever, with a spectrum of two spikes at \u00b1\u03c9\u2080. It needs a uniform phase \u0398.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Harmonic Process Model:</strong> Consider $X(t) = A \\cos(\\omega_0 t + \\Theta)$ where amplitude $A$ and phase $\\Theta$ are independent, and $\\omega_0$ is carrier frequency. For $X(t)$ to be WSS, its mean and autocorrelation must be time-invariant.",
      "<strong>Uniform Phase Requirement:</strong> The expected mean is $\\mathbb{E}[X(t)] = \\mathbb{E}[A]\\mathbb{E}[\\cos(\\omega_0 t + \\Theta)]$. This is constant (and equal to 0) for all $t$ if and only if $\\Theta \\sim \\text{Uniform}(-\\pi, \\pi)$ (or any length $2\\pi$ interval).",
      "<strong>Pure Periodic Autocorrelation & PSD Spikes:</strong> When $\\Theta \\sim \\text{Uniform}(-\\pi, \\pi)$, $R_X(\\tau) = \\frac{\\mathbb{E}[A^2]}{2} \\cos(\\omega_0 \\tau)$, which does not decay to zero as $\\tau \\to \\infty$. Its PSD consists of two discrete Dirac delta functions at $\\pm \\omega_0$: $S_X(\\omega) = \\frac{\\pi \\mathbb{E}[A^2]}{2}[\\delta(\\omega - \\omega_0) + \\delta(\\omega + \\omega_0)]$."
    ],
    "math": "$$R_X(\\tau) = \\frac{\\mathbb{E}[A^2]}{2} \\cos(\\omega_0 \\tau) \\iff \\Theta \\sim \\text{Uniform}(-\\pi, \\pi); \\quad S_X(\\omega) = \\frac{\\pi \\mathbb{E}[A^2]}{2} [\\delta(\\omega - \\omega_0) + \\delta(\\omega + \\omega_0)]$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The engine note at fixed revs.</strong> Held at steady revs, the engine shakes at one frequency $\\omega_0$, so its spectrum is a single spike. But the signal only counts as stationary if the moment the recording starts is completely random within one cycle, so the phase is uniform.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming X(t) = cos(\u03c9_0 t) without random phase is WSS! A deterministic cosine has \ud835\udd3c[X(t)] = cos(\u03c9_0 t), which oscillates with time t. It is NOT stationary; random phase uniform over [-\u03c0, \u03c0] is strictly required!",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Random harmonic process.</b> Let $X(t)=A\\cos(\\omega_0t+\\Theta)$ with $A$ independent of $\\Theta$. Then $R_X(\\tau)=\\frac{\\mathbb E[A^2]}2\\cos(\\omega_0\\tau)$ and $\\mathbb E[X(t)]=\\mathbb E[A]\\,\\mathbb E[\\cos(\\omega_0t+\\Theta)]=0$ for all $t$ iff $\\Theta\\sim\\text{Uniform}(-\\pi,\\pi)$. Then $S_X(\\omega)=\\frac{\\pi\\mathbb E[A^2]}2[\\delta(\\omega-\\omega_0)+\\delta(\\omega+\\omega_0)]$ (Papoulis 9\u201310; Grimmett 9.3).",
    "hint": "Why must the phase of the engine's vibration be completely random for the signal to be stationary?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$R_X(\\tau)=\\frac{\\mathbb E[A^2]}2\\cos(\\omega_0\\tau)$ = a cosine in the lag.</strong> The product of two shifted cosines averages to half the amplitude-power times $\\cos(\\omega_0\\tau)$.",
      "<strong>$\\Theta\\sim\\text{Uniform}(-\\pi,\\pi)$ = needed for stationarity.</strong> Only a fully random phase gives a mean that does not move with $t$ and a correlation that depends on $\\tau$ alone.",
      "<strong>$S_X=\\frac{\\pi\\mathbb E[A^2]}2[\\delta(\\omega-\\omega_0)+\\delta(\\omega+\\omega_0)]$ = two spikes.</strong> All the power sits at the frequency $\\pm\\omega_0$."
    ],
