    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32305\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"12\" y=\"50\" width=\"52\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"38.0\" y=\"68.0\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">X(t)</text><rect x=\"84\" y=\"50\" width=\"62\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"115.0\" y=\"68.0\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">h(t)  H(\u03c9)</text><rect x=\"166\" y=\"50\" width=\"52\" height=\"30\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"192.0\" y=\"68.0\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Y(t)</text><line x1=\"64.0\" y1=\"65.0\" x2=\"84.0\" y2=\"65.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32305)\"/><line x1=\"146.0\" y1=\"65.0\" x2=\"166.0\" y2=\"65.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32305)\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">track bumps \u2192 suspension \u2192 what the chassis feels</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Sout(\u03c9) = |H(\u03c9)|\u00b2 Sin(\u03c9)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Rout(\u03c4) = Rin(\u03c4) * h(\u03c4) * h(\u2212\u03c4)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\ud835\udd3cY\u00b2 = (1/2\u03c0) \u222b |H(\u03c9)|\u00b2 Sin(\u03c9) d\u03c9</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">the filter reweights each frequency by its power gain</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "WSS track bumps X(t) through the suspension h give the chassis motion Y(t) with S_Y = |H|\u00b2 S_X. The output power is the area under the reweighted spectrum.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Output Stationarity:</strong> When a WSS process $X(t)$ is applied to a stable LTI system with impulse response $h(t)$, the output $Y(t) = X(t) * h(t) = \\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty h(s)X(t-s)ds$ is also Wide-Sense Stationary.",
      "<strong>Power Spectral Transfer Law:</strong> The output PSD satisfies the fundamental multiplicative relationship: $S_Y(\\omega) = |H(\\omega)|^2 S_X(\\omega)$, where $|H(\\omega)|^2$ is the filter power transfer function.",
      "<strong>RC Low-Pass Filter Benchmark:</strong> When white noise $W(t)$ with PSD $S_W(\\omega) = N_0/2$ drives an RC filter $H(\\omega) = \\frac{1}{1 + j\\omega RC}$, the output PSD is $S_Y(\\omega) = \\frac{N_0/2}{1 + (\\omega RC)^2}$, yielding exponential autocorrelation $R_Y(\\tau) = \\frac{N_0}{4RC} e^{-|\\tau|/RC}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$S_Y(\\omega) = |H(\\omega)|^2 S_X(\\omega), \\qquad R_Y(\\tau) = R_X(\\tau) * h(\\tau) * h(-\\tau), \\qquad \\mathbb{E}[Y^2(t)] = \\frac{1}{2\\pi}\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty |H(\\omega)|^2 S_X(\\omega) d\\omega$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The suspension as a filter.</strong> The track bumps go in, and the chassis feels a smoothed version. The suspension passes the slow swells and damps the sharp jolts. Its effect on the spectrum is just a multiplication by the squared gain at each frequency.",
    "examTrap": "Using H(\u03c9) instead of |H(\u03c9)|\u00b2 for power spectral density! PSD represents power (quadratic in amplitude), so it scales with the magnitude-squared |H(\u03c9)|\u00b2, not the linear frequency response H(\u03c9).",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>LTI filtering of a WSS process.</b> If $X(t)$ is WSS with spectrum $S_X$ and passes through a stable LTI system with impulse response $h$ and transfer function $H(\\omega)$, then $Y=h*X$ is WSS with $S_Y(\\omega)=|H(\\omega)|^2S_X(\\omega)$, $R_Y(\\tau)=R_X(\\tau)*h(\\tau)*h(-\\tau)$ and $\\mathbb E[Y^2(t)]=\\frac1{2\\pi}\\int|H(\\omega)|^2S_X(\\omega)d\\omega$ (Papoulis 10; Grimmett 9.3).",
    "hint": "What does the suspension do to the power of the track bumps at each frequency?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$S_Y(\\omega)=|H(\\omega)|^2S_X(\\omega)$ = reweight each frequency.</strong> A filter multiplies the power at frequency $\\omega$ by its squared gain $|H(\\omega)|^2$.",
      "<strong>$R_Y=R_X*h*h(-\\cdot)$ = in the lag domain.</strong> The same statement for the correlation, by the inverse Fourier transform.",
      "<strong>$\\mathbb E[Y^2]=\\frac1{2\\pi}\\int|H|^2S_Xd\\omega$ = output power.</strong> The total output power is the area under the reweighted spectrum."
    ],
