    "title": "Mean-Ergodicity & Slutsky\u2019s Integral Condition",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32306\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32306)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32306)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">T</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc\u0302\u1d1b</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bc</text><path d=\"M28.0,50.0 L32.0,61.2 L36.0,57.1 L40.0,62.0 L44.0,62.1 L48.0,53.3 L52.0,53.0 L56.0,64.5 L60.0,57.0 L64.0,56.8 L68.0,65.7 L72.0,59.7 L76.0,63.5 L80.0,59.8 L84.0,61.4 L88.0,56.7 L92.0,61.2 L96.0,63.3 L100.0,60.2 L104.0,62.0 L108.0,61.4 L112.0,56.5 L116.0,62.0 L120.0,60.7 L124.0,58.5 L128.0,56.5 L132.0,62.7 L136.0,59.8 L140.0,61.5 L144.0,62.6 L148.0,61.5 L152.0,62.8 L156.0,59.3 L160.0,62.0 L164.0,59.6 L168.0,62.8 L172.0,62.4 L176.0,57.5 L180.0,57.8 L184.0,58.3 L188.0,62.8 L192.0,59.6 L196.0,60.7 L200.0,58.9 L204.0,60.0 L208.0,59.4 L212.0,59.2 L216.0,60.5 L220.0,60.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">time average over [\u2212T, T] \u2192 \u03bc in mean square</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">iff (1/T)\u222b\u2080\u00b2\u1d40 (1 \u2212 \u03c4/2T) C(\u03c4) d\u03c4 \u2192 0</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">correlations must die away fast enough</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The time average \u03bc\u0302\u1d1b of a single telemetry trace homes in on \u03bc as T grows, provided the covariance C(\u03c4) fades fast enough (Slutsky's condition).",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Temporal Mean Estimator:</strong> For a WSS process, the time average over $[-T, T]$ is $\\hat{\\mu}_T = \\frac{1}{2T} \\int_{-T}^T X(t) dt$. By linearity of expectation, $\\mathbb{E}[\\hat{\\mu}_T] = \\mu$, making $\\hat{\\mu}_T$ an unbiased estimator of ensemble mean $\\mu$.",
      "<strong>Variance Decomposition & Slutsky\u2019s Condition:</strong> The variance is $\\operatorname{Var}(\\hat{\\mu}_T) = \\frac{1}{T} \\int_0^{2T} \\left(1 - \\frac{\\tau}{2T}\\right) C_X(\\tau) d\\tau$. The process is mean-ergodic in mean-square ($\\hat{\\mu}_T \\xrightarrow{L^2} \\mu$) if and only if $\\lim_{T \\to \\infty} \\operatorname{Var}(\\hat{\\mu}_T) = 0$.",
      "<strong>Sufficient Covariance Decay Condition:</strong> If the autocovariance decays asymptotically to zero, $\\lim_{\\tau \\to \\infty} C_X(\\tau) = 0$ (or $\\int_0^\\infty |C_X(\\tau)| d\\tau \\lt  \\infty$), then by the dominated convergence theorem $\\operatorname{Var}(\\hat{\\mu}_T) \\to 0$, guaranteeing mean-ergodicity."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\hat{\\mu}_T = \\frac{1}{2T}\\int_{-T}^T X(t) dt \\xrightarrow{L^2} \\mu \\iff \\lim_{T \\to \\infty} \\frac{1}{T}\\int_0^{2T}\\left(1 - \\frac{\\tau}{2T}\\right) C_X(\\tau) d\\tau = 0$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>One long trace is enough.</strong> If the vibration now is basically unrelated to the vibration a few laps later, then averaging one long telemetry trace gives the true mean. You don't need the same run repeated in many cars.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming all WSS processes are mean-ergodic! Consider X(t) = A where A ~ \ud835\udca9(0, 1) is a single random variable frozen across all time. It is WSS with C_X(\u03c4) = 1, but \u03bc\u0302_T = A \u2260 0 for any single realization, so Var(\u03bc\u0302_T) = 1 does not decay to 0!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Mean ergodicity (Slutsky).</b> For a WSS process with mean $\\mu$ and covariance $C_X(\\tau)$, $\\hat\\mu_T=\\frac1{2T}\\int_{-T}^TX(t)\\,dt\\to\\mu$ in $L^2$ if and only if $\\lim_{T\\to\\infty}\\frac1T\\int_0^{2T}\\bigl(1-\\frac{\\tau}{2T}\\bigr)C_X(\\tau)\\,d\\tau=0$ (Papoulis 13; Grimmett 9.5).",
    "hint": "When does one long telemetry trace give you the true mean vibration level?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\hat\\mu_T=\\frac1{2T}\\int_{-T}^TX(t)dt$ = the time average.</strong> Average one long recording over the window $[-T,T]$.",
      "<strong>$\\hat\\mu_T\\to\\mu$ in $L^2$ = ergodic in the mean.</strong> The mean-square error $\\mathbb E|\\hat\\mu_T-\\mu|^2$ goes to zero.",
      "<strong>$\\frac1T\\int_0^{2T}(1-\\frac\\tau{2T})C_X(\\tau)d\\tau\\to0$ = Slutsky's condition.</strong> This is $\\operatorname{Var}(\\hat\\mu_T)$: the covariance must fade fast enough that the long average loses its randomness."
    ],
