    "category": "SCALING & COVARIANCE",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "Brownian Covariance Kernel & Self-Similarity Scaling",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32503\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"108\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32503)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32503)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">s</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">Cov(B(s), B(t))</text><path d=\"M24.0,108.0 L29.3,104.7 L34.6,101.4 L39.9,98.1 L45.2,94.9 L50.5,91.6 L55.8,88.3 L61.1,85.0 L66.4,81.7 L71.7,78.4 L77.0,75.1 L82.3,71.9 L87.6,68.6 L92.9,65.3 L98.2,62.0 L103.5,58.7 L108.8,55.4 L114.1,52.1 L119.4,48.9 L124.7,45.6 L130.0,42.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"42.28\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"42.28\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"108.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"42.3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"130.0\" y1=\"106.0\" x2=\"130.0\" y2=\"110.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">t</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">= s for s \u2264 t</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">= t for s \u2265 t</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"6.8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Cov(B(t), B(s)) = min(t, s);  B(ct) =\u1d48 \u221ac B(t);  tB(1/t) =\u1d48 B(t)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">zoom in by c and out by \u221ac: same picture</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The covariance min(s, t) as a function of s for a fixed t: it rises like s until t and then stays at t. Self-similarity: time scaled by c, the gap by \u221ac.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Covariance Kernel Derivation:</strong> For $s \\le t$, write $B(t) = B(s) + [B(t) - B(s)]$. Since the increment is independent of $B(s)$: $\\operatorname{Cov}(B(t), B(s)) = \\mathbb{E}[B(s)(B(s) + B(t) - B(s))] = \\mathbb{E}[B^2(s)] + 0 = s$. Thus $\\operatorname{Cov}(B(t), B(s)) = \\min(t, s)$.",
      "<strong>Diffusive Self-Similarity:</strong> For any scale $c > 0$, the scaled process $X(t) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{c}} B(ct)$ is also a standard Brownian motion: $B(ct) \\stackrel{d}{=} \\sqrt{c} B(t)$. Zooming into time by $c$ magnifies amplitude by $\\sqrt{c}$, confirming Hurst exponent $H = 1/2$.",
      "<strong>Time Inversion Invariance:</strong> The time-inverted process $Y(t) = t B(1/t)$ for $t > 0$ with $Y(0) = 0$ is a standard Brownian motion, establishing deep asymptotic connections between $t \\to 0$ and $t \\to \\infty$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\operatorname{Cov}(B(t), B(s)) = \\min(t, s), \\qquad B(ct) \\stackrel{d}{=} \\sqrt{c} B(t) \\quad \\forall c > 0, \\qquad t B(1/t) \\stackrel{d}{=} B(t)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>The final gap contains the halfway gap.</strong> The gap at the chequered flag is the gap at half distance plus whatever happened after. So how the two relate is set by the earlier time, and a zoomed-out view of the gap looks like the original.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming Cov(B(t), B(s)) = max(t, s) or s\u00b7t! For s < t, future innovations B(t) - B(s) are independent of past values, so only the shared past interval [0, s] contributes to covariance!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Brownian covariance and scaling.</b> $\\operatorname{Cov}(B(t),B(s))=\\min(t,s)$. For every $c\\gt 0$, $B(ct)\\overset d=\\sqrt c\\,B(t)$ (self-similarity), and $tB(1/t)\\overset d=B(t)$ (time inversion, with value $0$ at $t=0$) (Ross 10.1; Durrett 8).",
    "hint": "How are the gap at half distance and the gap at the flag related, and what happens when you zoom in or out?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\operatorname{Cov}(B(t),B(s))=\\min(t,s)$ = shared history.</strong> For $s\\le t$, $B(t)=B(s)+(\\text{independent increment})$, so the covariance is $\\operatorname{Var}B(s)=s$.",
      "<strong>$B(ct)\\overset d=\\sqrt cB(t)$ = scaling.</strong> Speeding up time by $c$ and shrinking the gap scale by $\\sqrt c$ gives the same law.",
      "<strong>$tB(1/t)\\overset d=B(t)$ = time inversion.</strong> It has the same covariance, so the same law as a Gaussian process."
    ],
