    "cardNumber": "05",
    "category": "REFLECTION PRINCIPLE",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "The Reflection Principle & Running Maximum Law",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32505\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32505)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"14\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32505)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">t</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">a</text><path d=\"M26.0,90.0 L50.0,76.0 L74.0,60.0 L98.0,46.0 L122.0,34.0 L146.0,44.0 L170.0,52.0 L196.0,60.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><path d=\"M122.0,34.0 L146.0,36.0 L170.0,28.0 L196.0,20.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><line x1=\"122.0\" y1=\"88.0\" x2=\"122.0\" y2=\"92.0\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"122\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c4</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">path</text><text x=\"192.32\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">mirror image</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">reflect after hitting level a</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">\u2119(M(t) \u2265 a) = 2\u2119(B(t) \u2265 a) = 2(1 \u2212 \u03a6(a/\u221at))</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"130\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">f(\u03c4\u2090)(t) = a / \u221a(2\u03c0t\u00b3) \u00b7 e^(\u2212a\u00b2/2t)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">hitting time of a has a heavy tail: no mean</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "The gap hits level a at time \u03c4. Reflecting the rest of the path about a gives a mirror path, so \u2119(M(t) \u2265 a) = 2\u2119(B(t) \u2265 a), where M(t) is the biggest lead so far. The hitting time has a heavy tail.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Reflection Principle Argument:</strong> Let $M(t) = \\max_{0 \\le s \\le t} B(s)$ and $\\tau_a = \\inf\\{s: B(s) = a\\}$. Paths hitting $a$ before $t$ either end above $a$ or below $a$ at time $t$. By the strong Markov property and spatial symmetry at $\\tau_a$, both branches are equally likely, proving $\\mathbb P(M(t) \\ge a) = 2 \\mathbb P(B(t) \\ge a)$.",
      "<strong>Running Maximum Distribution:</strong> Because $B(t) \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, t)$, the running maximum has CDF $\\mathbb P(M(t) \\le a) = 2\\Phi(a/\\sqrt{t}) - 1$, revealing that $M(t) \\stackrel{d}{=} |B(t)|$ has the folded half-normal distribution.",
      "<strong>L\u00e9vy First Passage Density:</strong> Differentiating $\\mathbb P(\\tau_a \\le t) = \\mathbb P(M(t) \\ge a)$ with respect to $t$ yields the heavy-tailed L\u00e9vy hitting-time density $f_{\\tau_a}(t) = \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2\\pi t^3}} e^{-a^2/(2t)}$ with infinite expected hitting time $\\mathbb{E}[\\tau_a] = \\infty$."
    ],
    "math": "$$\\mathbb P(M(t) \\ge a) = 2 \\mathbb P(B(t) \\ge a) = 2\\left(1 - \\Phi\\left(\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{t}}\\right)\\right); \\quad f_{\\tau_a}(t) = \\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2\\pi t^3}} e^{-a^2/(2t)}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Will the lead ever reach 5 seconds?</strong> The chance that Max's biggest lead so far has reached 5 seconds is twice the chance that his lead right now is above 5 seconds, because every path that touched 5 has a mirror twin that ends below it.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming \ud835\udd3c[\u03c4_a] is finite because \u2119(\u03c4_a < \u221e) = 1! Although standard Brownian motion is guaranteed to hit level a eventually with probability 1, the heavy tail t^{-3/2} causes the expected wait time \ud835\udd3c[\u03c4_a] to diverge to infinity!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Reflection principle.</b> Let $M(t)=\\max_{s\\le t}B(s)$ and $\\tau_a=\\inf\\{t:B(t)=a\\}$, $a\\gt 0$. Then $\\mathbb P(M(t)\\ge a)=\\mathbb P(\\tau_a\\le t)=2\\mathbb P(B(t)\\ge a)=2\\bigl(1-\\Phi(a/\\sqrt t)\\bigr)$, and $\\tau_a$ has density $f_{\\tau_a}(t)=\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2\\pi t^3}}e^{-a^2/(2t)}$ (Ross 10.2; Durrett 8).",
    "hint": "What is the chance that Max's lead ever reaches a seconds before time t?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(M(t)\\ge a)=\\mathbb P(\\tau_a\\le t)$ = reaching the level.</strong> The biggest lead so far is at least $a$ iff the lead first hit $a$ by time $t$.",
      "<strong>$=2\\mathbb P(B(t)\\ge a)$ = reflect after hitting.</strong> After $\\tau_a$ the path is symmetric about $a$, so ending above $a$ is half as likely as hitting it.",
      "<strong>$f_{\\tau_a}(t)=\\frac a{\\sqrt{2\\pi t^3}}e^{-a^2/2t}$ = the hitting time.</strong> It decays like $t^{-3/2}$, a heavy tail with infinite mean."
    ],
