    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32602\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"14\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"62.0\" y=\"30.0\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">S\u2099 \u2212 n\u03bc</text><rect x=\"130\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"178.0\" y=\"30.0\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">S\u2099\u00b2 \u2212 n\u03c3\u00b2</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">centred total</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">centred square</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"62\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"62.0\" y=\"78.0\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">e^(\u03b8S\u2099) / M(\u03b8)\u207f</text><rect x=\"130\" y=\"62\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"178.0\" y=\"78.0\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">M\u2099 = \ud835\udd3c[Y | \u2131\u2099]</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">exponential (tilted)</text><text x=\"178\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">running forecast of Y</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">each subtracts off its predictable drift (the compensator)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">what is left is a fair game</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "Four martingale families: the centred total S\u2099 \u2212 n\u03bc, the compensated square S\u2099\u00b2 \u2212 n\u03c3\u00b2, the exponential martingale, and the forecast M\u2099 = \ud835\udd3c[Y | \u2131\u2099].",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Linear & Variance Compensated Walks:</strong> For i.i.d. increments $X_i$ with mean $\\mu$ and variance $\\sigma^2$: (1) $M_n = S_n - n\\mu$ is a zero-mean martingale; (2) When $\\mu = 0$, $M_n = S_n^2 - n\\sigma^2$ is a variance martingale, neutralizing quadratic growth via compensator $-n\\sigma^2$.",
      "<strong>Exponential Wald Martingale:</strong> For any $\\theta$ where MGF $M_X(\\theta) = \\mathbb{E}[e^{\\theta X}] \\lt  \\infty$, the geometric product $M_n = \\frac{e^{\\theta S_n}}{(M_X(\\theta))^n}$ is a positive martingale with $\\mathbb{E}[M_n] = 1$, vital for large deviations and ruin probabilities.",
      "<strong>Doob\u2019s Martingale Construction:</strong> For any integrable random variable $Y$ with $\\mathbb{E}[|Y|] \\lt  \\infty$, the sequence of progressive conditional estimates $M_n = \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid \\mathcal{F}_n]$ is automatically a martingale. As information accumulates ($n \\to \\infty$), $M_n \\to Y$ almost surely."
    ],
    "math": "$$S_n - n\\mu, \\qquad S_n^2 - n\\sigma^2, \\qquad \\frac{e^{\\theta S_n}}{(M_X(\\theta))^n}, \\qquad M_n = \\mathbb{E}[Y \\mid \\mathcal{F}_n]$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Remove the drift.</strong> Max's total race time after $n$ laps grows by about one average lap time per lap; subtract that drift and what is left is a fair game. His live win probability, a forecast of the final result, is also a fair game.",
    "examTrap": "Assuming S_n\u00b2 is a martingale! For zero-mean random walks, \ud835\udd3c[S_{n+1}\u00b2 | F_n] = S_n\u00b2 + \u03c3\u00b2 > S_n\u00b2, making S_n\u00b2 a strict *submartingale*. One must subtract the compensator n\u03c3\u00b2 to form a true martingale!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Canonical martingales.</b> For i.i.d. $X_i$ with mean $\\mu$, variance $\\sigma^2$ and MGF $M_X(\\theta)\\lt \\infty$, and $S_n=\\sum_{i\\le n}X_i$: $S_n-n\\mu$, $(S_n-n\\mu)^2-n\\sigma^2$ and $\\dfrac{e^{\\theta S_n}}{M_X(\\theta)^n}$ are martingales. For any integrable $Y$, $M_n=\\mathbb E[Y\\mid\\mathcal F_n]$ is a martingale (Doob) (Williams 10; Grimmett 12.1).",
    "hint": "Which natural quantities built from lap times are fair games?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$S_n-n\\mu$ = the centred total.</strong> Subtract the expected drift $n\\mu$; the rest has zero mean increments.",
      "<strong>$(S_n-n\\mu)^2-n\\sigma^2$ and $e^{\\theta S_n}/M_X(\\theta)^n$ = compensated square and exponential.</strong> Subtract the compensator $n\\sigma^2$, or divide by the MGF to the $n$.",
      "<strong>$M_n=\\mathbb E[Y\\mid\\mathcal F_n]$ = Doob martingale.</strong> Your best forecast of the final result, updated as each lap comes in, is a fair game."
    ],
