    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32606\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32606)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32606)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">n</text><path d=\"M26.0,64.0 L32.5,60.4 L39.1,64.0 L45.6,67.6 L52.1,64.0 L58.7,60.4 L65.2,56.8 L71.7,53.2 L78.3,56.8 L84.8,60.4 L91.3,64.0 L97.9,67.6 L104.4,71.2 L110.9,67.6 L117.5,64.0 L124.0,60.4 L130.5,64.0 L137.1,60.4 L143.6,64.0 L150.1,60.4 L156.7,64.0 L163.2,60.4 L169.7,56.8 L176.3,60.4 L182.8,56.8 L189.3,53.2 L195.9,56.8 L202.4,60.4 L208.9,56.8 L215.5,60.4 L222.0,64.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03bb</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"11\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Doob: \u2119(max X\u2096 \u2265 \u03bb) \u2264 \ud835\udd3c[X\u2099]/\u03bb  (non-negative submartingale)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Azuma: \u2119(|M\u2099 \u2212 M\u2080| \u2265 t) \u2264 2 exp(\u2212t\u00b2 / 2\u2211c\u2096\u00b2)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">bounded moves per lap \u21d2 it rarely strays far</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"6.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">(c\u2096 = the cap on lap k's move)</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A non-negative fair game and the level \u03bb: Doob bounds the chance that its running maximum reaches \u03bb. With capped moves per lap, Azuma bounds the chance it strays far.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Doob\u2019s Submartingale Maximal Inequality:</strong> Let $\\{X_n\\}$ be a non-negative submartingale. For any threshold $\\lambda > 0$: $P\\left(\\max_{0 \\le k \\le n} X_k \\ge \\lambda\\right) \\le \\frac{\\mathbb{E}[X_n]}{\\lambda}$. This remarkably bounds the entire running maximum envelope using only the final time-$n$ expectation.",
      "<strong>Doob\u2019s $L^p$ Maximal Inequality:</strong> For a martingale $M_n$ with $p > 1$: $\\mathbb{E}\\left[\\left(\\max_{0 \\le k \\le n} |M_k|\\right)^p\\right] \\le \\left(\\frac{p}{p-1}\\right)^p \\mathbb{E}[|M_n|^p]$, showing the running supremum is $L^p$-controlled by terminal value.",
      "<strong>Azuma-Hoeffding Concentration:</strong> If martingale increments are bounded ($|M_k - M_{k-1}| \\le c_k$ a.s.), then $\\mathbb P(|M_n - M_0| \\ge t) \\le 2 \\exp\\left(-\\frac{t^2}{2\\sum_{k=1}^n c_k^2}\\right)$, extending Hoeffding's inequality to dependent stochastic processes."
    ],
    "math": "$$P\\left(\\max_{0 \\le k \\le n} X_k \\ge \\lambda\\right) \\le \\frac{\\mathbb{E}[X_n]}{\\lambda}, \\qquad \\mathbb P(|M_n - M_0| \\ge t) \\le 2\\exp\\left(-\\frac{t^2}{2\\sum_{k=1}^n c_k^2}\\right)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Caps on each lap.</strong> If no single lap can move Max's win probability by more than a little, then the chance that it ends up far from where it started after many laps is very small, like a bell's tail.",
    "examTrap": "Applying Doob's maximal inequality to supermartingales or signed martingales! The classic maximal inequality requires a *non-negative submartingale* (such as |M_n| or M_n^+). For general martingales, apply it to |M_n| or |M_n|^p.",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Doob's inequality and Azuma\u2013Hoeffding.</b> For a non-negative submartingale $(X_k)$, $\\mathbb P\\bigl(\\max_{0\\le k\\le n}X_k\\ge\\lambda\\bigr)\\le\\frac{\\mathbb E[X_n]}\\lambda$. For a martingale with $|M_k-M_{k-1}|\\le c_k$, $\\mathbb P(|M_n-M_0|\\ge t)\\le2\\exp\\Bigl(-\\frac{t^2}{2\\sum_{k=1}^nc_k^2}\\Bigr)$ (Williams 14; Grimmett 12.6).",
    "hint": "How likely is a fair game, like Max's win probability, ever to swing far from where it started?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\mathbb P(\\max_kX_k\\ge\\lambda)\\le\\mathbb E[X_n]/\\lambda$ = Doob.</strong> Markov's inequality for the whole running maximum, not just the last value.",
      "<strong>$|M_k-M_{k-1}|\\le c_k$ = capped moves per lap.</strong> No single lap can move the value by more than $c_k$.",
      "<strong>$2\\exp(-t^2/2\\sum c_k^2)$ = Azuma\u2013Hoeffding.</strong> The value strays by $t$ with chance that falls off as a Gaussian tail in $t/\\sqrt{\\sum c_k^2}$.",
      "<strong>$\\sup_n\\mathbb E|M_n|\\lt\\infty\\Rightarrow M_n\\to M_\\infty$ a.s. = martingales settle (Doob's convergence theorem).</strong> A martingale that stays bounded in mean, for instance one in $[0,1]$ like Max's live win probability, converges almost surely; bounded ones also converge in $L^1$, so $\\mathbb E[M_\\infty]=\\mathbb E[M_0]$."
    ],
