    "highlighterClass": "highlight-cyan",
    "title": "Infinitesimal Generator Q & Exponential Holding Times",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32701\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"46\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"46\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"26\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"68\" y2=\"38\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"47.0\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">i</text><line x1=\"72\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"128\" y2=\"38\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"100.0\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">j</text><line x1=\"132\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"148\" y2=\"38\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"140.0\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">i</text><line x1=\"152\" y1=\"38\" x2=\"224\" y2=\"38\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"188.0\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">k</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">stay in a state for an Exp(q\u1d62) time, then jump</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">rate of jumping i \u2192 j in h: q\u1d62\u2c7c h + o(h)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Q: q\u1d62\u2c7c \u2265 0 off the diagonal, q\u1d62\u1d62 = \u2212\u2211\u2c7c\u2260\u1d62 q\u1d62\u2c7c</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">Q1 = 0  (each row sums to zero)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">holding time T\u1d62 ~ Exp(q\u1d62),  q\u1d62 = \u2212q\u1d62\u1d62</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">next state j with chance q\u1d62\u2c7c / q\u1d62</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A path of the chain: racing (i), in the pits (j), racing again, then retired (k). Each stay is an exponential holding time. The generator Q holds the jump rates q\u1d62\u2c7c, and each row sums to zero.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Sojourn & Jump Formulation:</strong> In a continuous-time Markov chain, upon entering state $i$, the process remains there for an exponential holding time $T_i \\sim \\text{Exp}(q_i)$ where $q_i = \\sum_{j \\ne i} q_{ij}$. It then transitions to state $j \\ne i$ with jump probability $P_{ij} = \\frac{q_{ij}}{q_i}$.",
      "<strong>Infinitesimal Generator Definition:</strong> The generator matrix $Q = (q_{ij})$ represents transition rates: $q_{ij} = \\lim_{h \\downarrow 0} \\frac{P_{ij}(h) - \\delta_{ij}}{h}$. Thus for small $h$, $P_{ij}(h) = q_{ij} h + o(h)$ for $i \\ne j$, and $P_{ii}(h) = 1 - q_i h + o(h)$.",
      "<strong>Row-Sum Zero Invariant:</strong> Conservation of probability dictates that the diagonal entries must equal the negative sum of off-diagonal entries: $q_{ii} = -q_i = -\\sum_{j \\ne i} q_{ij} \\le 0$, ensuring $Q \\mathbf{1} = \\mathbf{0}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$q_{ij} = \\lim_{h \\downarrow 0} \\frac{P_{ij}(h)}{h} \\ (i \\ne j), \\qquad q_{ii} = -\\sum_{j \\ne i} q_{ij}, \\qquad Q \\mathbf{1} = \\mathbf{0}, \\qquad T_i \\sim \\text{Exp}(q_i)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Racing, pitting, retired.</strong> Max's car is racing, in the pits or retired. While racing it pits at a rate of, say, 2 per hour and retires at 0.1 per hour. So it stays out for an exponential time, then jumps: to the pits with chance 2/2.1, to retirement with chance 0.1/2.1.",
    "examTrap": "Thinking diagonal entries q_{ii} are probabilities! Generator entries q_{ij} are transition *rates* (units 1/time), not probabilities. Diagonals q_{ii} are strictly non-positive (q_{ii} \u2264 0) and can be less than -1!",
    "stmtKind": "DEFINITION",
    "statement": "<b>Generator of a CTMC.</b> A continuous-time Markov chain on $S$ has transition functions $P_{ij}(t)$ and generator $Q$ with $q_{ij}=\\lim_{h\\downarrow0}\\frac{P_{ij}(h)}h\\ (i\\ne j)$, $q_{ii}=-\\sum_{j\\ne i}q_{ij}$, so $Q\\mathbf 1=\\mathbf 0$. The holding time in $i$ is $T_i\\sim\\operatorname{Exp}(q_i)$, $q_i=-q_{ii}$, and the next state is $j$ with probability $q_{ij}/q_i$ (Ross 6.2; Grimmett 6.9).",
    "hint": "If Max's car can change state at any instant, what takes the place of the one-step table?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$q_{ij}=\\lim P_{ij}(h)/h$ = jump rates.</strong> In a short time $h$ the chance of moving from $i$ to $j$ is about $q_{ij}h$.",
      "<strong>$q_{ii}=-\\sum_{j\\ne i}q_{ij}$ and $Q\\mathbf 1=\\mathbf 0$ = rows sum to zero.</strong> The diagonal is minus the total rate of leaving $i$.",
      "<strong>$T_i\\sim\\operatorname{Exp}(q_i)$ = the holding time.</strong> The car stays for an exponential time, then jumps to $j$ with probability $q_{ij}/q_i$."
    ],
