    "cardNumber": "03",
    "category": "TWO-STATE TRANSIENT",
    "highlighterClass": "highlight-emerald",
    "title": "Two-State CTMC Transient Solutions & Relaxation Rate",
    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32703\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32703)\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"104\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\" marker-end=\"url(#arr-32703)\"/><text x=\"226\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">t</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">P\u2081\u2081(t)</text><path d=\"M24.0,26.0 L27.4,28.2 L30.7,30.2 L34.1,32.1 L37.5,33.8 L40.8,35.4 L44.2,36.8 L47.6,38.2 L50.9,39.4 L54.3,40.5 L57.7,41.5 L61.0,42.5 L64.4,43.4 L67.8,44.2 L71.1,44.9 L74.5,45.6 L77.9,46.2 L81.2,46.8 L84.6,47.3 L88.0,47.8 L91.3,48.2 L94.7,48.6 L98.1,49.0 L101.4,49.4 L104.8,49.7 L108.2,50.0 L111.5,50.2 L114.9,50.5 L118.3,50.7 L121.6,50.9 L125.0,51.1 L128.4,51.3 L131.7,51.5 L135.1,51.6 L138.5,51.7 L141.8,51.9 L145.2,52.0 L148.6,52.1 L151.9,52.2 L155.3,52.3 L158.7,52.4 L162.0,52.4 L165.4,52.5 L168.8,52.6 L172.1,52.6 L175.5,52.7 L178.9,52.7 L182.2,52.8 L185.6,52.8 L189.0,52.9 L192.3,52.9 L195.7,52.9 L199.1,53.0 L202.4,53.0 L205.8,53.0 L209.2,53.0 L212.5,53.1 L215.9,53.1 L219.3,53.1 L222.6,53.1 L226.0,53.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"53.3\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"53.3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"0.8\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"48.3\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#000000\">\u03c0\u2081 = \u03bc/(\u03bb+\u03bc)</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#000000\">decays at rate \u03bb + \u03bc</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">P\u2081\u2081(t) = \u03bc/(\u03bb+\u03bc) + \u03bb/(\u03bb+\u03bc) e^(\u2212(\u03bb+\u03bc)t)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">memory of the start fades at rate \u03bb + \u03bc</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "P\u2081\u2081(t), the chance of green flag at time t given green at the start, starts at 1 and decays at rate \u03bb + \u03bc to its limit \u03c0\u2081 = \u03bc/(\u03bb + \u03bc), the long-run share of green-flag time.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Two-State Machine Failure Model:</strong> Let state 1 be Operating (failure rate $\\lambda$) and state 2 be Broken (repair rate $\\mu$). The generator matrix is $Q = \\begin{pmatrix} -\\lambda & \\lambda \\\\ \\mu & -\\mu \\end{pmatrix}$.",
      "<strong>First-Order Differential Solution:</strong> The Kolmogorov forward equation yields $\\frac{d P_{11}(t)}{dt} = \\mu - (\\lambda + \\mu) P_{11}(t)$. With initial condition $P_{11}(0) = 1$, solving via integrating factor $e^{(\\lambda+\\mu)t}$ yields $P_{11}(t) = \\frac{\\mu}{\\lambda + \\mu} + \\frac{\\lambda}{\\lambda + \\mu} e^{-(\\lambda + \\mu)t}$.",
      "<strong>Spectral Gap & Relaxation Time:</strong> The eigenvalues of $Q$ are $\\lambda_1 = 0$ (stationary mode) and $\\lambda_2 = -(\\lambda + \\mu)$ (decay mode). The spectral gap $\\lambda + \\mu$ defines the relaxation rate, with mixing time $\\tau_{\\text{relax}} = \\frac{1}{\\lambda + \\mu}$."
    ],
    "math": "$$P_{11}(t) = \\frac{\\mu}{\\lambda + \\mu} + \\frac{\\lambda}{\\lambda + \\mu} e^{-(\\lambda + \\mu)t}, \\qquad \\lim_{t \\to \\infty} P_{11}(t) = \\pi_1 = \\frac{\\mu}{\\lambda + \\mu}$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>Green flag or safety car.</strong> If a safety car comes out at rate 1 per hour under green, and goes back in at rate 5 per hour, then after about 10 minutes the race is green with chance close to $\\frac56$, whether it started green or not.",
    "examTrap": "Thinking relaxation rate is min(\u03bb, \u03bc)! The transient exponent is the *sum* of the transition rates, -(\u03bb + \u03bc)t. Transitions in both directions accelerate convergence toward stationary balance.",
    "stmtKind": "WORKED EXAMPLE",
    "statement": "<b>Two-state chain.</b> States $1\\to2$ at rate $\\lambda$ and $2\\to1$ at rate $\\mu$. Then $P_{11}(t)=\\dfrac\\mu{\\lambda+\\mu}+\\dfrac\\lambda{\\lambda+\\mu}e^{-(\\lambda+\\mu)t}$, and $\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}P_{11}(t)=\\pi_1=\\frac\\mu{\\lambda+\\mu}$. The memory of the start decays at rate $\\lambda+\\mu$ (Ross 6.4; Grimmett 6.9).",
    "hint": "How quickly does a race that starts under green flag forget that it started green?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$\\pi_1=\\frac\\mu{\\lambda+\\mu}$ = the long-run share in state 1.</strong> Time in 1 is proportional to $1/\\lambda$, in 2 to $1/\\mu$; the share is $\\mu/(\\lambda+\\mu)$.",
      "<strong>$\\frac\\lambda{\\lambda+\\mu}e^{-(\\lambda+\\mu)t}$ = the transient.</strong> The extra chance of still being green because the race started green, which decays exponentially.",
      "<strong>$\\lambda+\\mu$ = the relaxation rate.</strong> The chain forgets its start on a time scale $1/(\\lambda+\\mu)$."
    ],
