    "drawingSvg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 240 145\" class=\"w-full h-full\"><defs><marker id=\"arr-32706\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"5\" markerHeight=\"5\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 8 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"44\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"44\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"66\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"66\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"118\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"118\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"66\" cy=\"50\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"118\" cy=\"50\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><circle cx=\"190\" cy=\"50\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#000000\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"7.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">ticks at rate \u03bd \u2265 max\u1d62 q\u1d62 (Poisson clock)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"34\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">each tick: move by K = I + Q/\u03bd (some ticks do nothing)</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">K = I + Q/\u03bd</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"8\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">P(t) = \u2211\u2099 (\u03bdt)\u207f e^(\u2212\u03bdt)/n!  K\u207f</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">a discrete chain run at Poisson(\u03bdt) clock ticks</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"7\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-style=\"normal\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#000000\">sum is a probability mixture: stable to compute</text></svg>",
    "drawingCaption": "A Poisson clock ticks at rate \u03bd. At each tick the chain moves by K = I + Q/\u03bd (some ticks leave it in place). So P(t) is a Poisson mixture of the matrix powers K\u207f.",
    "coreTranslation": [
      "<strong>Uniformization Rate Selection:</strong> Let $\\nu \\ge \\max_i q_i \\lt  \\infty$ be a uniform rate dominating all state departure rates. Define the discrete-time transition probability matrix $K = I + \\frac{1}{\\nu} Q$.",
      "<strong>Valid DTMC Stochasticity:</strong> Because off-diagonals $K_{ij} = \\frac{q_{ij}}{\\nu} \\ge 0$ and diagonals $K_{ii} = 1 - \\frac{q_i}{\\nu} \\ge 0$ with row sums $\\sum_j K_{ij} = 1 + \\frac{1}{\\nu}\\sum_j q_{ij} = 1$, $K$ is a valid row-stochastic matrix with self-loops representing fictitious null transitions.",
      "<strong>Poisson Mixture Expansion:</strong> Rewriting the matrix exponential $P(t) = e^{Qt} = e^{\\nu t(K - I)} = \\sum_{n=0}^\\infty \\frac{(\\nu t)^n e^{-\\nu t}}{n!} K^n$. Continuous CTMC transitions reduce to a standard Poisson counting clock $N(t) \\sim \\text{Poisson}(\\nu t)$ governing discrete matrix multiplications $K^n$."
    ],
    "math": "$$K = I + \\frac{1}{\\nu} Q, \\qquad P(t) = \\sum_{n=0}^\\infty \\frac{(\\nu t)^n e^{-\\nu t}}{n!} K^n \\quad (\\nu \\ge \\max_i q_i)$$",
    "personalConnection": "<strong>A clock ticks, the race may switch.</strong> Fix a fast random clock that ticks at least as often as any switch could happen. At each tick, race control sends out or calls in the safety car with the right small chance, or nothing changes.",
    "examTrap": "Choosing \u03bd smaller than max_i q_i! If \u03bd < q_i for some state i, the diagonal entry K_{ii} = 1 - q_i/\u03bd becomes negative, invalidating K as a probability matrix and causing uniformization to blow up!",
    "stmtKind": "THEOREM",
    "statement": "<b>Uniformization (Jensen).</b> Pick $\\nu\\ge\\max_iq_i$ and let $K=I+\\frac1\\nu Q$, a stochastic matrix. Then $P(t)=\\sum_{n\\ge0}\\frac{(\\nu t)^ne^{-\\nu t}}{n!}K^n$: the chain is a discrete chain with transition matrix $K$ observed at the ticks of a rate-$\\nu$ Poisson clock (Ross 6.7; Grimmett 6.9).",
    "hint": "Can a continuous-time chain, like green flag and safety car, be run as a discrete one on the ticks of a clock?",
    "breakdown": [
      "<strong>$K=I+Q/\\nu$ = a one-tick transition matrix.</strong> With $\\nu\\ge\\max_iq_i$ all entries are in $[0,1]$ and rows add to 1; some ticks leave you in place.",
      "<strong>$\\frac{(\\nu t)^ne^{-\\nu t}}{n!}$ = the number of ticks.</strong> By time $t$ a rate-$\\nu$ Poisson clock has ticked $n$ times with this probability.",
      "<strong>$P(t)=\\sum_n\\ldots K^n$ = a mixture.</strong> Weight the $n$-step matrices by the Poisson tick probabilities: a stable way to compute $e^{Qt}$."
    ],
